<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the modern data ecosystem, information is increasingly aggregated from decentralized and heterogeneous sources <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>, <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>, <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>, <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite>. Because these data are generated across diverse institutions and devices (subject to shifting demographics, varying measurement procedures, and fluctuating contexts) the classical i.i.d. assumption is no longer a valid assumption <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>, <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>, <a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>. While pooling such information allows entities to solve problems that are <span id="S1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">statistically impossible</span> in isolation, it requires a principled framework that can distinguish between two distinct forms of data deviation: natural statistical heterogeneity among legitimate participants and strategic interference from adversarial ones.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We address these challenges through the lens of the <span id="S1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">untrusted batch model</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite>, providing a rigorous foundation for reliable inference by introducing a <span id="S1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">double corruption</span> landscape. This landscape captures the tiered complexity of real-world data: we consider a learner seeking to estimate the <span id="S1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">mean</span> <math id="S1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> of a target distribution <math id="S1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> using data from <math id="S1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> users, where each user contributes a <span id="S1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">batch</span> of <math id="S1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples. In this setting, an <math id="S1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of users are <span id="S1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">adversarially corrupted</span>, while the remaining “good” users provide data from distributions that are related to <math id="S1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> but exhibit diminishing quality, governed by a proximity parameter <math id="S1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. We consider two natural variants for this relationship: either the good users’ distributions have a mean shifted by <math id="S1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> from the truth, or an <math id="S1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of the samples <span id="S1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">within</span> each good batch are themselves adversarially corrupted.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This second variant marks a significant departure from existing results in the untrusted batch model. While prior research <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite> has primarily characterized the quality of good batches through total variation (TV) distance, such measures typically account for randomized replacement of <math id="S1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> fraction of the data. In the continuous high-dimensional regime, this distinction is critical: unlike TV-bounded shifts, an adversary can inspect the samples within a batch and strategically replace an <math id="S1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of them with new points. This allows the adversary to erase legitimate signals and induce shifts in the empirical mean and covariance by an arbitrary distance—an impact far more pronounced than the randomized replacements captured by distributional proximity.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">By providing algorithms that navigate this dual-layer of adversarial corruption and mean-shifts, we provide the minimax-optimal error rate <math id="S1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\sqrt{\varepsilon/n}+\sqrt{d/nN}+\sqrt{\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\sqrt{\varepsilon/n}+\sqrt{d/nN}+\sqrt{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math>. This rate reveals a fundamental insight: while the heterogeneity <math id="S1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> represents an inherent statistical difficulty, the adversary’s influence on fraction of “bad” users is suppressed by a factor of <math id="S1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\sqrt{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\sqrt{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. This occurs because the <math id="S1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples within a batch provide a more stable statistical signature than individual points, allowing the learner to partially “average away” the effect of user-level corruption as the batch size increases.</p>
</div>
<section id="S1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.1 </span>Problem Setup</h3>

<div id="S1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We study the <span id="S1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">untrusted batch model</span> introduced in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite>. We consider an unknown distribution <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> with mean <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and bounded covariance <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>⪯</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Both <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> are unknown to the algorithm. The goal is to estimate the mean by leveraging data contributed by <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> other users (or collaborators) in <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm. Each user <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math> possesses a local dataset consisting of <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> data points, referred to as a <span id="S1.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">batch</span>. The setting is particularly interesting in the case where <math id="S1.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\ll d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\ll d</annotation></semantics></math>, where the data of each user is not sufficient to perform mean estimation on their own, but can be jointly leveraged to recover the mean accurately.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The users in our model are not homogeneous: some may provide statistically relevant data, while others may be unreliable or even adversarial. Our framework explicitly models both cases as <span id="S1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">good</span> and <span id="S1.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">bad</span> users. We assume that at most an <math id="S1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of the users are <em id="S1.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">bad</em>. Formally, there exists a subset <math id="S1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}\subseteq[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}\subseteq[N]</annotation></semantics></math> of size at most <math id="S1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon N</annotation></semantics></math> such that for every <math id="S1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, the dataset of user <math id="S1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> may be chosen arbitrarily by an adversary, with no assumptions on its distribution or quality. The remaining users, <math id="S1.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}=[N]\setminus\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}=[N]\setminus\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, are <em id="S1.SS1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">good users</em>. The informativeness of their data is governed by a parameter <math id="S1.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, which measures how statistically related their data is to the target user’s distribution. We consider two natural variants that capture distinct notions of relevance.</p>
</div>
<section id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Mean Shift Model.</h5>

<figure id="S1.F1" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatright" style="width:55%;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.20698v1/model_1.svg" id="S1.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:262/129;" width="262" height="129"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S1.F1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 1</span>: </span><span id="S1.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Mean Shift Model. Illustration of Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Problem 1.1 (Mean shift). ‣ Mean Shift Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>: each good user provides samples drawn from a distribution whose mean lies within a <math id="S1.F1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>-neighborhood of the target mean <math id="S1.F1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, while an <math id="S1.F1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of users (yellow) are fully adversarial and may provide arbitrary samples.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the first variant, as a motivating example, we quantify heterogeneity as a mean-shift, where the distribution of each good user is centered within an <math id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>-neighborhood of the target mean <math id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>. Our problem setup is formally defined as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_problem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Problem 1.1</span></span><span id="S1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Mean shift)<span id="S1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider parameters <math id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\varepsilon\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\varepsilon\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, a target mean <math id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> users, each providing a batch of <math id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> data points in <math id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. We are guaranteed that at least a <math id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of these users are good; each good user <math id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> provides <math id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> i.i.d. samples drawn from an unknown distribution <math id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with mean <math id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and covariance <math id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{i}\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⪯</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{i}\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. The relevance of a good user’s data is quantified by its proximity to the target: <math id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mu_{i}-\mu\|_{2}\leq\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mu_{i}-\mu\|_{2}\leq\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. The remaining <math id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of users are adversarial and may contribute entirely arbitrary batches. Our goal is to robustly estimate the true mean <math id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> distance.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Adversarial Model.</h5>

<figure id="S1.F2" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatright" style="width:55%;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.20698v1/model_2.svg" id="S1.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:262/119;" width="262" height="119"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S1.F2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 2</span>: </span><span id="S1.F2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Adversarial Model. Illustration of Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Problem 1.2 (Adversarial). ‣ Adversarial Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>: beyond an <math id="S1.F2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of entirely adversarial users (yellow clusters), each good user’s batch contains an <math id="S1.F2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of adversarially corrupted samples (yellow points within blue clusters), resulting in a two-level corruption model.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the second variant, we consider a more malicious form of heterogeneity where even the good users’ datasets contain corrupted samples. This introduces a <span id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">double-layered contamination</span>: beyond the <math id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of entirely adversarial users, an <math id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of samples within each good batch is also replaced by corrupted points.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_problem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Problem 1.2</span></span><span id="S1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Adversarial)<span id="S1.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider parameters <math id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\varepsilon\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\varepsilon\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, a target distribution <math id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> with mean <math id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and covariance <math id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>⪯</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> users, each providing a batch of <math id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> data points in <math id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. We are guaranteed that at least a <math id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of these users are good; each good user <math id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> draws <math id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> i.i.d. samples from <math id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>. Then an <math id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of the <math id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples are replaced by arbitrary, adversarially chosen points. This is in addition to the
entirely adversarial datasets of the remaining <math id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of users. Our goal is to robustly estimate the true mean <math id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> distance.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This framework captures a broad range of realistic challenges: some users may be entirely unreliable, while even honest users may possess partially compromised datasets due to sensor errors, distribution shifts, or localized interference.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Corruption Model.</h5>

<div id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In both variants, we adopt the <em id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">strong contamination model</em> (see Definition <a href="#S1.SS1.SSS0.Px3" title="Corruption Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>). Conceptually, the data of all users are first generated according to their ideal distributions, after which a <span id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">globally coordinated adversary</span> is allowed to inspect the entire dataset of batches and modify the samples subject to its corruption budgets. This ensures that the corruption is not merely independent across users, but can be strategically orchestrated to maximize the bias of the global estimate based on the specific realization of all uncorrupted data.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1.3</span></span><span id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Strong contamination model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>)<span id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Given <math id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and a distribution <math id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-strong contamination model works as follows: <math id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples are drawn i.i.d. from <math id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>. An adversary receives all samples and can change up to <math id="S1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon n</annotation></semantics></math> of them arbitrarily. The algorithm takes the modified samples as input.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1.2 </span>Related Work</h3>

<section id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Robust statistics</h5>

<div id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Robustly learning an underlying parameter from an unknown distribution is a long-standing field in statistics, dating back to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>. The Tukey median <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite> achieves the optimal error for mean estimation but is inefficient in high-dimensions. The works <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, <a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite> resolved the computation inefficiency and inspired many subsequent works to design efficient and robust learning algorithms in various settings of practical interest. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>, <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite> further improve the computational efficiency to near-linear time. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> studied the heterogeneous corruption rates for each sample. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite> studied sparse mean estimation. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite> studied high-dimensional robust mean estimation using gradient descent.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The sum-of-squares method <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>, <a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite> has proven to be a powerful tool for robust statistics <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>, <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>. It provides a unified framework to design efficient algorithms as opposed to relying on problem-specific heuristics. For many robust estimation problems, optimal or best-known time and sample complexity can often be achieved using the sum-of-squares approach <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>, <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>, <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Robust estimation from corrupted batches</h5>

<div id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite> initiated the study of robust density estimation from corrupted batches for discrete distributions under the TV distance. Subsequent works <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite> further improved the computational and sample complexities. All of these prior works <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite> typically assume that the data from each good user follow a mildly perturbed distribution—for example, each user’s samples are drawn from some distribution <math id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TV}(P_{i},P)\leq\Theta(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TV}(P_{i},P)\leq\Theta(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In contrast, our work is the first to address high-dimensional mean estimation under a fully general, multi-level corruption model. We introduce and analyze a setting in which corruption can occur at both the user level and the sample level: beyond corrupting entire users, an adversary may arbitrarily corrupt up to an <math id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of samples within each good user. This strictly generalizes the settings considered in previous works.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This generalization is particularly challenging in the continuous, high-dimensional regime. In discrete distributions, corrupting an <math id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of samples in a good batch leads to at most an <math id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> increase in the <math id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> distance of the empirical histogram. In contrast, for high-dimensional distributions, even a small <math id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of corrupted samples can arbitrarily shift the empirical mean of a batch.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In addition to density estimation of discrete distributions, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>, <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite> studied robust density estimation of structured continuous distribution as well as <math id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> distance, which is always upper bounded by TV distance. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite> also designed algorithms for piecewise interval classification. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite> analyzed linear regression with the presence of heterogeneous data batches.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Other related robust learning models</h5>

<div id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite> studied robust personalized federated learning under Byzantine attack, where each user has clean local data from some distribution and a personalized optimization objective, but a fraction of users may be untruthful.
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite> studied robust distribution learning under Wasserstein distance where an adversary may arbitrarily corrupt a fraction of samples and locally perturb the remainder with bounded average magnitude. Our adversarial corruption model (Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Problem 1.2 (Adversarial). ‣ Adversarial Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>), the main focus of our work, is stronger than both works in that our good users may suffer from adversarial corruption that could shift the local mean arbitrarily.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Organization</h5>

<div id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The remaining parts of this paper are organized as follows. In <a href="#S2" title="2 Main Results ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we present the main results of our work. In <a href="#S3" title="3 Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we present the preliminaries and notation. In <a href="#S4" title="4 Technical Overview ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we provide a detailed overview of the techniques used to obtain our main results.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Main Results</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first review standard results in high-dimensional statistics. In the standard setting without any corruption, estimating the mean of a <math id="S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional distribution with bounded covariance from <math id="S2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples yields a minimax error bound of <math id="S2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(\sqrt{d/n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(\sqrt{d/n})</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm.
When an <math id="S2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of the samples may be adversarially corrupted, there exists a polynomial-time algorithm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, <a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite> that achieves an error of <math id="S2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="S2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=\widetilde{O}\left(d/\varepsilon\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=\widetilde{O}\left(d/\varepsilon\right)</annotation></semantics></math> samples.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We then discuss simple solutions to some special cases of our problem. When <math id="S2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0</annotation></semantics></math> (for both corruption models), we can simply run the standard robust mean estimation algorithm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite> on the empirical mean of each user with corruption parameter <math id="S2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the covariance shrinks by <math id="S2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/n</annotation></semantics></math>, we can achieve an error of <math id="S2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\sqrt{\varepsilon/n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\sqrt{\varepsilon/n})</annotation></semantics></math> as long as <math id="S2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=\Omega(d/\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=\Omega(d/\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>.
On the other hand, when <math id="S2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=0</annotation></semantics></math>, we can run robust mean estimation with corruption parameter <math id="S2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> over all <math id="S2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Nn" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Nn</annotation></semantics></math> samples and obtain an estimate with accuracy <math id="S2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> as long as <math id="S2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Nn=\Omega(d/\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Nn=\Omega(d/\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The main question is what happens when both <math id="S2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Ideally, we hope to achieve an error of <math id="S2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\varepsilon/n}+\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\varepsilon/n}+\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, but the presence of both batch and sample corruptions could amplify the error. Our contribution is to show that this ideal performance can be achieved in this challenging scenario.
First, we state the result for mean shift corruption:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2.1</span></span><span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Mean shift)<span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&lt;0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&lt;0.1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&lt;0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&lt;0.1</annotation></semantics></math>. Under the setup of Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Problem 1.1 (Mean shift). ‣ Mean Shift Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>, there exists a polynomial-time algorithm (Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Algorithm ideas. ‣ 4.2 Leveraging Per-User Structure (Problem ). ‣ 4 Technical Overview ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) that outputs <math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\mu-\widehat{\mu}\right\|_{2}=O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\mu-\widehat{\mu}\right\|_{2}=O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>
with probability at least <math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, as long as <math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Nn=\min\left\{\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon/n}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right),\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Nn=\min\left\{\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon/n}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right),\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The error rate is minimax optimal, and the sample complexity is nearly optimal.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To see the optimality of sample complexity, we note that <math id="S2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(\min\{dn/\varepsilon,d/\alpha\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(\min\{dn/\varepsilon,d/\alpha\})</annotation></semantics></math> is necessary to achieve an error of <math id="S2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\alpha}+\sqrt{\varepsilon/n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\alpha}+\sqrt{\varepsilon/n}</annotation></semantics></math>, even without corruption.
The error upper bound is proved in Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem C.1 (Upper bound result of Theorem ). ‣ C.1 Main Result ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a> and the lower bound part is proved in Theorem <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem F.1. ‣ F.1 Hardness of Problem ‣ Appendix F Hardness ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we discuss the adversarial corruption model (Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Problem 1.2 (Adversarial). ‣ Adversarial Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>). A simple solution is to treat all samples as <math id="S2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon+\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon+\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> corrupted version of the clean samples, and thus running robust mean estimation gives an error of <math id="S2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\sqrt{\varepsilon+\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\sqrt{\varepsilon+\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Nn=\Omega(d/(\varepsilon+\alpha))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Nn=\Omega(d/(\varepsilon+\alpha))</annotation></semantics></math>. This would not be ideal if the fraction of bad users is large. We prove that the effect of bad users can be essentially removed,</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2.2</span></span><span id="S2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Adversarial)<span id="S2.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon,\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon,\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon+5\alpha&lt;\frac{1}{18}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>18</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon+5\alpha&lt;\frac{1}{18}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under the setup of Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Problem 1.2 (Adversarial). ‣ Adversarial Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>, there exists a polynomial-time algorithm (Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Algorithm ideas. ‣ 4.3 Handling Small Corruption in Good Users (Problem ). ‣ 4 Technical Overview ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) that outputs <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\widehat{\mu}-\mu\right\|_{2}=O\left(\sqrt{\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\widehat{\mu}-\mu\right\|_{2}=O\left(\sqrt{\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> with probability at least <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, as long as <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="nN=\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">nN=\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The error rate is minimax optimal, and the sample complexity is nearly optimal.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The upper and lower bounds are proved in Theorem <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1 (Upper bound result of Theorem ). ‣ D.1 Main Result ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> and Theorem <a href="#A6.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem F.2. ‣ F.2 Hardness of Problem ‣ Appendix F Hardness ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.2</span></a> respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 2.3</span></span><span id="S2.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Problem 1.2 (Adversarial). ‣ Adversarial Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a> when <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, at least one sample from each user is corrupted, so we implicitly require <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\geq 1/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\geq 1/n</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\alpha}\geq\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mo>≥</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\alpha}\geq\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we do not have the extra <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> term in the error.</p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Unknown corruption</h5>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In practice, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon,\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon,\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> may not be known in advance. We can adapt to the unknown corruption level by performing binary search over the parameters, and stop when we reach beyond the “true” corruption level, leading to only an extra logarithmic factor in the sample complexity and running time. The stopping criteria could be determined using intersection of confidence balls <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite> or tolerant testing <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> (which requires <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\sqrt{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\sqrt{d})</annotation></semantics></math> clean samples). We will elaborate on this in <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Adaptive Collaborative Mean Estimation Under Unknown Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Preliminaries</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we first introduce all notation used throughout the paper. Then, in <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Sum-of-squares proof ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>, we give the formal definition of the sum-of-squares proof; in <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Pseudo-distributions ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, we define pseudo-distributions and show that, for constant-degree pseudo-distributions, we can find an approximate solution that satisfies a given set of constraints in polynomial time.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notation</h5>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[N]:=\{1,2,\dots,N\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[N]:=\{1,2,\dots,N\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> as the set of positive integers.
For a vector <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we write <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x\|_{2}:=\sqrt{\sum_{i\in[d]}x_{i}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x\|_{2}:=\sqrt{\sum_{i\in[d]}x_{i}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> for its <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm.
For all vectors <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we denote <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x,y\rangle:=\sum_{i\in[d]}x_{i}\cdot y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x,y\rangle:=\sum_{i\in[d]}x_{i}\cdot y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> as the inner product of <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>.
We let <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{tr}\left[A\right]:=\sum_{i\in[d]}A_{i,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{tr}\left[A\right]:=\sum_{i\in[d]}A_{i,i}</annotation></semantics></math> be the trace of <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For matrices <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we write <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\succeq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⪰</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\succeq B</annotation></semantics></math> to denote that <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A-B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A-B</annotation></semantics></math> is positive semidefinite, namely for all <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\top}\left(A-B\right)x\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\top}\left(A-B\right)x\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a random variable <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E[X]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E[X]</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the expectation and <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}[X]:=\E[(X-\E[X])(X-\E[X])^{\top}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}[X]:=\E[(X-\E[X])(X-\E[X])^{\top}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the covariance matrix.
The identity matrix in <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> is denoted by <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Sum-of-squares proof</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our algorithm relies on the sum-of-squares algorithm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>, <a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>. We describe the results needed for our algorithm and refer the readers to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>, <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> for more detailed exposition of the method. The formal definition of the sum-of-squares (SoS) proof is as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.SS1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.SS1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Sum-of-squares (SoS) proof)<span id="S3.SS1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For polynomials <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we say that <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq q</annotation></semantics></math> has a degree-<math id="S3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> sum-of-squares proof if there exists polynomials <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1},\ldots,s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1},\ldots,s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> with degree at most <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k/2</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p-q=\sum_{i=1}^{t}s_{i}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p-q=\sum_{i=1}^{t}s_{i}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">We denote this as <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.53467pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{-6.82222pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{k}$}}}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\{p\geq q\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:8.5pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:8.5pt;" voffset="-6.8pt" width="8.5pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></mpadded><mpadded style="width:8.5pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="8.5pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.53467pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{-6.82222pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{k}$}}}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\{p\geq q\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Given a set of polynomial constraints <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{A}=\{f_{i}=0\}_{i\in[m]}\cup\{g_{j}\geq 0\}_{j\in[n]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}=\{f_{i}=0\}_{i\in[m]}\cup\{g_{j}\geq 0\}_{j\in[n]}</annotation></semantics></math>, we say that there exists a degree-<math id="S3.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> proof of <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq q</annotation></semantics></math> modulo <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> if there exists polynomials <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i},b_{j},s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i},b_{j},s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(a_{i}f_{i})\leq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(a_{i}f_{i})\leq k</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(b_{j}^{2}g_{j})\leq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(b_{j}^{2}g_{j})\leq k</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(s_{t}^{2})\leq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(s_{t}^{2})\leq k</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j,t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j,t</annotation></semantics></math>, and</p>
<table id="S3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p-q=\sum_{t}s_{t}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}a_{i}f_{i}+\sum_{j=1}^{n}b_{j}^{2}g_{j}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></munder><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p-q=\sum_{t}s_{t}^{2}+\sum_{i=1}^{m}a_{i}f_{i}+\sum_{j=1}^{n}b_{j}^{2}g_{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">This can be denoted as <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{A}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.53467pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{-6.82222pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{k}$}}}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\{p\geq q\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:8.5pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:8.5pt;" voffset="-6.8pt" width="8.5pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></mpadded><mpadded style="width:8.5pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="8.5pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.53467pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{-6.82222pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{k}$}}}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\{p\geq q\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Pseudo-distributions</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Pseudo-distribution is a generalization of probability distributions in that their “probability” weight can be negative and “expectations” are only guaranteed to be non-negative for square polynomials of finite degree.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.SS2.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.2</span></span><span id="S3.SS2.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be a finite set of vectors. A level-<math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> (or degree-<math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>) pseudo-distribution over <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> has a “mass function” <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(x)</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all polynomial <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(f)\leq\ell/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(f)\leq\ell/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="S3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}D(x)=1,\quad\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}D(x)f(x)^{2}\geq 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.000em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}D(x)=1,\quad\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}D(x)f(x)^{2}\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and we define the pseudo-expectation for <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="S3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\E}_{D}\left[f(x)\right]:=\sum_{x}D(x)f(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>x</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\E}_{D}\left[f(x)\right]:=\sum_{x}D(x)f(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This relaxation is crucial for the Sum-of-Squares framework: rather than searching over discrete or combinatorial objects directly, we optimize over pseudo-expectations that behave like expectations on all low-degree polynomials. In particular, any feasible SoS solution corresponds to a pseudo-distribution whose pseudo-expectation operator satisfies basic probabilistic inequalities (such as Cauchy–Schwarz) up to the prescribed degree.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.SS2.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3.3</span></span><span id="S3.SS2.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Polynomial constraints and satisfiability)<span id="S3.SS2.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Given a set of polynomial constraints <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}=\{f_{1}\geq 0,\ldots f_{m}\geq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}=\{f_{1}\geq 0,\ldots f_{m}\geq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we say that <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> at degree <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> if for every <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subseteq[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subseteq[m]</annotation></semantics></math> and every sum-of-squares polynomial <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\deg(h)=\sum_{i\in S}\max\{\deg(f_{i}),r\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\deg(h)=\sum_{i\in S}\max\{\deg(f_{i}),r\}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\E}_{D}\left[h(x)\prod_{i\in S}f_{i}(x)\right]\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\E}_{D}\left[h(x)\prod_{i\in S}f_{i}(x)\right]\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">We say that <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> approximately at degree <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> if the above inequalities are satisfied up to an error of <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{-d\ell}\left\|h\right\|_{2}\prod_{i\in S}\left\|f_{i}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{-d\ell}\left\|h\right\|_{2}\prod_{i\in S}\left\|f_{i}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\cdot\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\cdot\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is the 2-norm of the coefficients of each monomial.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Due to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>, <a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>, we can efficiently find a level-<math id="S3.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> pseudo-distribution that approximately satisfies a given set of constraints <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> in time <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d+m)^{O(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d+m)^{O(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math>. See also <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, Fact 3.9]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Technical Overview</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Brief Review of SoS for Robust Mean Estimation ‣ 4 Technical Overview ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, we present a brief overview of SoS for robust mean estimation. In <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Leveraging Per-User Structure (Problem ). ‣ 4 Technical Overview ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>, we introduce how to adapt traditional SoS to mean shift corruption (Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Problem 1.1 (Mean shift). ‣ Mean Shift Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>). In <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 Handling Small Corruption in Good Users (Problem ). ‣ 4 Technical Overview ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>, we address the more challenging Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Problem 1.2 (Adversarial). ‣ Adversarial Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a> by designing a novel two-level refinement polynomial system and provide the proof overview.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Brief Review of SoS for Robust Mean Estimation</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The key structural insight for robust mean estimation is the following: if one can identify a subset of samples <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> that contains at least a <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> fraction of the data and whose empirical covariance is small, then the empirical mean of <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> must be close to the true mean. Intuitively, low empirical covariance ensures that no small group of samples can “pull” the mean in any particular direction. Thus, even if <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> includes a small number of corrupted points, their collective influence on the mean is limited.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The main algorithmic challenge is to efficiently find such a subset <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. A powerful framework for this task is provided by the <em id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">sum-of-squares (SoS)</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>, <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite> relaxation. In this approach, the search for a large, low-covariance subset is formulated as a system of polynomial constraints over indicator variables representing sample membership to <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. Formally, the polynomial constraints should at least include:</p>
<ol id="S4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> is sufficiently large:</span> with <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}\in\left\{0,1\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}\in\left\{0,1\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes whether or not the <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th sample is selected in our subset <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, we need the total number of selected sample <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n}W_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n}W_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> should be equal to the number of good samples <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\varepsilon)n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\varepsilon)n</annotation></semantics></math>, and</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bounded covariance:</span> We use <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the selected data point, which should satisfy <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(Z_{i}-\overline{Z})(Z_{i}-\overline{Z})^{\top}\preceq 2\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(Z_{i}-\overline{Z})(Z_{i}-\overline{Z})^{\top}\preceq 2\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> is the average of <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The SoS hierarchy then yields a tractable convex relaxation of this polynomial system, from which one can extract an accurate mean estimate. The standard SoS analysis involves two main parts:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Satisfiability:</span> With high probability, a feasible solution to the SoS relaxation exists when the data satisfy the assumed corruption model.
A natural idea is to prove that the set of clean samples satisfies the constraints with high probability. However, for bounded covariance random variables, we cannot directly obtain a high-probability bound on <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(Z_{i}-\overline{Z})(Z_{i}-\overline{Z})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(Z_{i}-\overline{Z})(Z_{i}-\overline{Z})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we must introduce a truncation step that modifies <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> of samples whose deviations from the mean are excessively large (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>, Section 3.2.2]</cite>). Samples from this truncated distribution satisfies bounded empirical covariance with high probability when <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=\operatorname{\tilde{\Omega}}\left(d/\varepsilon\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=\operatorname{\tilde{\Omega}}\left(d/\varepsilon\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, so we treat our samples as <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> corrupted versions of the this new distribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Identifiability:</span> Any feasible (or approximately feasible) SoS solution corresponds to a mean estimate that is provably close to the true mean of the uncorrupted distribution.
For a review of the SoS preliminaries, see <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Sum-of-squares proof ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Leveraging Per-User Structure (Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Problem 1.1 (Mean shift). ‣ Mean Shift Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>).</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this part, we present our techniques for analyzing Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Problem 1.1 (Mean shift). ‣ Mean Shift Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a> and for deriving Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1 (Mean shift). ‣ 2 Main Results ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>.
Our approach goes beyond this naive aggregation by explicitly leveraging the <em id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">per-user structure</em> of the data in order to obtain a sharper error bound than <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon+\alpha}+\sqrt{\frac{d}{Nn}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon+\alpha}+\sqrt{\frac{d}{Nn}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. A crucial observation is that, for each uncorrupted user, the empirical mean of their local dataset has variance smaller than that of a single sample by a factor of <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/n</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the central question we study is how to exploit this variance reduction to improve the overall error bound.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Algorithm ideas.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this model, each good user’s data come from a neighboring distribution and contain no additional corruption, so we can view each user’s empirical mean as a <em id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">low-variance point</em> whose expectation is slightly shifted from the target mean. Bad users, on the other hand, may contribute arbitrary empirical means. Therefore, we denote all the <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s, which were used to represent the uncorrupted sample (<a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Brief Review of SoS for Robust Mean Estimation ‣ 4 Technical Overview ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>), as the empirical mean of <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples from uncorrupted users. As each sample is from a distribution with covariance bounded by <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, the empirical mean over <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples can be further bounded by <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, giving us a much better approximation on the average of all empirical means across all good users. In addition, after taking the mean shift <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> into consideration, we can express the bound as <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\frac{1}{n}+\alpha\right)\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\frac{1}{n}+\alpha\right)\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote this set of constraints as a polynomial system <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖠</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Definition <a href="#A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="Algorithmic design. ‣ C.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> for a more formal and complete definition). Therefore, our SoS algorithm can return <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\overline{z}-\widehat{\mu}\right\|_{2}&lt;O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon\left(\frac{1}{n}+\alpha\right)}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\overline{z}-\widehat{\mu}\right\|_{2}&lt;O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon\left(\frac{1}{n}+\alpha\right)}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> SoS for solving mean shift (Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Problem 1.1 (Mean shift). ‣ Mean Shift Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>).</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input</span>: <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples from each user, <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,0.1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,0.1)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in(0,0.1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in(0,0.1)</annotation></semantics></math>, polynomial system <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖠</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> (Definition <a href="#A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="Algorithmic design. ‣ C.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>).

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
                
                
              Compute a pseudoexpectation <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the constraints of the polynomial system <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖠</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}=\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}\left[\overline{Z}\right]\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}=\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}\left[\overline{Z}\right]\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Upper bound error analysis.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We further bound the deviation between each user’s mean and the population mean <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>. As explained in <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Brief Review of SoS for Robust Mean Estimation ‣ 4 Technical Overview ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, we use truncation to ensure the satisfiabilty, but it also causes new challenges. The corrupted samples can be viewed as <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> corrupted from the pure samples. We truncate the pure samples<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
                
                
                
                
                
                
                
              Although the pure samples are unknown to us, the goal of the satisfiability argument is to show that such a solution exists. Since the pure samples must exist under our model assumptions, we can apply truncation to them in the analysis to establish existence.</span></span></span> by an additional <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction so that we can treat the corrupted samples we receive as a <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> corrupted version. In addition, since truncation inevitably shifts the mean, we must show that this change is small, namely, <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}\leq O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}\leq O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Combining this with the assumption that uncorrupted users satisfy
<math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mu_{i}-\mu\|_{2}\leq\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mu_{i}-\mu\|_{2}\leq\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can eventually bound the distance between the truncated mean and the true mean <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To get the error of the true mean <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and our SoS output approximation <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>, we still need to bound each user’s true mean and their empirical mean <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples. By Markov’s inequality, we get</p>
<table id="S4.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\overline{z}-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}&lt;O\left(\sqrt{\frac{d}{nN}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\overline{z}-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}&lt;O\left(\sqrt{\frac{d}{nN}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">so that <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\mu-\widehat{\mu}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\mu-\widehat{\mu}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> can be eventually bounded by <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\frac{d}{nN}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\frac{d}{nN}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Now we sketch the proof idea for satisfiability. The main challenge is that naively applying the standard truncation described in <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Brief Review of SoS for Robust Mean Estimation ‣ 4 Technical Overview ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> requires at least <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="nN\geq\Omega\left(\frac{dn}{\varepsilon}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">nN\geq\Omega\left(\frac{dn}{\varepsilon}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> total samples. To improve this sample complexity bound to the optimal rate, we set the cardinality of <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\varepsilon^{\prime})N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\varepsilon^{\prime})N</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{\prime}=\min\left\{\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\},\frac{1}{10}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{\prime}=\min\left\{\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\},\frac{1}{10}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, thereby allowing for a more careful selection of samples. With a careful choice of this relationship, the relaxed selection does not negatively affect the error guarantee; instead, it enables a tighter bound on the failure probability in the satisfiability argument, leading to an improved sample-complexity bound:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle nN\geq\min\left\{\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon/n}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right),\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle nN\geq\min\left\{\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon/n}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right),\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">For more details, we kindly refer the readers to <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Techniques for lower bound.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(\sqrt{\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(\sqrt{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math> lower bound is straightforward: suppose the true mean is <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, for all users, the adversary could simply change the mean to some <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> that is <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> apart, and no algorithms could tell whether the true mean is <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F3" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatright" style="width:50%;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.20698v1/hardness_1.svg" id="S4.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:238/139;" width="238" height="139"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 3</span>: </span><span id="S4.F3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Lower Bound Construction for <math id="S4.F3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(\sqrt{\varepsilon/n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(\sqrt{\varepsilon/n})</annotation></semantics></math>. Distributions <math id="S4.F3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.F3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> differ in their means by <math id="S4.F3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\varepsilon/n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\varepsilon/n}</annotation></semantics></math> while maintaining bounded variance.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To prove the <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(\sqrt{\varepsilon/n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(\sqrt{\varepsilon/n})</annotation></semantics></math> lower bound, we construct two hypotheses
<math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> with global means <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
Let <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}:=\varepsilon/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}:=\varepsilon/n</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, each sample is drawn independently as</p>
<table id="S4.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[X=0]=1-\varepsilon_{0},\qquad\Pr\left[X=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\varepsilon_{0}}}\right]=\varepsilon_{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[X=0]=1-\varepsilon_{0},\qquad\Pr\left[X=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\varepsilon_{0}}}\right]=\varepsilon_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Under <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, all samples satisfy <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math> deterministically.
Both distributions have variance bounded by a constant, while their means differ by</p>
<table id="S4.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{0}=\mathbb{E}[X]=\sqrt{\varepsilon_{0}}=\sqrt{\varepsilon/n},\qquad\mu_{1}=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{0}=\mathbb{E}[X]=\sqrt{\varepsilon_{0}}=\sqrt{\varepsilon/n},\qquad\mu_{1}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Under <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, each user draws <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> i.i.d. samples from <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>.
With constant probability, each user contains <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> nonzero samples, which are precisely the samples distinguishing <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
An adversary may modify these <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> samples per user—replacing them by zero—without exceeding its corruption budget.
After this modification, the observed data under <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> are identical to those under <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, no algorithm can distinguish <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> with probability better than <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2/3</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since the mean separation between the two hypotheses is <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon/n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon/n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, this establishes a minimax lower bound of <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon/n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon/n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> on the estimation error.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, combining with the lower bound in the classical high-dimensional mean estimation <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta\left(\sqrt{\frac{d}{Nn}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta\left(\sqrt{\frac{d}{Nn}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have shown that our result is <em id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">minimax-optimal</em>.
For more information, we kindly refer the readers to <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Hardness ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Handling Small Corruption in Good Users (Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Problem 1.2 (Adversarial). ‣ Adversarial Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>).</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this setting, the bad samples of good users can shift the local mean arbitrarily. Thus, the per-user empirical mean is no longer a low-variance quantity, which means the solution in <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Leveraging Per-User Structure (Problem ). ‣ 4 Technical Overview ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> cannot be applied, calling for a new colution</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Simple solutions</h5>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As discussed in <a href="#S2" title="2 Main Results ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, a naive solution is to leverage the observation that the total fraction of corrupted samples is <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon+\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon+\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, so running the standard robust mean estimation gives an error of <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon+\alpha}+\sqrt{\frac{d}{Nn}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon+\alpha}+\sqrt{\frac{d}{Nn}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Another naive solution is to apply robust mean estimation for each user individually. However, achieving an accuracy of <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> requires each user to have at least <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=\Omega(d/\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=\Omega(d/\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> samples. It leaves the question whether <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> error can be achieved even when <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=o(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=o(d)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Algorithm ideas.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We design a novel SoS formulation <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖡</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{B}</annotation></semantics></math> formally defined in Definition <a href="#A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>, which synergizes the sample constraint <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Brief Review of SoS for Robust Mean Estimation ‣ 4 Technical Overview ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> and the user-level constraint in <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Leveraging Per-User Structure (Problem ). ‣ 4 Technical Overview ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>,</p>
<ol id="S4.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Crude refinement:</span> The purpose is to filter out gross outliers among bad users and corrupted samples from good users. These constraints are similar to the standard SoS constraints over all samples, with the key distinction that we additionally add an indicator <math id="S4.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}\in\left\{0,1\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}\in\left\{0,1\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> to select good users, and require that at least <math id="S4.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\alpha)n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\alpha)n</annotation></semantics></math> number of samples are kept if <math id="S4.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. All the selected samples <math id="S4.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{Z_{i,j}\}_{i\in[N],j\in[n]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{Z_{i,j}\}_{i\in[N],j\in[n]}</annotation></semantics></math> should have bounded empirical covariance <math id="S4.I2.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\preceq 2\mathbb{I}_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\preceq 2\mathbb{I}_{d})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">User-level refinement:</span> The second set of constraints performs an additional selection step for good users, which leverages the concentration of good users and enforces that the empirical covariance of their (cleaned) empirical means remains small, similar to <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Leveraging Per-User Structure (Problem ). ‣ 4 Technical Overview ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>. More concretely, this user-level filtering requires the number of users <math id="S4.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> selected is at least <math id="S4.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\varepsilon)N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\varepsilon)N</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, let <math id="S4.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> be the empirical mean of samples of user <math id="S4.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, the set <math id="S4.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{Y_{i}:U_{i}=1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{Y_{i}:U_{i}=1\}</annotation></semantics></math> should have covariance with spectral norm at most <math id="S4.I2.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{n}+\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n}+\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.I2.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\frac{\alpha}{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\frac{\alpha}{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> is used to reduce the failure probability of this largest singular value bound, without sacrificing the accuracy.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By coupling these two levels of constraints, our SoS algorithm enjoys the benefits of both the large sample size of all users as well as concentration within each user, thereby achieving optimal error while remaining computationally and sample efficient.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> SoS for solving adversarial (Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Problem 1.2 (Adversarial). ‣ Adversarial Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>).</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input</span>: <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples from each user, <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in\left(0,\frac{1}{18}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>18</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in\left(0,\frac{1}{18}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\left(0,\frac{1}{90}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>90</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\left(0,\frac{1}{90}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon+5\alpha&lt;\frac{1}{18}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>18</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon+5\alpha&lt;\frac{1}{18}</annotation></semantics></math>, and polynomial system <math id="alg2.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖡</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{B}</annotation></semantics></math> (crude and user-level refinement, see the full definition in Definition <a href="#A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>).

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
                
                
              Compute a pseudoexpectation <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the constraints of the polynomial system <math id="alg2.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖡</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{B}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}:=\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}\left[\overline{Y}\right]\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}:=\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}\left[\overline{Y}\right]\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Upper bound error analysis.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This change in polynomial constraint structure makes our proof of correctness significantly different from that of prior works. Our error bound can be expressed as two major components:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\leq 2\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(1-U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i})\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\rangle\right)^{2}+2\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i}\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\rangle\right)^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\leq 2\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(1-U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i})\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\rangle\right)^{2}+2\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i}\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\rangle\right)^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{i}\in\left\{0,1\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{i}\in\left\{0,1\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates whether user <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is an actual good user with at most <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha n</annotation></semantics></math> corrupted samples,
<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is the SoS variable representing the cleaned user-level mean, <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{Y}:=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}Y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{Y}:=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}Y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mu}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mu}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is the empirical mean of clean samples of user <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mu}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mu}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is the empirical mean of all clean samples.
The first term captures the total adversarial pull contributed by users that the SoS solution does not certify as good,
while the second term represents the systematic bias introduced by users that the SoS solution believes to be good.
In traditional SoS algorithms, since there is only a single layer of refinement, the second term is zero: one layer of “good” users is sufficient to ensure that this bias vanishes.
Therefore, the first term can be bounded by <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon/n</annotation></semantics></math>-scaled term using similar techniques used in traditional SoS.
We mainly focus on presenting the bound on the second term.
Using the SoS Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we can further express it as</p>
<table id="S4.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle 2\cdot\left(\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i}\left(1-W_{i,j}\mathds{1}_{\left\{v_{i,j}=x_{i,j}\right\}}\right)\right)\cdot\left(\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\rangle^{2}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\cdot\left(\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i}\left(1-W_{i,j}\mathds{1}_{\left\{v_{i,j}=x_{i,j}\right\}}\right)\right)\cdot\left(\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\rangle^{2}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the (unknown) clean sample and <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is the SoS variable
representing the sample retained by the crude refinement.
The second factor measures the total “surviving bad mass” among users that are both selected and certified
(via <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>): by the crude-refinement constraints and the fact that each uncorrupted user contains
at most an <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction corrupted samples, we can show this factor is <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 2\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 2\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the third factor, letting <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c:=\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c:=\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>, we expand</p>
<table id="S4.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z_{i,j}-\overline{Y}=(Z_{i,j}-\overline{Z})+(\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu})+(\widetilde{\mu}-\overline{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z_{i,j}-\overline{Y}=(Z_{i,j}-\overline{Z})+(\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu})+(\widetilde{\mu}-\overline{Y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">so that <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j}=\left(Z_{i,j}-\overline{Y}\right)+c+\left(\widetilde{\mu}-v_{i,j}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j}=\left(Z_{i,j}-\overline{Y}\right)+c+\left(\widetilde{\mu}-v_{i,j}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. We can bound the inner product between each of them with <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>.
The term involving <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mu}-v_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mu}-v_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> is controlled by the empirical covariance of the clean samples
(since <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> is their empirical mean), while <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu},c\rangle^{2}=\|c\|_{2}^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu},c\rangle^{2}=\|c\|_{2}^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> is immediate.
The remaining fluctuation term <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i,j}-\overline{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i,j}-\overline{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded using the bounded-covariance constraints from the crude refinement,
and the bridging terms <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\widetilde{\mu}-\overline{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widetilde{\mu}-\overline{Y})</annotation></semantics></math> are the final terms we want to bound under <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> distance in SoS indentifiability, where <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}&lt;O\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}&lt;O\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)</annotation></semantics></math> can be obtained via the standard SoS in <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Brief Review of SoS for Robust Mean Estimation ‣ 4 Technical Overview ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.
Combining these bounds yields an <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-scaled upper bound on the trusted contribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The above steps yield a constant-degree SoS proof,
which means that provided the constraints can be satisfied, the SoS algorithm can find a pseudoexpectation <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}=\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}\left[\overline{Y}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}=\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}\left[\overline{Y}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> gives the desired error of <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math> .
We further combine it with the classical high-dimensional mean estimation bound <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta\left(\sqrt{\frac{d}{Nn}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta\left(\sqrt{\frac{d}{Nn}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, which finishes the proof of identifiability.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof of satisfiability</h5>

<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">It remains to show satisfiability, namely, that these constraints can be satisfied with high probability over the samples. This task is more challenging than in Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Problem 1.1 (Mean shift). ‣ Mean Shift Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>, since we require both refinements to hold simultaneously.
Recall that in SoS algorithm for standard robust mean estimation, the technique is to apply truncation.
In our setting, because we employ two refinements, we need to design a two-layer truncation procedure.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">First, we construct a new random variable <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> via truncation by modifying a small fraction of the clean samples <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> whose deviations from the mean are excessively large. Since <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> differs from the corrupted samples we observe, <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, on at most an <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon+\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon+\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of indices (due to the two levels of strong contamination in Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Problem 1.2 (Adversarial). ‣ Adversarial Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>), and since <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> differs from <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> on at most an <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of indices, the truncated random variable <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> can be viewed as an <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varepsilon+2\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varepsilon+2\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>-strong contamination of the observed samples <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. The sample complexity required to ensure that this step holds with probability at least <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,0.1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,0.1)</annotation></semantics></math>, is
<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="nN\geq\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">nN\geq\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">However, the problematic part is the second truncation step, where we define
<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{i}^{\prime}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}Y^{\prime}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{i}^{\prime}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}Y^{\prime}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>
by truncating <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We note that <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{\prime}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{\prime}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> can be viewed as an <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-strong contamination of <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{\prime}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{\prime}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> can be regarded as a <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2\varepsilon+2\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2\varepsilon+2\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>-strong contamination of the corrupted samples <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> that we receive. We highlight that the second truncation operates by keeping or collapsing whole users, not by truncating individual samples independently.
Therefore, the expected largest singular value of the empirical covariance of <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is more tightly bounded.
As a consequence, putting this inside of the matrix Chernoff bound yields a worse failure probability. Therefore, to achieve a success probability of <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, the required number of samples satisfies
<math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="nN\geq\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon/n}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">nN\geq\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon/n}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Combining this with the first truncation step, we need at least</p>
<table id="S4.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle nN\geq\max\left\{\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\left(\varepsilon/n\right)}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right),\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle nN\geq\max\left\{\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\left(\varepsilon/n\right)}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right),\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">samples. This is worse than our desired sample complexity (Eq. (<a href="#S4.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ Upper bound error analysis. ‣ 4.2 Leveraging Per-User Structure (Problem ). ‣ 4 Technical Overview ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)), even when using the tighter choice <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{\prime}=\min\left\{\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\},\frac{1}{18}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>18</mn></mfrac><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{\prime}=\min\left\{\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\},\frac{1}{18}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> as in our first problem setting: since <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the fraction of corrupted samples, we have <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To address this issue, we instead relax the bound on the largest singular value in the user-level refinement from <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{n}+\frac{\alpha}{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n}+\frac{\alpha}{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>. This relaxation allows for a broader choice of parameters in the matrix Chernoff bound, thereby further reducing the failure probability. Since the tail probability decays exponentially, we are able to tighten the sample complexity bound to Eq. (<a href="#S4.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ Upper bound error analysis. ‣ 4.2 Leveraging Per-User Structure (Problem ). ‣ 4 Technical Overview ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Additional details are provided in <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Techniques for lower bound.</h5>

<figure id="S4.F4" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatright" style="width:50%;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.20698v1/hardness_2.svg" id="S4.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:238/142;" width="238" height="142"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="S4.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Lower Bound Construction for <math id="S4.F4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(\sqrt{\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(\sqrt{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math>. Distributions <math id="S4.F4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.F4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> differ in their means by <math id="S4.F4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> while maintaining bounded variance.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The lower bound <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\left(\sqrt{\frac{d}{nN}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\left(\sqrt{\frac{d}{nN}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> follows with exactly the same technique from <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Leveraging Per-User Structure (Problem ). ‣ 4 Technical Overview ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>. To show the <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(\sqrt{\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(\sqrt{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math> lower bound, we construct two hypotheses <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> is the degenerate distribution at 0, and <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as</p>
<table id="S4.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[X=0]=1-\alpha\qquad\text{and}\qquad\Pr\!\left[X=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha}}\right]=\alpha." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mtext>and</mtext><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[X=0]=1-\alpha\qquad\text{and}\qquad\Pr\!\left[X=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha}}\right]=\alpha.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Both distributions have variance at most 1, and their means differ by <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Given samples from <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the adversary replaces each nonzero sample by <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, making the samples exactly the same as <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. The fraction of samples changed for each user is roughly <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, no algorithm can distinguish <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> with probability better than <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2/3</annotation></semantics></math>,
implying a minimax lower bound of <math id="S4.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(\sqrt{\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(\sqrt{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math> on the estimation error. We refer to <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Hardness ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a> for more details.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Sx1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Acknowledgment</h2>

<div id="Sx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Maryam Aliakbarpour is affiliated with the Ken Kennedy Institute at Rice University.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div id="Sx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="Sx1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:173%;">Appendix</span></p>
</div>
<section id="A0.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Roadmap</h5>

<div id="A0.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>, we present the mathematical background of SoS and basic probabilistic tools.
In <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>, we introduce the SoS algorithm for the traditional robust mean estimation problem, where the corruption level <math id="A0.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> is given and <math id="A0.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
In <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>, we analyze our first problem (<a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Problem 1.1 (Mean shift). ‣ Mean Shift Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Problem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>), present our main upper bound result (<a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem C.1 (Upper bound result of Theorem ). ‣ C.1 Main Result ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>), and provide its complete proof. In <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>, we analyze our second problem (<a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Problem 1.2 (Adversarial). ‣ Adversarial Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Problem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>), present our main upper bound result (<a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1 (Upper bound result of Theorem ). ‣ D.1 Main Result ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>), and provide its complete proof.
In <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Adaptive Collaborative Mean Estimation Under Unknown Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>, we further apply this technique to the settings of <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Problem 1.1 (Mean shift). ‣ Mean Shift Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Problem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a> and <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Problem 1.2 (Adversarial). ‣ Adversarial Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Problem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>, thereby enabling our algorithms for these more complex problems to handle unknown corruption levels <math id="A0.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A0.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.
Finally, in <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Hardness ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>, we present our lower bound results for <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Problem 1.1 (Mean shift). ‣ Mean Shift Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Problem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a> and <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Problem 1.2 (Adversarial). ‣ Adversarial Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Problem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>, showing that our upper bounds are minimax optimal.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Additional Preliminaries</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we first present the notation that we use throughout the paper.
Then, in <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1 Sum-of-squares ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, we present sum-of-squares properties. In <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2 Pseudo-expectation properties ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, we introduce the mathematical properties of pseudo-expectation. In <a href="#A1.SS3" title="A.3 Probabilistic and Algebraic Tools ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>, we present the probabilistic and algebraic tools used in this paper.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notation.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[N]:=\{1,2,\dots,N\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[N]:=\{1,2,\dots,N\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> as the set of positive integers. For all set <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, we denote <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{A}</annotation></semantics></math> as its complement.
For a vector <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we write <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x\|_{2}:=\sqrt{\sum_{i\in[d]}x_{i}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x\|_{2}:=\sqrt{\sum_{i\in[d]}x_{i}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> for its <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm. For all vectors <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we denote <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle x,y\rangle:=\sum_{i\in[d]}x_{i}\cdot y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x,y\rangle:=\sum_{i\in[d]}x_{i}\cdot y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> as the inner product of <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a matrix <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|A\|_{2}:=\sup_{\|x\|_{2}=1}\|Ax\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|A\|_{2}:=\sup_{\|x\|_{2}=1}\|Ax\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes its spectral norm, and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|A\|_{F}:=\sqrt{\sum_{i,j}A_{i,j}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|A\|_{F}:=\sqrt{\sum_{i,j}A_{i,j}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes its Frobenius norm.
For a symmetric matrix <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, we let <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\max}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\max}(A)</annotation></semantics></math> denote its largest eigenvalue.
We use <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{0}_{d\times d}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{0}_{d\times d}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> as a matrix with all 0 entries.
We let <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{tr}\left[A\right]:=\sum_{i\in[d]}A_{i,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{tr}\left[A\right]:=\sum_{i\in[d]}A_{i,i}</annotation></semantics></math> be the trace of <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>.
For matrices <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we write <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\succeq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⪰</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\succeq B</annotation></semantics></math> to denote that <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A-B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A-B</annotation></semantics></math> is positive semidefinite, namely for all <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\top}\left(A-B\right)x\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\top}\left(A-B\right)x\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. For an arbitrary matrix <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we let <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> be its transpose.
For a probability space <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Omega,\mathcal{F},\Pr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Omega,\mathcal{F},\Pr)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> is the sample space, <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-algebra of events, and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr:\mathcal{F}\to[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr:\mathcal{F}\to[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> is the probability measure.
For a random variable <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X:\Omega\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X:\Omega\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E[X]\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E[X]\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the expectation and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}[X]:=\E[(X-\E[X])(X-\E[X])^{\top}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}[X]:=\E[(X-\E[X])(X-\E[X])^{\top}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the covariance matrix.
For a random variable <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y:\Omega\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y:\Omega\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, we let <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}[Y]:=\E[(Y-\E[Y])^{2}]\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}[Y]:=\E[(Y-\E[Y])^{2}]\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote its variance.
For all <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the indicator function <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathds{1}_{\left\{A\right\}}:\Omega\to\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathds{1}_{\left\{A\right\}}:\Omega\to\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathds{1}_{\left\{A\right\}}(\omega):=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathds{1}_{\left\{A\right\}}(\omega):=1</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\in A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathds{1}_{\left\{A\right\}}(\omega):=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathds{1}_{\left\{A\right\}}(\omega):=0</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\notin A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\notin A</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\in\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\in\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>.
The identity matrix in <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> is denoted by <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We use <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m46" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.53467pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{-6.82222pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{k}$}}}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\{p(x)\geq q(x)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:8.5pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:8.5pt;" voffset="-6.8pt" width="8.5pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></mpadded><mpadded style="width:8.5pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="8.5pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.53467pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{-6.82222pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{k}$}}}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\{p(x)\geq q(x)\}</annotation></semantics></math> to represent that there exists a degree-<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m47" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> sum-of-squares proof that the polynomial inequality <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m48" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(x)\geq q(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(x)\geq q(x)</annotation></semantics></math> holds, with variable <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m49" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, by assuming the polynomial constraints in the set <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m50" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖡</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{B}</annotation></semantics></math>. We define <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m51" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}[x_{1},\dots,x_{d}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}[x_{1},\dots,x_{d}]</annotation></semantics></math> as the polynomial ring over the real variables <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m52" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},\dots,x_{d}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},\dots,x_{d}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Sum-of-squares</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We introduce the sum-of-squares proof system in this section.
The following inference rules are helpful to establish new sum-of-square proofs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(SoS Cauchy-Schwarz, Claim 2.6 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>]</cite>)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b</annotation></semantics></math> be vector-valued polynomials of degree at most <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for any <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\vdash_{2k}\left\{\langle a,b\rangle\leq\frac{\varepsilon}{2}\left\|a\right\|_{2}^{2}+\frac{1}{2\varepsilon}\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}\right\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>⊢</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vdash_{2k}\left\{\langle a,b\rangle\leq\frac{\varepsilon}{2}\left\|a\right\|_{2}^{2}+\frac{1}{2\varepsilon}\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\vdash_{4k}\left\{\langle a,b\rangle^{2}\leq\left\|a\right\|_{2}^{2}\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>⊢</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vdash_{4k}\left\{\langle a,b\rangle^{2}\leq\left\|a\right\|_{2}^{2}\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(SoS operator norm, Claim 2.7 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>]</cite>)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{M=\lambda I-BB^{\top}\}\vdash_{k}\{y^{\top}My\leq\lambda\|y\|_{2}^{2}\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><msub><mo>⊢</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>M</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{M=\lambda I-BB^{\top}\}\vdash_{k}\{y^{\top}My\leq\lambda\|y\|_{2}^{2}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq\deg\bigl(y^{\top}My+y^{\top}BB^{\top}y\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq\deg\bigl(y^{\top}My+y^{\top}BB^{\top}y\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Basic rules)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Sum-of-squares operations satisfy the following rules:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<dl id="A1.I1" class="ltx_description">
<dt id="A1.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.ix1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Addition</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A1.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.53467pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{-6.82222pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\ell}$}}}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\{f\geq 0,g\geq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:8.5pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:8.5pt;" voffset="-6.8pt" width="8.5pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mpadded><mpadded style="width:8.5pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="8.5pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.53467pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{-6.82222pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\ell}$}}}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\{f\geq 0,g\geq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{A}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.53467pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{-6.82222pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\ell}$}}}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\{f+g\geq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:8.5pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:8.5pt;" voffset="-6.8pt" width="8.5pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mpadded><mpadded style="width:8.5pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="8.5pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.53467pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{-6.82222pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\ell}$}}}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\{f+g\geq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A1.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.ix2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Multiplication</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A1.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{A}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.53467pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{-6.82222pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\ell}$}}}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\{f\geq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:8.5pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:8.5pt;" voffset="-6.8pt" width="8.5pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mpadded><mpadded style="width:8.5pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="8.5pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.53467pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{-6.82222pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\ell}$}}}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\{f\geq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{A}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{10.05208pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-10.05208pt\raisebox{-7.75671pt}{\makebox[10.05208pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\ell^{\prime}}$}}}\hskip-10.05208pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[10.05208pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\{g\geq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:10.1pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:10.1pt;" voffset="-7.8pt" width="10.1pt"><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">′</mo></msup></mpadded><mpadded style="width:10.1pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="10.1pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{10.05208pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-10.05208pt\raisebox{-7.75671pt}{\makebox[10.05208pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\ell^{\prime}}$}}}\hskip-10.05208pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[10.05208pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\{g\geq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{A}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{19.53825pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-19.53825pt\raisebox{-7.75671pt}{\makebox[19.53825pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\ell+\ell^{\prime}}$}}}\hskip-19.53825pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[19.53825pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\{fg\geq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:19.5pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:19.5pt;" voffset="-7.8pt" width="19.5pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">+</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">′</mo></msup></mpadded><mpadded style="width:19.5pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="19.5pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>f</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{19.53825pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-19.53825pt\raisebox{-7.75671pt}{\makebox[19.53825pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\ell+\ell^{\prime}}$}}}\hskip-19.53825pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[19.53825pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\{fg\geq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A1.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.ix3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Transitivity</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A1.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="A1.I1.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.53467pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{-6.82222pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\ell}$}}}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:8.5pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:8.5pt;" voffset="-6.8pt" width="8.5pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mpadded><mpadded style="width:8.5pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="8.5pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi></mpadded></mpadded><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.53467pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{-6.82222pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\ell}$}}}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A1.I1.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{10.05208pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-10.05208pt\raisebox{-7.75671pt}{\makebox[10.05208pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\ell^{\prime}}$}}}\hskip-10.05208pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[10.05208pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:10.1pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:10.1pt;" voffset="-7.8pt" width="10.1pt"><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">′</mo></msup></mpadded><mpadded style="width:10.1pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="10.1pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi></mpadded></mpadded><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{10.05208pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-10.05208pt\raisebox{-7.75671pt}{\makebox[10.05208pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\ell^{\prime}}$}}}\hskip-10.05208pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[10.05208pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="A1.I1.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{13.39934pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-13.39934pt\raisebox{-7.75671pt}{\makebox[13.39934pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\ell\ell^{\prime}}$}}}\hskip-13.39934pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[13.39934pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:13.4pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:13.4pt;" voffset="-7.8pt" width="13.4pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">′</mo></msup></mpadded><mpadded style="width:13.4pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="13.4pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi></mpadded></mpadded><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{13.39934pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-13.39934pt\raisebox{-7.75671pt}{\makebox[13.39934pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\ell\ell^{\prime}}$}}}\hskip-13.39934pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[13.39934pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A1.I1.ix4" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A1.I1.ix4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Substitution</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A1.I1.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.ix4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let </span><math id="A1.I1.ix4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F:\mathbb{R}^{n}\to\mathbb{R}^{m},G:\mathbb{R}^{n}\to\mathbb{R}^{k},H:\mathbb{R}^{p}\to\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F:\mathbb{R}^{n}\to\mathbb{R}^{m},G:\mathbb{R}^{n}\to\mathbb{R}^{k},H:\mathbb{R}^{p}\to\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be vector-valued polynomials. If </span><math id="A1.I1.ix4.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{F\geq 0\}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.53467pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{-6.82222pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\ell}$}}}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\{G\geq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:8.5pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:8.5pt;" voffset="-6.8pt" width="8.5pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mpadded><mpadded style="width:8.5pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="8.5pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{F\geq 0\}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.53467pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{-6.82222pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\ell}$}}}\hskip-8.53467pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.53467pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\{G\geq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="A1.I1.ix4.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{F(H)\geq 0\}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{32.64035pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-32.64035pt\raisebox{-7.21112pt}{\makebox[32.64035pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\ell\deg(H)}$}}}\hskip-32.64035pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[32.64035pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\{G(H)\geq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:32.6pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:32.6pt;" voffset="-7.2pt" width="32.6pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">H</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mpadded><mpadded style="width:32.6pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="32.6pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{F(H)\geq 0\}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{32.64035pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-32.64035pt\raisebox{-7.21112pt}{\makebox[32.64035pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\ell\deg(H)}$}}}\hskip-32.64035pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[32.64035pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\{G(H)\geq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.ix4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></dd>
</dl>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact A.4</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> be a univariate polynomial in <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(x)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(x)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{26.3307pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-26.3307pt\raisebox{-7.21112pt}{\makebox[26.3307pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\deg(p)}$}}}\hskip-26.3307pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[26.3307pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\{p(x)\geq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:26.3pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:26.3pt;" voffset="-7.2pt" width="26.3pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em">deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">p</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mpadded><mpadded style="width:26.3pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="26.3pt"><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{26.3307pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-26.3307pt\raisebox{-7.21112pt}{\makebox[26.3307pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\deg(p)}$}}}\hskip-26.3307pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[26.3307pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{x}$}}}$}}}\{p(x)\geq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact A.5</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y,z\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y,z\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\vdash_{2}\left\{3\left(x^{2}+y^{2}+z^{2}\right)\geq\left(x+y+z\right)^{2}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>⊢</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>3</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\vdash_{2}\left\{3\left(x^{2}+y^{2}+z^{2}\right)\geq\left(x+y+z\right)^{2}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 3\left(x^{2}+y^{2}+z^{2}\right)-\left(x+y+z\right)^{2}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 3\left(x^{2}+y^{2}+z^{2}\right)-\left(x+y+z\right)^{2}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~3x^{2}+3y^{2}+3z^{2}-x^{2}-y^{2}-z^{2}-2xy-2xz-2yz" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~3x^{2}+3y^{2}+3z^{2}-x^{2}-y^{2}-z^{2}-2xy-2xz-2yz</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~2x^{2}+2y^{2}+2z^{2}-2xy-2xz-2yz" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~2x^{2}+2y^{2}+2z^{2}-2xy-2xz-2yz</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left(x-y\right)^{2}+\left(x-z\right)^{2}+\left(y-z\right)^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left(x-y\right)^{2}+\left(x-z\right)^{2}+\left(y-z\right)^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">which completes the proof by Definition <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Sum-of-squares proof ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Pseudo-expectation properties</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present pseudo-expectation properties. It satisfies the linearity property.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact A.6</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Linearity of Pseudoexpectation)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any polynomials <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f,g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f,g</annotation></semantics></math> and scalars <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\beta\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\beta\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, the pseudoexpectation operator <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}</annotation></semantics></math> is linear:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}[\alpha f+\beta g]=\alpha\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}[f]+\beta\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}[g]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}[\alpha f+\beta g]=\alpha\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}[f]+\beta\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}[g].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In addition, we can use Cauchy Schwarz inequality in pseudoexpectation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact A.7</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Cauchy Schwarz for Pseudoexpectation, Fact 3.10 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f,g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f,g</annotation></semantics></math> be polynomials of degree at most <math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[fg\right]\leq\sqrt{\widetilde{\E}\left[f^{2}\right]}\sqrt{\widetilde{\E}\left[g^{2}\right]}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>fg</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[fg\right]\leq\sqrt{\widetilde{\E}\left[f^{2}\right]}\sqrt{\widetilde{\E}\left[g^{2}\right]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact A.8</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We have the following facts:</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Part 1.</span><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> If </span><math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then we can get</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0\leq\widetilde{\E}\left[\left(X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right)^{2}\right]=\widetilde{\E}\left[X^{2}\right]-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0.1389em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0.1389em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0\leq\widetilde{\E}\left[\left(X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right)^{2}\right]=\widetilde{\E}\left[X^{2}\right]-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Part 2.</span><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> If </span><math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=(x_{1},\dots,x_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=(x_{1},\dots,x_{d})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> denotes the tuple of indeterminates, where each </span><math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}\in R[x_{1},\dots,x_{d}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}\in R[x_{1},\dots,x_{d}]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]=\left(\widetilde{\E}\left[x_{1}\right],\dots,\widetilde{\E}\left[x_{d}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]=\left(\widetilde{\E}\left[x_{1}\right],\dots,\widetilde{\E}\left[x_{d}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then we can get</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]=\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|X\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]-\left\|\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right\|_{2}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0.1389em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]=\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|X\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]-\left\|\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Part 3.</span><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> Let </span><math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be a given vector. If </span><math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=(x_{1},\dots,x_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=(x_{1},\dots,x_{d})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> denotes the tuple of indeterminates, where each </span><math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}\in\mathbb{R}[x_{1},\dots,x_{d}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}\in\mathbb{R}[x_{1},\dots,x_{d}]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]=\left(\widetilde{\E}\left[x_{1}\right],\dots,\widetilde{\E}\left[x_{d}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]=\left(\widetilde{\E}\left[x_{1}\right],\dots,\widetilde{\E}\left[x_{d}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then we can get</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|x-X\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]\geq\left\|x-\widetilde{\E}[X]\right\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|x-X\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]\geq\left\|x-\widetilde{\E}[X]\right\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Part 1.<span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, we consider the case where <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left(X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right)^{2}\right]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left(X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right)^{2}\right]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[X^{2}+\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]^{2}-2X\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[X^{2}+\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]^{2}-2X\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[X^{2}\right]+\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]^{2}-2\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[X^{2}\right]+\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]^{2}-2\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[X^{2}\right]-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[X^{2}\right]-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second step follows from the linearity of pseudo-expectation (see <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem6" title="Fact A.6 (Linearity of Pseudoexpectation). ‣ A.2 Pseudo-expectation properties ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fact</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Part 2.<span id="A1.SS2.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Second, we consider the case where <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\left(X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right)\left(X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right)^{\top}\right)_{i,i}=\left(X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right)_{i}\cdot\left(X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right)_{i}=\left(X_{i}-\widetilde{\E}\left[X_{i}\right]\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\left(X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right)\left(X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right)^{\top}\right)_{i,i}=\left(X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right)_{i}\cdot\left(X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right)_{i}=\left(X_{i}-\widetilde{\E}\left[X_{i}\right]\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\langle X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right],X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right\rangle\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\langle X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right],X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right\rangle\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\mathrm{tr}\left[\widetilde{\E}\left[\left(X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right)\left(X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right)^{\top}\right]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\mathrm{tr}\left[\widetilde{\E}\left[\left(X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right)\left(X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right)^{\top}\right]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{i=1}^{d}\left(\widetilde{\E}\left[X_{i}^{2}\right]-\widetilde{\E}\left[X_{i}\right]^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{i=1}^{d}\left(\widetilde{\E}\left[X_{i}^{2}\right]-\widetilde{\E}\left[X_{i}\right]^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{d}X_{i}^{2}\right]-\sum_{i=1}^{d}\widetilde{\E}\left[X_{i}\right]^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0.167em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{d}X_{i}^{2}\right]-\sum_{i=1}^{d}\widetilde{\E}\left[X_{i}\right]^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|X\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]-\left\|\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right\|_{2}^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|X\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]-\left\|\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right\|_{2}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">where third step follows from <span id="A1.SS2.p9.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 1</span> and Eq. (<a href="#A1.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.2 Pseudo-expectation properties ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), the fourth step follows from linearity (see <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem6" title="Fact A.6 (Linearity of Pseudoexpectation). ‣ A.2 Pseudo-expectation properties ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fact</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a>), and the last step follows from the definition of the <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Part 3.<span id="A1.SS2.p10.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Furthermore, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|x-X\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|x-X\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|X\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|x\right\|_{2}^{2}-2\langle x,X\rangle\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|X\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|x\right\|_{2}^{2}-2\langle x,X\rangle\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|X\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]+\left\|x\right\|_{2}^{2}-2\left\langle x,\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|X\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]+\left\|x\right\|_{2}^{2}-2\left\langle x,\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left(\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|X\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]-\left\|\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right\|_{2}^{2}\right)+\left(\left\|\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|x\right\|_{2}^{2}-2\left\langle x,\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right\rangle\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left(\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|X\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]-\left\|\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right\|_{2}^{2}\right)+\left(\left\|\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|x\right\|_{2}^{2}-2\left\langle x,\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right\rangle\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]+\left\|x-\widetilde{\E}[X]\right\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|X-\widetilde{\E}\left[X\right]\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]+\left\|x-\widetilde{\E}[X]\right\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|x-\widetilde{\E}[X]\right\|_{2}^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|x-\widetilde{\E}[X]\right\|_{2}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second step follows from the linearity of the pseudo-expectation (see <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem6" title="Fact A.6 (Linearity of Pseudoexpectation). ‣ A.2 Pseudo-expectation properties ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fact</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a>), the fourth step follows from <span id="A1.SS2.p11.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 2</span> of <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem8" title="Fact A.8. ‣ A.2 Pseudo-expectation properties ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fact</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a>, and the last step follows from the definition of pseudo-expectation that <math id="A1.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\E}[X^{2}]\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\E}[X^{2}]\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Probabilistic and Algebraic Tools</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present basic probabilistic and algebraic tools.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact A.9</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Union Bound)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1},A_{2},\dots,A_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1},A_{2},\dots,A_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> be events in a probability space. Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\left[\bigcup_{i=1}^{m}A_{i}\right]\leq\sum_{i=1}^{m}\Pr[A_{i}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\left[\bigcup_{i=1}^{m}A_{i}\right]\leq\sum_{i=1}^{m}\Pr[A_{i}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact A.10</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Markov’s Inequality)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be a non-negative random variable and let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[X\geq a]\leq\frac{\mathbb{E}[X]}{a}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[X\geq a]\leq\frac{\mathbb{E}[X]}{a}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact A.11</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Multiplicative Chernoff Bound)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},X_{2},\dots,X_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},X_{2},\dots,X_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be independent random variables taking values in <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=\sum_{i=1}^{n}X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=\sum_{i=1}^{n}X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=\mathbb{E}[X]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=\mathbb{E}[X]</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for any <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the following holds:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr[X\geq(1+\delta)\mu]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr[X\geq(1+\delta)\mu]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\exp\left(-\frac{\delta^{2}\mu}{3}\right)\quad\text{for }0&lt;\delta\leq 1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\exp\left(-\frac{\delta^{2}\mu}{3}\right)\quad\text{for }0&lt;\delta\leq 1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr[X\geq(1+\delta)\mu]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr[X\geq(1+\delta)\mu]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\exp\left(-\frac{\delta\mu}{3}\right)\quad\text{for }\delta&gt;1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\exp\left(-\frac{\delta\mu}{3}\right)\quad\text{for }\delta&gt;1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact A.12</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be two distributions with means <math id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E\left[X\right]=\mu_{X},\E\left[X^{\prime}\right]=\mu_{X^{\prime}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E\left[X\right]=\mu_{X},\E\left[X^{\prime}\right]=\mu_{X^{\prime}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}\left[X^{\prime}\right]\preceq\E\left[\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)\cdot\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)^{\top}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">⪯</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}\left[X^{\prime}\right]\preceq\E\left[\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)\cdot\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)^{\top}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since for any arbitrary vector <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\setminus\left\{0\right\}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>∖</mo><msup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\setminus\left\{0\right\}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x^{\top}\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\cdot\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}x=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x^{\top}\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\cdot\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}x=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\langle x,\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\rangle^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\langle x,\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\rangle^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we can see</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}\left[X^{\prime}\right]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}\left[X^{\prime}\right]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\E\left[\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\cdot\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\E\left[\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\cdot\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\E\left[\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}+\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\cdot\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}+\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\E\left[\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}+\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\cdot\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}+\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\E\left[\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)\cdot\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)^{\top}\right]+\E\left[\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)\cdot\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\E\left[\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)\cdot\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)^{\top}\right]+\E\left[\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)\cdot\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~+\E\left[\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\cdot\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)^{\top}\right]+\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\cdot\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~+\E\left[\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\cdot\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)^{\top}\right]+\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\cdot\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex51.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\E\left[\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)\cdot\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)^{\top}\right]+\left(\E\left[X^{\prime}\right]-\mu_{X}\right)\cdot\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\E\left[\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)\cdot\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)^{\top}\right]+\left(\E\left[X^{\prime}\right]-\mu_{X}\right)\cdot\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~+\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\cdot\left(\E\left[X^{\prime}\right]-\mu_{X}\right)^{\top}+\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\cdot\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~+\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\cdot\left(\E\left[X^{\prime}\right]-\mu_{X}\right)^{\top}+\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\cdot\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex53.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\E\left[\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)\cdot\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)^{\top}\right]-2\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X}^{\prime}\right)\cdot\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}+\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\cdot\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\E\left[\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)\cdot\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)^{\top}\right]-2\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X}^{\prime}\right)\cdot\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}+\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\cdot\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex54.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\E\left[\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)\cdot\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)^{\top}\right]-\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\cdot\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\E\left[\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)\cdot\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)^{\top}\right]-\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\cdot\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\preceq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⪯</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\preceq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex55.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\E\left[\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)\cdot\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)^{\top}\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\E\left[\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)\cdot\left(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right)^{\top}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from the definition of <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}\left[\cdot\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}\left[\cdot\right]</annotation></semantics></math>, the third and the fourth steps follow from the linearity property of the expectation, the fifth step follows from <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E\left[X^{\prime}\right]=\mu_{X^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E\left[X^{\prime}\right]=\mu_{X^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the last step follows from the fact that <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\cdot\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\cdot\left(\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is PSD (see Eq. (<a href="#A1.Ex46" title="In Proof. ‣ A.3 Probabilistic and Algebraic Tools ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>)).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact A.13</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|uu^{\top}\right\|_{2}=\left\|u\right\|_{2}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|uu^{\top}\right\|_{2}=\left\|u\right\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that by the definition of the spectral norm, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|uu^{\top}\right\|_{2}=\sup_{v\in\mathbb{R}^{d},\left\|v\right\|_{2}=1}\left\|uu^{\top}v\right\|_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|uu^{\top}\right\|_{2}=\sup_{v\in\mathbb{R}^{d},\left\|v\right\|_{2}=1}\left\|uu^{\top}v\right\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the definition of the <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|uu^{\top}v\right\|_{2}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|uu^{\top}v\right\|_{2}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex57.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sqrt{\sum_{i=1}^{d}\left(uu^{\top}v\right)_{i}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sqrt{\sum_{i=1}^{d}\left(uu^{\top}v\right)_{i}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex58.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sqrt{\sum_{i=1}^{d}\left(u\left(u^{\top}v\right)\right)_{i}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sqrt{\sum_{i=1}^{d}\left(u\left(u^{\top}v\right)\right)_{i}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex59.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sqrt{\left(u^{\top}v\right)^{2}\sum_{i=1}^{d}u_{i}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sqrt{\left(u^{\top}v\right)^{2}\sum_{i=1}^{d}u_{i}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex60.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~|u^{\top}v|\cdot\left\|u\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~|u^{\top}v|\cdot\left\|u\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|u\right\|_{2}^{2}\cdot\left\|v\right\|_{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|u\right\|_{2}^{2}\cdot\left\|v\right\|_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second step follows from the associative law, the third step follows from <math id="A1.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\top}v\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\top}v\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the last step follows from the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining Eq. (<a href="#A1.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ Proof. ‣ A.3 Probabilistic and Algebraic Tools ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A1.Ex57" title="In Proof. ‣ A.3 Probabilistic and Algebraic Tools ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|uu^{\top}\right\|_{2}=\left\|u\right\|_{2}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|uu^{\top}\right\|_{2}=\left\|u\right\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact A.14</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Vector Bernstein inequality, Theorem 12 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},\ldots,X_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},\ldots,X_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> be independent zero-mean vector-valued random variables.
Let</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=\left\|\sum_{i=1}^{m}X_{i}\right\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=\left\|\sum_{i=1}^{m}X_{i}\right\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\left[N\geq\sqrt{V}+t\right]\leq\exp\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{4V}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><msqrt><mi>V</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\left[N\geq\sqrt{V}+t\right]\leq\exp\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{4V}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=\sum_{i}\E[\left\|X_{i}\right\|_{2}^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=\sum_{i}\E[\left\|X_{i}\right\|_{2}^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem14.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq V/\left(\max\left\|X_{i}\right\|_{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq V/\left(\max\left\|X_{i}\right\|_{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem15" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact A.15</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Hoeffding’s Inequality)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem15.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem15.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem15.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},X_{2},\dots,X_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},X_{2},\dots,X_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be independent random variables such that <math id="A1.Thmtheorem15.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}\leq X_{i}\leq b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}\leq X_{i}\leq b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely.
Define the empirical mean <math id="A1.Thmtheorem15.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{X}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{X}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and the true mean <math id="A1.Thmtheorem15.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=\E[\hat{X}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=\E[\hat{X}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then for any <math id="A1.Thmtheorem15.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\left[|\hat{X}-\mu|\geq\varepsilon\right]\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{2n^{2}\varepsilon^{2}}{\sum_{i=1}^{N}(b_{i}-a_{i})^{2}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≥</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\left[|\hat{X}-\mu|\geq\varepsilon\right]\leq 2\exp\left(-\frac{2n^{2}\varepsilon^{2}}{\sum_{i=1}^{N}(b_{i}-a_{i})^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem16" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact A.16</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem16.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem16.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem16.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem16.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},\dots,X_{n}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},\dots,X_{n}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be i.i.d. random variables satisfying <math id="A1.Thmtheorem16.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[X_{i}]=\mu\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[X_{i}]=\mu\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem16.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}\left[X_{i}\right]=\Sigma\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}\left[X_{i}\right]=\Sigma\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="A1.Thmtheorem16.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem16.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{X}:=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{X}:=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem16.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem16.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem16.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}\left[\overline{X}\right]=\frac{1}{n}\Sigma." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}\left[\overline{X}\right]=\frac{1}{n}\Sigma.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can get</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}\left[\overline{X}\right]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}\left[\overline{X}\right]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex66.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\mathrm{Cov}\left[\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}X_{i}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\mathrm{Cov}\left[\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}X_{i}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex67.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n^{2}}\mathrm{Cov}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{n}X_{i}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n^{2}}\mathrm{Cov}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{n}X_{i}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex68.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n^{2}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathrm{Cov}\left[X_{i}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n^{2}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathrm{Cov}\left[X_{i}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex69.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n^{2}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n^{2}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex70.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{n}{n^{2}}\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{n}{n^{2}}\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex71.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\Sigma." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\Sigma.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#A2.SS1" title="B.1 Accurate Estimation of the Empirical Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, we extend the traditional SoS approach on arbitrary bound on the empirical covariance. In <a href="#A2.SS2" title="B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>, we improve the result of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>, Proposition 3.9]</cite> showing that using truncation is sufficient to obtain a stable subset with high probability.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Accurate Estimation of the Empirical Mean</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Any large subset of points with a sufficiently low empirical covariance will have an empirical mean close to the true mean <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>. We know that the set of all clean samples satisfies this property with high probability. The crucial implication, however, is that a valid subset <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> does not need to be perfectly clean. It can include corrupted points, provided they are not <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">harmful</span> in a way that significantly pulls the mean and consequently increases the set’s empirical covariance. This gives us a <em id="A2.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">verifiable criterion</em>: instead of needing to know which samples are clean, we only need to find a large subset that satisfies this geometric condition.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To identify such a large subset, we employ the SoS framework from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>, <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite>. This framework reformulates algorithmic and statistical problems into an algebraic representation described by a collection of polynomial constraints.
In the context of robust mean estimation, these polynomial constraints can be formulated as:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{i}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{i}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=W_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=W_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}W_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}W_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\varepsilon)n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\varepsilon)n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{i}(Z_{i}-v_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{i}(Z_{i}-v_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overline{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overline{Z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(Z_{i}-\overline{Z})(Z_{i}-\overline{Z})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(Z_{i}-\overline{Z})(Z_{i}-\overline{Z})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\xi\mathbb{I}_{d}-BB^{\top}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\xi\mathbb{I}_{d}-BB^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1},\ldots,Z_{n}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1},\ldots,Z_{n}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> are variables representing approximations of the clean samples <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},\ldots,z_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},\ldots,z_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1},\ldots,W_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1},\ldots,W_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are real-valued variables such that, for each <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> serves as an indicator of whether <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}=v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}=v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> is a matrix of auxiliary (“slack”) variables; <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is an arbitrary positive real number.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.SS1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.1</span></span><span id="A2.SS1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1},\dots,v_{n}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1},\dots,v_{n}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>-corrupted sample drawn from a distribution <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> of mean <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and covariance <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma\preceq\chi\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma\preceq\chi\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> for some arbitrary <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{*}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{*}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> is unknown. Let <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> be the input of the SoS algorithm and <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> be the failure probability. If the degree-<math id="A2.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> pseudoexpectation <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the system of polynomial constraints <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{C}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. (<a href="#A2.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ B.1 Accurate Estimation of the Empirical Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), Eq. (<a href="#A2.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ B.1 Accurate Estimation of the Empirical Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), Eq. (<a href="#A2.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ B.1 Accurate Estimation of the Empirical Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>), Eq. (<a href="#A2.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ B.1 Accurate Estimation of the Empirical Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>), and Eq. (<a href="#A2.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ B.1 Accurate Estimation of the Empirical Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>)), then there exists a polynomial time algorithm that outputs <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}[\overline{Z}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}[\overline{Z}]\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}[\overline{Z}]-\overline{z}\right\|_{2}=O(\sqrt{\left(\varepsilon+\varepsilon^{*}\right)\upsilon})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>υ</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}[\overline{Z}]-\overline{z}\right\|_{2}=O(\sqrt{\left(\varepsilon+\varepsilon^{*}\right)\upsilon}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with probability at least <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\upsilon:=\max\{\chi,\xi\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>υ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\upsilon:=\max\{\chi,\xi\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We use a similar proof structure compared with <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>, Lemma 2.11]</cite>, but our analysis focuses on more general settings:</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is unknown,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the empirical covariance bound is not fixed (for arbitrary <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. (<a href="#A2.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ B.1 Accurate Estimation of the Empirical Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>)), and</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the covariance bound of the distribution <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> is not fixed (for arbitrary <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma\preceq\chi\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma\preceq\chi\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},\ldots,z_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},\ldots,z_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the uncorrupted samples drawn from the distribution <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}=z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}=z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> holds for a <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> fraction of indices <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall that the empirical mean is defined as <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{Z}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{Z}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let the empirical covariance be</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{Z}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(Z_{i}-\overline{Z})(Z_{i}-\overline{Z})^{\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{Z}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(Z_{i}-\overline{Z})(Z_{i}-\overline{Z})^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Define <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{z}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{z}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\E\left[\Sigma_{z}\right]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\E\left[\Sigma_{z}\right]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex74.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\E\left[\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left(z_{i}-\overline{z}\right)\left(z_{i}-\overline{z}\right)^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\E\left[\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left(z_{i}-\overline{z}\right)\left(z_{i}-\overline{z}\right)^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex75.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\E\left[\left(z_{i}-\overline{z}\right)\left(z_{i}-\overline{z}\right)^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\E\left[\left(z_{i}-\overline{z}\right)\left(z_{i}-\overline{z}\right)^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex76.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathrm{Cov}\left[z_{i}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathrm{Cov}\left[z_{i}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\preceq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⪯</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\preceq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex77.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\chi\mathbb{I}_{d}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\chi\mathbb{I}_{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">which implies that with high probability, for all arbitrary vector <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b^{\top}\Sigma_{z}b\leq 2\chi\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b^{\top}\Sigma_{z}b\leq 2\chi\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can get</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{C}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{4}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Z}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖢</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:9.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="9.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">4</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="9.0pt"><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mpadded></mpadded><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{C}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{4}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Z}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex78.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex79.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\langle\overline{z}-\overline{Z},\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\rangle^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\langle\overline{z}-\overline{Z},\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\rangle^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex80.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~\left(\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(1-W_{i}\mathds{1}_{\left\{z_{i}=v_{i}\right\}})\langle z_{i}-Z_{i},\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\rangle+\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}W_{i}\mathds{1}_{\left\{z_{i}=v_{i}\right\}}\langle z_{i}-Z_{i},\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\rangle\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left(\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(1-W_{i}\mathds{1}_{\left\{z_{i}=v_{i}\right\}})\langle z_{i}-Z_{i},\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\rangle+\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}W_{i}\mathds{1}_{\left\{z_{i}=v_{i}\right\}}\langle z_{i}-Z_{i},\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\rangle\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex81.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~\left(\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(1-W_{i}\mathds{1}_{\left\{z_{i}=v_{i}\right\}})\langle z_{i}-Z_{i},\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\rangle\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left(\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(1-W_{i}\mathds{1}_{\left\{z_{i}=v_{i}\right\}})\langle z_{i}-Z_{i},\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\rangle\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex82.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~\left(\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(1-W_{i}\mathds{1}_{\left\{z_{i}=v_{i}\right\}})^{2}\right)\left(\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\langle z_{i}-Z_{i},\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\rangle^{2}\right)\Bigg\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left(\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(1-W_{i}\mathds{1}_{\left\{z_{i}=v_{i}\right\}})^{2}\right)\left(\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\langle z_{i}-Z_{i},\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\rangle^{2}\right)\Bigg\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle a,a\rangle=\left\|a\right\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle a,a\rangle=\left\|a\right\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the second step follows from the constraint <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}(v_{i}-Z_{i})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}(v_{i}-Z_{i})=0</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. (<a href="#A2.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ B.1 Accurate Estimation of the Empirical Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>)), the third step follows from the <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vdash\langle p,q\rangle^{2}\leq\left\|p\right\|_{2}^{2}\left\|q\right\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⊢</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vdash\langle p,q\rangle^{2}\leq\left\|p\right\|_{2}^{2}\left\|q\right\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> version of degree-6 SoS Cauchy–Schwarz (Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Fact A.1 (SoS Cauchy-Schwarz, Claim 2.6 in []). ‣ A.1 Sum-of-squares ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Considering the first term, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{C}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{2}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Z}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(1-W_{i}\mathds{1}_{\left\{z_{i}=v_{i}\right\}})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖢</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:9.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="9.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="9.0pt"><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{C}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{2}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Z}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(1-W_{i}\mathds{1}_{\left\{z_{i}=v_{i}\right\}})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex83.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(1-2W_{i}\mathds{1}_{\left\{z_{i}=v_{i}\right\}}+W_{i}^{2}\mathds{1}_{\left\{z_{i}=v_{i}\right\}}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(1-2W_{i}\mathds{1}_{\left\{z_{i}=v_{i}\right\}}+W_{i}^{2}\mathds{1}_{\left\{z_{i}=v_{i}\right\}}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(1-W_{i}\mathds{1}_{\left\{z_{i}=v_{i}\right\}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(1-W_{i}\mathds{1}_{\left\{z_{i}=v_{i}\right\}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(1-W_{i})+\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(1-\mathds{1}_{\left\{z_{i}=v_{i}\right\}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(1-W_{i})+\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(1-\mathds{1}_{\left\{z_{i}=v_{i}\right\}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\varepsilon+\varepsilon^{*}\Bigg\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\varepsilon+\varepsilon^{*}\Bigg\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second step follows from <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}^{2}=W_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}^{2}=W_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Eq. (<a href="#A2.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ B.1 Accurate Estimation of the Empirical Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>)) and the third step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A2.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ B.1 Accurate Estimation of the Empirical Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) and <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathds{1}_{\left\{z_{i}\neq v_{i}\right\}}\leq\varepsilon^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mn>𝟙</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathds{1}_{\left\{z_{i}\neq v_{i}\right\}}\leq\varepsilon^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Considering <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\langle z_{i}-Z_{i},\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\rangle^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\langle z_{i}-Z_{i},\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\rangle^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we define <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\overline{z}-\overline{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\overline{z}-\overline{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{C}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{4}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Z}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\langle z_{i}-Z_{i},b\rangle^{2}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖢</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:9.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="9.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">4</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="9.0pt"><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{C}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{4}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Z}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\langle z_{i}-Z_{i},b\rangle^{2}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex87.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\langle z_{i}-Z_{i}+b-b,b\rangle^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\langle z_{i}-Z_{i}+b-b,b\rangle^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex88.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(\langle z_{i}-\overline{z},b\rangle-\langle Z_{i}-Z,b\rangle+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(\langle z_{i}-\overline{z},b\rangle-\langle Z_{i}-Z,b\rangle+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex89.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{3}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\langle z_{i}-\overline{z},b\rangle^{2}+\langle Z_{i}-Z,b\rangle^{2}+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{3}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\langle z_{i}-\overline{z},b\rangle^{2}+\langle Z_{i}-Z,b\rangle^{2}+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex90"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex90.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~3\left(b^{\top}\Sigma_{z}b+b^{\top}\Sigma_{Z}b+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)\Bigg\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~3\left(b^{\top}\Sigma_{z}b+b^{\top}\Sigma_{Z}b+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)\Bigg\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second step follows from the linearity, the third step follows from Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem5" title="Fact A.5. ‣ A.1 Sum-of-squares ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>, and the last step follows from the definition of the covariance matrix.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{Z}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{Z}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(Z_{i}-\overline{Z})(Z_{i}-\overline{Z})^{\top}=2\xi\mathbb{I}_{d}-BB^{\top}\}\vdash\{b^{\top}\Sigma_{Z}b\leq 2\xi\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊢</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mi>b</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>ξ</mi><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(Z_{i}-\overline{Z})(Z_{i}-\overline{Z})^{\top}=2\xi\mathbb{I}_{d}-BB^{\top}\}\vdash\{b^{\top}\Sigma_{Z}b\leq 2\xi\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, so combining with Eq. (<a href="#A2.E11" title="Equation 11 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.1 Accurate Estimation of the Empirical Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>), we conclude that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{C}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{4}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Z}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\langle z_{i}-Z_{i},b\rangle^{2}\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖢</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:9.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="9.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">4</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="9.0pt"><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{C}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{4}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Z}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\langle z_{i}-Z_{i},b\rangle^{2}\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex91.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~3\left(2\xi\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}+2\chi\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~3\left(2\xi\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}+2\chi\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex92"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex92.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~3\left(4\upsilon\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)\Bigg\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>υ</mi><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~3\left(4\upsilon\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)\Bigg\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second step follows from <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\upsilon:=\max\{\xi,\chi\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>υ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\upsilon:=\max\{\xi,\chi\}</annotation></semantics></math> (see from the lemma statement).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, putting everything together, we conclude that <math id="A2.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{4}\leq O(\varepsilon+\varepsilon^{*})\cdot(4\upsilon\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{4})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>υ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{4}\leq O(\varepsilon+\varepsilon^{*})\cdot(4\upsilon\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{4})</annotation></semantics></math> has a degree-6 sum-of-squares proof, as desired.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Until now, we have shown the following upper bound for the 4-th moment:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]\leq\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]O\left(\left(\varepsilon+\varepsilon^{*}\right)\upsilon\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0.1389em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>υ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]\leq\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]O\left(\left(\varepsilon+\varepsilon^{*}\right)\upsilon\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, by using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, the 4-th moment can also be lower bounded:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex93"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]^{2}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]^{2}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex93.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{2}\cdot 1\right]^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{2}\cdot 1\right]^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex94"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex94.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\left(\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right)^{2}\right]\cdot\widetilde{\E}\left[1^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0.055em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\left(\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right)^{2}\right]\cdot\widetilde{\E}\left[1^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the last step follows from the definition of pseudo-expectation that <math id="A2.SS1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\E}[1]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\E}[1]=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining Eq. (<a href="#A2.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.1 Accurate Estimation of the Empirical Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A2.Ex93" title="In Proof. ‣ B.1 Accurate Estimation of the Empirical Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>), we can get</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex95"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]^{2}\leq\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]\leq\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]O\left(\left(\varepsilon+\varepsilon^{*}\right)\upsilon\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0.1389em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0.1389em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>υ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]^{2}\leq\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]\leq\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]O\left(\left(\varepsilon+\varepsilon^{*}\right)\upsilon\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">which implies</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]\leq O\left(\left(\varepsilon+\varepsilon^{*}\right)\upsilon\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>υ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]\leq O\left(\left(\varepsilon+\varepsilon^{*}\right)\upsilon\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Furthermore, by <span id="A2.SS1.p14.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 3</span> of Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem8" title="Fact A.8. ‣ A.2 Pseudo-expectation properties ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]\geq\left\|\overline{z}-\widetilde{\E}[\overline{Z}]\right\|_{2}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{z}-\overline{Z}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]\geq\left\|\overline{z}-\widetilde{\E}[\overline{Z}]\right\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, combining Eq. (<a href="#A2.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.1 Accurate Estimation of the Empirical Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A2.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.1 Accurate Estimation of the Empirical Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>), we can get</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex96"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\overline{z}-\widetilde{\E}[Z]\right\|_{2}^{2}\leq O\left(\left(\varepsilon+\varepsilon^{*}\right)\upsilon\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>υ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\overline{z}-\widetilde{\E}[Z]\right\|_{2}^{2}\leq O\left(\left(\varepsilon+\varepsilon^{*}\right)\upsilon\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">which completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, our goal is to prove Lemma <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2" title="B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a>. It states that given a sufficiently large <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-corrupted set, each of its elements is sampled from a distribution <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, we can get that its empirical mean is close to the mean of the distribution <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> with high probability. However, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite> claims that this statement holds with probability at least <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, which is not sufficient for our use. Therefore, we show that this statement holds with probability at least <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-d\exp(-\Omega(n\varepsilon/d))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-d\exp(-\Omega(n\varepsilon/d))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.2.1 </span>Background</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we list basic definitions and mathematical properties from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>. We define a stable set as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.2</span></span><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Stability Condition, Definition 2.1 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>)<span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Fix <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;1/2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\geq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\geq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. A finite set <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varepsilon,\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varepsilon,\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>-stable (with respect to a vector <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> or a distribution <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{X}:=\mathbb{E}[X]=\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{X}:=\mathbb{E}[X]=\mu</annotation></semantics></math>) if for every unit vector <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and every <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}\subseteq S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊆</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}\subseteq S</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|S^{\prime}|\geq(1-\varepsilon)|S|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|S^{\prime}|\geq(1-\varepsilon)|S|</annotation></semantics></math>, the following conditions hold:</p>
<ol id="A2.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\frac{1}{|S^{\prime}|}\sum_{x\in S^{\prime}}v\cdot(x-\mu)\right|\leq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\frac{1}{|S^{\prime}|}\sum_{x\in S^{\prime}}v\cdot(x-\mu)\right|\leq\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\frac{1}{|S^{\prime}|}\sum_{x\in S^{\prime}}\left(v\cdot(x-\mu)\right)^{2}-1\right|\leq\delta^{2}/\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\frac{1}{|S^{\prime}|}\sum_{x\in S^{\prime}}\left(v\cdot(x-\mu)\right)^{2}-1\right|\leq\delta^{2}/\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">If we have a stable set with respect to a distribution, then we can easily approximate the mean of this distribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Theorem 2.11 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(3\varepsilon,\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(3\varepsilon,\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>-stable set with respect to a distribution <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently small. Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> be an <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-corrupted version of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. There exists a polynomial time algorithm which given <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> returns <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex97" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\hat{\mu}-\mu_{X}\right\|_{2}=O(\delta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\hat{\mu}-\mu_{X}\right\|_{2}=O(\delta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To prove a set is stable with respect to a distribution, we need to show that 1). the empirical mean of this set is close to the mean of the distribution, and 2). the covariance of this set satisfies <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}\left[S\right]\preceq O(\mathbb{I}_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}\left[S\right]\preceq O(\mathbb{I}_{d})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.4</span></span><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Lemma 3.11 from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>)<span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A set <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varepsilon,O(\sqrt{\varepsilon}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varepsilon,O(\sqrt{\varepsilon}))</annotation></semantics></math>-stable with respect to a distribution <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if the following conditions hold:</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\mu_{S}-\mu_{X}\right\|_{2}=O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\mu_{S}-\mu_{X}\right\|_{2}=O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon}\right)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}\left[S\right]\preceq O\left(\mathbb{I}_{d}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}\left[S\right]\preceq O\left(\mathbb{I}_{d}\right)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.2.2 </span>The Existence of a Stable Set</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, our goal is to show the following lemma. With high probability, the empirical mean of a sufficiently large subset of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-corrupted samples from a distribution is close to the true mean of this distribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.5</span></span><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(An improved version of Proposition 3.9 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>)<span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">With <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},\dots,X_{n}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},\dots,X_{n}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-corrupted samples from the distribution <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}\left[X\right]=\Sigma\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>⪯</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}\left[X\right]=\Sigma\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E\left[X\right]=\mu_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E\left[X\right]=\mu_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> be at least a sufficiently large constant <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\log(d)/\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\log(d)/\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, with probability at least <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=d\exp(-\Omega(n\varepsilon/d))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=d\exp(-\Omega(n\varepsilon/d))</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a set <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subseteq\left\{X_{1},\dots,X_{n}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subseteq\left\{X_{1},\dots,X_{n}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|S|=(1-2\varepsilon)n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|S|=(1-2\varepsilon)n</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex98"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{S}-\mu_{X}\right\|_{2}\leq O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{S}-\mu_{X}\right\|_{2}\leq O(\sqrt{\varepsilon}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{S}:=\frac{1}{|S|}\sum_{X_{i}\in S}X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{S}:=\frac{1}{|S|}\sum_{X_{i}\in S}X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">The advantage of Lemma <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2" title="B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a> over the standard confidence amplification.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To boost the success probability from constant to arbitrary <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, one way is to use a standard
confidence amplification argument.
Let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the event that there exists a stable set in the <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th independent trial,
which holds with probability at least <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define indicator variables <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}=\mathds{1}_{\left\{E_{i}\right\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}=\mathds{1}_{\left\{E_{i}\right\}}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. Bernoulli
random variables with <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[b_{i}]=p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[b_{i}]=p</annotation></semantics></math>. By Hoeffding’s inequality, the empirical average <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{k}\sum_{i=1}^{k}b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{k}\sum_{i=1}^{k}b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>
concentrates around its expectation <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex99"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[p-1/k\sum_{i=1}^{k}b_{i}\geq(p-1/2)\right]\leq\exp\left(-\frac{2k^{2}(p-1/2)^{2}}{k}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>k</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[p-1/k\sum_{i=1}^{k}b_{i}\geq(p-1/2)\right]\leq\exp\left(-\frac{2k^{2}(p-1/2)^{2}}{k}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">so that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex100"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[\sum_{i=1}^{k}b_{i}\leq\frac{k}{2}\right]\leq\exp(-2k(p-\frac{1}{2})^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[\sum_{i=1}^{k}b_{i}\leq\frac{k}{2}\right]\leq\exp(-2k(p-\frac{1}{2})^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Setting this probability to be at most <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq\frac{1}{2(p-\tfrac{1}{2})^{2}}\log(1/\delta)=\Omega(\log(1/\delta))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq\frac{1}{2(p-\tfrac{1}{2})^{2}}\log(1/\delta)=\Omega(\log(1/\delta)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Hence, by repeating the procedure <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=\Omega(\log(1/\delta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=\Omega(\log(1/\delta))</annotation></semantics></math> times and taking a majority vote, we can ensure that a stable subset exists with probability at least <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining this amplification with the per-trial sample requirement
<math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=\Theta\big(\frac{d}{\varepsilon}\log(\frac{d}{\delta})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=\Theta\big(\frac{d}{\varepsilon}\log(\frac{d}{\delta})\big)</annotation></semantics></math> yields the total sample complexity</p>
<table id="A2.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon}\log\left(\frac{d}{\delta}\right)\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon}\log\left(\frac{d}{\delta}\right)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">which guarantees that the estimator succeeds with overall confidence <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">On the other hand, our Lemma <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2" title="B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a> only requires</p>
<table id="A2.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex102"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d\exp(-\Omega(n\varepsilon/d))\leq\delta," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d\exp(-\Omega(n\varepsilon/d))\leq\delta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">which implies</p>
<table id="A2.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex103"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle N\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle N\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex103.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{d}{\varepsilon}\log\left(d/\delta\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{d}{\varepsilon}\log\left(d/\delta\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex104"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex104.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{d}{\varepsilon}\left(\log(d)+\log(1/\delta)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{d}{\varepsilon}\left(\log(d)+\log(1/\delta)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">number of samples which is better than the standard confidence amplification approach (Eq. (<a href="#A2.E16" title="Equation 16 ‣ The advantage of Lemma over the standard confidence amplification. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>)).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof overview.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To prove this lemma, we first establish three claims (Claims <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a>, <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a>, and <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a>), which we then combine to prove Lemma <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2" title="B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The high-level idea is to show that there exists a subset of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-corrupted samples whose empirical mean is close to the mean of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. Unfortunately, a sufficiently large subset <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> of samples from <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is generally not stable with respect to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, since the second condition of Lemma <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS1" title="B.2.1 Background ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.1</span></a> is not satisfied. Therefore, we cannot directly apply Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem B.3 (Theorem 2.11 in []). ‣ B.2.1 Background ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a> to conclude that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is close to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>. To address this issue, we construct a distribution <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> which, with high probability, differs from <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> on at most an <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> fraction of outputs (Claim <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a>), and whose mean <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{X^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{X^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is close to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> (Claim <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a>). Thus, we obtain a set <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> consisting of i.i.d. samples from <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Claim <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a>, we may view <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> as a set of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-corrupted samples from <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is stable with respect to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, then Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem B.3 (Theorem 2.11 in []). ‣ B.2.1 Background ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a> implies that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{S^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{S^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is close to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{X^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{X^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, by Claim <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a>, we conclude that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{S^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{S^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is close to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">It therefore suffices to verify that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is stable with respect to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is shown in our third claim (Claim <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a>), where we prove that the required stability condition holds with high probability:</p>
<ol id="A2.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\mu_{S^{\prime}}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}=O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\mu_{S^{\prime}}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}=O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math>, and</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}\left[S^{\prime}\right]\preceq O\left(\mathbb{I}_{d}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}\left[S^{\prime}\right]\preceq O\left(\mathbb{I}_{d}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">so that applying Lemma <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS1" title="B.2.1 Background ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.1</span></a>, we can validate this if condition.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now, we present the first claim: with probability at least <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\exp\left(-\frac{\varepsilon n}{4}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\exp\left(-\frac{\varepsilon n}{4}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, we can get <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i}\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{i}\neq X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}}\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>𝟙</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i}\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{i}\neq X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}}\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_claim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim B.6</span></span><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in\left(0,0.1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in\left(0,0.1\right)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the level of corruption and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be an arbitrary positive real number. For all <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, we let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be a random variable from the distribution <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with mean <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i}=\E\left[X_{i}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i}=\E\left[X_{i}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> and covariance <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}\left[X_{i}\right]\preceq\gamma\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}\left[X_{i}\right]\preceq\gamma\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We define the truncated random variable</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex105"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{i}^{\prime}=\begin{cases}X_{i},&amp;\left\|X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}\leq 2\sqrt{\gamma d/\varepsilon},\\
\mu_{i},&amp;\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">otherwise.</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{i}^{\prime}=\begin{cases}X_{i},&amp;\left\|X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}\leq 2\sqrt{\gamma d/\varepsilon},\\
\mu_{i},&amp;\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the distribution of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex106"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{i}\neq X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}}\geq\varepsilon\right]\leq\exp\left(-\frac{\varepsilon N}{4}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{i}\neq X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}}\geq\varepsilon\right]\leq\exp\left(-\frac{\varepsilon N}{4}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that since we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}\left[X_{i}\right]=\E\left[\left(X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right)\left(X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right)^{\top}\right]\preceq\gamma\mathbb{I}_{d}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}\left[X_{i}\right]=\E\left[\left(X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right)\left(X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right)^{\top}\right]\preceq\gamma\mathbb{I}_{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">we can get</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex107"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\E\left[\left\|X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\E\left[\left\|X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex107.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\E\left[\left\langle X_{i}-\mu_{i},X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right\rangle\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\E\left[\left\langle X_{i}-\mu_{i},X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right\rangle\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex108"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex108.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\mathrm{tr}\left[\E\left[\left(X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right)\left(X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right)^{\top}\right]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\mathrm{tr}\left[\E\left[\left(X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right)\left(X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right)^{\top}\right]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex109"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex109.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\mathrm{tr}\left[\gamma\mathbb{I}_{d}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\mathrm{tr}\left[\gamma\mathbb{I}_{d}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\gamma d," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\gamma d,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from the definition of the <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm, the second step follows from <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\left(X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right)\left(X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right)^{\top}\right)_{i,i}=\left(X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right)_{i}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\left(X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right)\left(X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right)^{\top}\right)_{i,i}=\left(X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right)_{i}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the third step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A2.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ Proof. ‣ Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>).
Therefore, we can see that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex110"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[X_{i}^{\prime}\neq X_{i}\right]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[X_{i}^{\prime}\neq X_{i}\right]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex110.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~\Pr\left[\left\|X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}^{2}&gt;4\frac{\gamma d}{\varepsilon}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>4</mn><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\Pr\left[\left\|X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}^{2}&gt;4\frac{\gamma d}{\varepsilon}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex111"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex111.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{\E\left[\left\|X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]}{4\gamma d/\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{\E\left[\left\|X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]}{4\gamma d/\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex112"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex112.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{\varepsilon}{4}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{\varepsilon}{4},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from the definition of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, the second step follows from the Markov inequality (see Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem10" title="Fact A.10 (Markov’s Inequality). ‣ A.3 Probabilistic and Algebraic Tools ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.10</span></a>), and the third step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A2.Ex107" title="In Proof. ‣ Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>).
Now, we consider drawing <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> numbers of i.i.d. samples from <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. We note that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex113"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{i}\neq X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathds{1}_{\left\{\left\|X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}^{2}&gt;4\gamma d/\varepsilon\right\}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mn>𝟙</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mn>𝟙</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mo>‖</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{i}\neq X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathds{1}_{\left\{\left\|X_{i}-\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}^{2}&gt;4\gamma d/\varepsilon\right\}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p6.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p6.5.1" class="ltx_text">These <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p6.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{i}\neq X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{i}\neq X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. Bernoulli with <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p6.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\E\left[\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{i}\neq X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}}\right]\leq\frac{\varepsilon}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E\left[\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{i}\neq X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}}\right]\leq\frac{\varepsilon}{4}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\E\left[\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{i}\neq X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}}\right]=Np\leq\frac{\varepsilon}{4}N." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Np</mi><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\E\left[\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{i}\neq X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}}\right]=Np\leq\frac{\varepsilon}{4}N.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the multiplicative Chernoff bound (see Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem11" title="Fact A.11 (Multiplicative Chernoff Bound). ‣ A.3 Probabilistic and Algebraic Tools ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.11</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex114"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{i}\neq X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}}\geq\varepsilon\right]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{i}\neq X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}}\geq\varepsilon\right]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex114.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~\Pr\left[\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{i}\neq X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}}\geq N\varepsilon\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>N</mi><mi>ε</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\Pr\left[\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{i}\neq X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}}\geq N\varepsilon\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex115"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex115.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~\Pr\left[\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{i}\neq X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}}\geq\left(1+3\right)\E\left[\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{i}\neq X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}}\right]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\Pr\left[\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{i}\neq X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}}\geq\left(1+3\right)\E\left[\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{i}\neq X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}}\right]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex116"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex116.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\exp\left(-\frac{\varepsilon N}{4}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\exp\left(-\frac{\varepsilon N}{4}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A2.E19" title="Equation 19 ‣ Proof. ‣ Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Now, we present our second claim: the mean of the distribution <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is close to that of the distribution <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_claim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim B.7</span></span><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i^{\prime}}:=\E\left[X_{i}^{\prime}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i^{\prime}}:=\E\left[X_{i}^{\prime}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i}=\E\left[X_{i}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i}=\E\left[X_{i}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex117"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}\leq O\left(\sqrt{\gamma\varepsilon}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}\leq O\left(\sqrt{\gamma\varepsilon}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first define</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F:=\left\{x\mid X_{i}=X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F:=\left\{x\mid X_{i}=X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can get</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex118"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}^{4}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}^{4}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex118.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\langle\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i},\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i}\right\rangle^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\langle\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i},\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i}\right\rangle^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex119"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex119.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex119.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\langle\E\left[X_{i}^{\prime}-X_{i}\right],\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i}\right\rangle^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\langle\E\left[X_{i}^{\prime}-X_{i}\right],\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i}\right\rangle^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex120"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex120.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex120.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\langle\E\left[\left(X_{i}^{\prime}-X_{i}\right)\left(\mathds{1}_{\left\{F\right\}}+\mathds{1}_{\left\{\overline{F}\right\}}\right)\right],\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i}\right\rangle^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\langle\E\left[\left(X_{i}^{\prime}-X_{i}\right)\left(\mathds{1}_{\left\{F\right\}}+\mathds{1}_{\left\{\overline{F}\right\}}\right)\right],\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i}\right\rangle^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex121"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex121.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex121.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\langle\E\left[\left(X_{i}^{\prime}-X_{i}\right)\mathds{1}_{\left\{\overline{F}\right\}}\right],\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i}\right\rangle^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\langle\E\left[\left(X_{i}^{\prime}-X_{i}\right)\mathds{1}_{\left\{\overline{F}\right\}}\right],\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i}\right\rangle^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex122"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex122.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\E\left[\mathds{1}_{\left\{\overline{F}\right\}}\left\langle\left(X_{i}^{\prime}-X_{i}\right),\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i}\right\rangle^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\E\left[\mathds{1}_{\left\{\overline{F}\right\}}\left\langle\left(X_{i}^{\prime}-X_{i}\right),\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i}\right\rangle^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E21.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~\varepsilon\E\left[\left\langle\left(X_{i}^{\prime}-X_{i}\right),\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i}\right\rangle^{2}\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\varepsilon\E\left[\left\langle\left(X_{i}^{\prime}-X_{i}\right),\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i}\right\rangle^{2}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second step follows from the definitions of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the third step follows from the definition of the indicator function, the fourth step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A2.E20" title="Equation 20 ‣ Proof. ‣ Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>), the fifth step follows from the linearity property, and the last step follows from the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality.
Defining <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b:=\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b:=\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex123"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\langle X_{i}^{\prime}-X_{i},b\right\rangle^{2}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\langle X_{i}^{\prime}-X_{i},b\right\rangle^{2}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex123.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\langle X_{i}^{\prime}-X_{i}-b+b,b\right\rangle^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\langle X_{i}^{\prime}-X_{i}-b+b,b\right\rangle^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex124"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex124.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\langle X_{i}^{\prime}-X_{i}-\mu_{i^{\prime}}+\mu_{i}+b,b\right\rangle^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\langle X_{i}^{\prime}-X_{i}-\mu_{i^{\prime}}+\mu_{i}+b,b\right\rangle^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex125"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex125.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left(\left\langle X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{i^{\prime}},b\right\rangle-\left\langle X_{i}-\mu_{i},b\right\rangle+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left(\left\langle X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{i^{\prime}},b\right\rangle-\left\langle X_{i}-\mu_{i},b\right\rangle+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex126"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex126.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~3\left(\left\langle X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{i^{\prime}},b\right\rangle^{2}+\left\langle X_{i}-\mu_{i},b\right\rangle^{2}+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~3\left(\left\langle X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{i^{\prime}},b\right\rangle^{2}+\left\langle X_{i}-\mu_{i},b\right\rangle^{2}+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex127"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex127.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~3\left(b^{\top}\mathrm{Cov}\left[X_{i}^{\prime}\right]b+b^{\top}\mathrm{Cov}\left[X_{i}\right]b+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~3\left(b^{\top}\mathrm{Cov}\left[X_{i}^{\prime}\right]b+b^{\top}\mathrm{Cov}\left[X_{i}\right]b+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~3\gamma\left(2\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~3\gamma\left(2\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{4}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the third step follows from the linearity property of the inner product, the fourth step follows from Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem5" title="Fact A.5. ‣ A.1 Sum-of-squares ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>, the fifth step follows from the definition of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}\left[\cdot\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}\left[\cdot\right]</annotation></semantics></math>, and the last step follows from <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}\left[X_{i}^{\prime}\right]\preceq\mathrm{Cov}\left[X_{i}\right]\preceq\gamma\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}\left[X_{i}^{\prime}\right]\preceq\mathrm{Cov}\left[X_{i}\right]\preceq\gamma\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Combining Eq. (<a href="#A2.Ex118" title="In Proof. ‣ Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A2.Ex123" title="In Proof. ‣ Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) together, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex128"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex128.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{4}\leq 3\gamma\varepsilon\left(2\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{4}\leq 3\gamma\varepsilon\left(2\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{4}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p11.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p11.4.1" class="ltx_text">which implies</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex129"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}^{2}\leq O\left(\gamma\varepsilon\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}^{2}\leq O\left(\gamma\varepsilon\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p11.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p11.5.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Now, we present our third claim: the set of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> i.i.d. samples from the distribution <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is stable.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_claim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim B.8</span></span><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We define <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}:=\left\{X_{1}^{\prime},X_{2}^{\prime},\dots,X_{n}^{\prime}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}:=\left\{X_{1}^{\prime},X_{2}^{\prime},\dots,X_{n}^{\prime}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> to be a set of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> i.i.d. samples from the distribution <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We define <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{S^{\prime}}:=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i\in S^{\prime}}X_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{S^{\prime}}:=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i\in S^{\prime}}X_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{X^{\prime}}:=\E\left[X^{\prime}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{X^{\prime}}:=\E\left[X^{\prime}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> be the true mean of the distribution <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}\left[X\right]=\Sigma\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>⪯</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}\left[X\right]=\Sigma\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in\left(0,1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in\left(0,1\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, we can get that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\varepsilon,O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\varepsilon,O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-stable with respect to the distribution <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability at least <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-d\exp(-\Omega(n\varepsilon/d))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-d\exp(-\Omega(n\varepsilon/d))</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">To show that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varepsilon,O(\sqrt{\varepsilon}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varepsilon,O(\sqrt{\varepsilon}))</annotation></semantics></math>-stable with respect to the distribution <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> with probability at least <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-d\exp(-\Omega(n\varepsilon/d))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-d\exp(-\Omega(n\varepsilon/d))</annotation></semantics></math>, by Lemma <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS1" title="B.2.1 Background ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.1</span></a>, we need to show that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[\left\|\mu_{S^{\prime}}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}=O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})\right]\geq 1-\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{n\varepsilon}{d}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[\left\|\mu_{S^{\prime}}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}=O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})\right]\geq 1-\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{n\varepsilon}{d}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx63" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[\mathrm{Cov}\left[S^{\prime}\right]\preceq O(\mathbb{I}_{d})\right]\geq 1-d\exp(-\Omega(n\varepsilon/d))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[\mathrm{Cov}\left[S^{\prime}\right]\preceq O(\mathbb{I}_{d})\right]\geq 1-d\exp(-\Omega(n\varepsilon/d))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Eq. (<a href="#A2.E23" title="Equation 23 ‣ Proof. ‣ Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>).<span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p16.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">We define <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{i}:=\frac{1}{n}\left(X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{i}:=\frac{1}{n}\left(X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">To show Eq. (<a href="#A2.E23" title="Equation 23 ‣ Proof. ‣ Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>), we first note that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex130"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex130.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}\left[X^{\prime}\right]\preceq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}\left[X^{\prime}\right]\preceq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex130.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\E\left[(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X})(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X})^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\E\left[(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X})(X^{\prime}-\mu_{X})^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex131"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\preceq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⪯</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\preceq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex131.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\E\left[(X-\mu_{X})(X-\mu_{X})^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\E\left[(X-\mu_{X})(X-\mu_{X})^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex132"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex132.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\mathrm{Cov}\left[X\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\mathrm{Cov}\left[X\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\preceq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⪯</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\preceq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\mathbb{I}_{d}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\mathbb{I}_{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p18.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p18.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem12" title="Fact A.12. ‣ A.3 Probabilistic and Algebraic Tools ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.12</span></a>, the second step follows from the definition of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Claim <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a>), the third step follows from the definition of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}\left[\cdot\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}\left[\cdot\right]</annotation></semantics></math>, and the last step follows from the claim statement <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}\left[X\right]=\Sigma\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>⪯</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}\left[X\right]=\Sigma\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex133"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{S^{\prime}}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{S^{\prime}}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex133.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex134"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex134.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex134.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\frac{1}{n}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left(X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\right)\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\frac{1}{n}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left(X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\right)\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex135"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex135.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex135.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\sum_{i=1}^{n}Y_{i}\right\|_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\sum_{i=1}^{n}Y_{i}\right\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">As in the definition of the Vector Bernstein inequality (see Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem14" title="Fact A.14 (Vector Bernstein inequality, Theorem 12 in []). ‣ A.3 Probabilistic and Algebraic Tools ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.14</span></a>), we also need</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex136"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex136.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex136.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{i=1}^{n}\E\left[\left\|Y_{i}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{i=1}^{n}\E\left[\left\|Y_{i}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex137"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex137.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex137.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sum_{i=1}^{n}\E\left[\left\|\frac{1}{n}\left(X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sum_{i=1}^{n}\E\left[\left\|\frac{1}{n}\left(X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex138"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex138.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex138.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n^{2}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\E\left[\left\|X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n^{2}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\E\left[\left\|X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex139"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex139.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex139.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\E\left[\left\|X^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\E\left[\left\|X^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{d}{n}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{d}{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p20.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p20.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from the definition of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> (see Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem14" title="Fact A.14 (Vector Bernstein inequality, Theorem 12 in []). ‣ A.3 Probabilistic and Algebraic Tools ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.14</span></a>), the second step follows from the definition of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the third step follows from the linearity of expectation, and the last step follows from <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}\left[X^{\prime}\right]\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}\left[X^{\prime}\right]\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. (<a href="#A2.Ex130" title="In Proof. ‣ Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>)).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">Additionally, using Claim <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a> and the definition of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> from Claim <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a>, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx67" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex140"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex140.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{i\in[n]}\left\|Y_{i}\right\|_{2}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{i\in[n]}\left\|Y_{i}\right\|_{2}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex140.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\max_{i\in[n]}\left\|\frac{1}{n}\left(X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\max_{i\in[n]}\left\|\frac{1}{n}\left(X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex141"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex141.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex141.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\max_{i\in[n]}\left\|X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\max_{i\in[n]}\left\|X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex142"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex142.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex142.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\max_{i\in[n]}\left\|X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{X}+\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\max_{i\in[n]}\left\|X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{X}+\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex143"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex143.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex143.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\max_{i\in[n]}\left(\left\|X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right\|_{2}+\left\|\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\max_{i\in[n]}\left(\left\|X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right\|_{2}+\left\|\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex144"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex144.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex144.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\left(2\sqrt{\frac{d}{\varepsilon}}+O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon}\right)\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\left(2\sqrt{\frac{d}{\varepsilon}}+O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon}\right)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p21.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p21.2.1" class="ltx_text">which implies</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx68" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{i\in[n]}\left\|Y_{i}\right\|_{2}=O\left(\frac{\sqrt{d}}{n\sqrt{\varepsilon}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{i\in[n]}\left\|Y_{i}\right\|_{2}=O\left(\frac{\sqrt{d}}{n\sqrt{\varepsilon}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the Vector Bernstein inequality (see Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem14" title="Fact A.14 (Vector Bernstein inequality, Theorem 12 in []). ‣ A.3 Probabilistic and Algebraic Tools ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.14</span></a>), for all <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=\left\|\sum_{i=1}^{n}Y_{i}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=\left\|\sum_{i=1}^{n}Y_{i}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\leq d/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\leq d/n</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p22.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq V/\max\left\|Y_{i}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq V/\max\left\|Y_{i}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx69" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex145"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex145.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[N\geq\sqrt{V}+t\right]\leq\exp\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{4V}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><msqrt><mi>V</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[N\geq\sqrt{V}+t\right]\leq\exp\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{4V}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Eq. (<a href="#A2.Ex136" title="In Proof. ‣ Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A2.E27" title="Equation 27 ‣ Proof. ‣ Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>), we can get</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx70" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex146"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex146.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle t\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle t\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex146.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~V/\max\left\|Y_{i}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~V/\max\left\|Y_{i}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex147"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex147.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex147.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{d/n}{O\left(\frac{\sqrt{d}}{n\sqrt{\varepsilon}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{d/n}{O\left(\frac{\sqrt{d}}{n\sqrt{\varepsilon}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex148"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex148.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex148.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~o\left(\sqrt{d\varepsilon}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~o\left(\sqrt{d\varepsilon}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p24" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text">We further note that if <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=\Omega\left(d/\varepsilon\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=\Omega\left(d/\varepsilon\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx71" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex149"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex149.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{V}\leq\sqrt{d/n}=O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>V</mi></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{V}\leq\sqrt{d/n}=O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p25" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p25.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p25.1.1" class="ltx_text">We choose <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t:=O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon}\right)&lt;o\left(\sqrt{d\varepsilon}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t:=O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon}\right)&lt;o\left(\sqrt{d\varepsilon}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p26" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p26.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p26.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx72" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex150"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex150.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[\left\|\mu_{S^{\prime}}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}\geq O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon}\right)\right]\leq\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{d/n}\right)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[\left\|\mu_{S^{\prime}}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}\geq O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon}\right)\right]\leq\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{d/n}\right)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p27" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p27.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p27.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Eq. (<a href="#A2.E24" title="Equation 24 ‣ Proof. ‣ Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>).<span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p27.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p28" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p28.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p28.1.1" class="ltx_text">We define</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx73" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overline{X}_{k}:=\frac{1}{n}(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}})(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}})^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overline{X}_{k}:=\frac{1}{n}(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}})(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}})^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p29" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p29.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p29.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first analyze <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx74" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex151"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex151.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex151.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X}+\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X}+\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex152"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex152.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex152.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right\|_{2}+\left\|\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X}\right\|_{2}+\left\|\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex153"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex153.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex153.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\frac{d}{\varepsilon}}\right)+\left\|\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\frac{d}{\varepsilon}}\right)+\left\|\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\frac{d}{\varepsilon}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\frac{d}{\varepsilon}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p29.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p29.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second step follows from the triangle inequality, the third step follows from the definition of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Claim <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a>), and the last step follows from <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p29.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}\leq O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\mu_{X}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}\leq O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> (see Claim <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p30" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p30.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p30.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx75" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex154"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex154.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{k\in[n]}\left\|\overline{X}_{k}\right\|=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{k\in[n]}\left\|\overline{X}_{k}\right\|=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex154.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\max_{k\in[n]}\left\|\frac{1}{n}(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}})(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}})^{\top}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\max_{k\in[n]}\left\|\frac{1}{n}(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}})(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}})^{\top}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex155"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex155.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex155.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\max_{k\in[n]}\left\|(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}})(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}})^{\top}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\max_{k\in[n]}\left\|(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}})(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}})^{\top}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex156"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex156.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex156.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\max_{k\in[n]}\left\|X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\max_{k\in[n]}\left\|X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex157"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex157.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex157.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon n}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon n}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p30.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p30.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A2.E28" title="Equation 28 ‣ Proof. ‣ Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>), the third step follows from Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem13" title="Fact A.13. ‣ A.3 Probabilistic and Algebraic Tools ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.13</span></a>, and the last step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A2.Ex151" title="In Proof. ‣ Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p31" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p31.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p31.1.1" class="ltx_text">This implies that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=O\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=O\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> with</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx76" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex158"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex158.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{0}_{d\times d}\preceq\overline{X}_{k}\preceq R\cdot\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⪯</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{0}_{d\times d}\preceq\overline{X}_{k}\preceq R\cdot\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p32" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p32.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p32.1.1" class="ltx_text">Additionally, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx77" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex159"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex159.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\E\left[\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\E\left[\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex159.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\E\left[\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\E\left[\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex160"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex160.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex160.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\mathrm{Cov}\left[X^{\prime}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\mathrm{Cov}\left[X^{\prime}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex161"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex161.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\preceq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⪯</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\preceq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex161.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\mathbb{I}_{d}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\mathbb{I}_{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p32.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p32.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from the linearity, the second step follows from the fact that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{k}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{k}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>s are i.i.d. samples from <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the third step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A2.Ex130" title="In Proof. ‣ Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p33" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p33.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p33.1.1" class="ltx_text">This implies the largest eigenvalue of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E\left[\sum_{k=1}^{n}\overline{X}_{k}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E\left[\sum_{k=1}^{n}\overline{X}_{k}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\max}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\max}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p34" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p34.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p34.1.1" class="ltx_text">Choosing <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=2/\mu_{\max}\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=2/\mu_{\max}\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> and including these into the matrix Chernoff inequality (Fact <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem5" title="Fact C.5 (Matrix Chernoff Inequality, Theorem 3.12 from []). ‣ C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a>), we can get</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx78" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex162"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex162.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[\left\lVert\sum_{k}\overline{X}_{k}\right\rVert_{2}&gt;(1+\Delta)\mu_{\max}\right]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[\left\lVert\sum_{k}\overline{X}_{k}\right\rVert_{2}&gt;(1+\Delta)\mu_{\max}\right]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex162.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~\Pr\left[\left\|\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{2}&gt;2+\mu_{\max}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\Pr\left[\left\|\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{2}&gt;2+\mu_{\max}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex163"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex163.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex163.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~d\left(\frac{e^{\Delta}}{(1+\Delta)^{1+\Delta}}\right)^{\mu_{\max}/R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~d\left(\frac{e^{\Delta}}{(1+\Delta)^{1+\Delta}}\right)^{\mu_{\max}/R}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex164"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex164.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex164.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~d(e/(1+\Delta))^{\Delta\mu_{\max}/R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~d(e/(1+\Delta))^{\Delta\mu_{\max}/R}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~d\exp(-\Omega(n\varepsilon/d))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~d\exp(-\Omega(n\varepsilon/d)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p34.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p34.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the third step follows from <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\max}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\max}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p34.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=O\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=O\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p35" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p35.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p35.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, we can get that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx79" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex165"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex165.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}\left[S\right]\preceq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}\left[S\right]\preceq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex165.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex166"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex166.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\preceq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⪯</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\preceq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex166.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left(2+\mu_{\max}\right)\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left(2+\mu_{\max}\right)\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex167"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex167.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\preceq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⪯</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\preceq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex167.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~3\mathbb{I}_{d}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~3\mathbb{I}_{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p35.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p35.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A2.Ex162" title="In Proof. ‣ Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>) and the last step follows from <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\max}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\max}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p36" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p36.1" class="ltx_p">Combining Claim <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a>, <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a>, <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a>, we can prove Lemma <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2" title="B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2" title="B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p37" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p37.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p37.1.1" class="ltx_text">As <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\varepsilon,O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\varepsilon,O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>-stable with respect to the distribution <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p37.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (Claim <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a>), we can get for all <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p37.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\subseteq S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\subseteq S</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p37.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|T|\geq\left(1-2\varepsilon\right)n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|T|\geq\left(1-2\varepsilon\right)n</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx80" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{T}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}\leq O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{T}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}\leq O(\sqrt{\varepsilon}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p38" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p38.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p38.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Claim <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a>, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx81" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{X^{\prime}}-\mu_{X}\right\|_{2}\leq O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{X^{\prime}}-\mu_{X}\right\|_{2}\leq O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p39" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p39.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p39.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining Eq. (<a href="#A2.E31" title="Equation 31 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A2.E32" title="Equation 32 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>), we can get</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx82" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex168"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex168.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{T}-\mu_{X}\right\|_{2}\leq O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{T}-\mu_{X}\right\|_{2}\leq O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p39.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p39.2.1" class="ltx_text">by the triangle inequality.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p40" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p40.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p40.1.1" class="ltx_text">Regarding the failure probability <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, in our proof, we have used the probabilistic statement in three places:</span></p>
<ul id="A2.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i}\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{i}\neq X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}}\geq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>𝟙</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i}\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{i}\neq X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}}\geq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> holds with probability at least <math id="A2.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\exp\left(-\frac{\varepsilon n}{4}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\exp\left(-\frac{\varepsilon n}{4}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> (Claim <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a>),</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\mu_{S^{\prime}}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}\leq O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\mu_{S^{\prime}}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}\leq O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> holds with probability at least <math id="A2.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\exp(-\Omega(n\varepsilon/d))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\exp(-\Omega(n\varepsilon/d))</annotation></semantics></math>, and</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I5.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}\left[S^{\prime}\right]\preceq O(\mathbb{I}_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}\left[S^{\prime}\right]\preceq O(\mathbb{I}_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> with probability at least <math id="A2.I5.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-d\exp(-\Omega(n\varepsilon/d))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-d\exp(-\Omega(n\varepsilon/d))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p40.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p40.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using the union bound to combine these failure probabilities together, we can get <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\mu_{T}-\mu_{X}\right\|_{2}\leq O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\mu_{T}-\mu_{X}\right\|_{2}\leq O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> with probability at least <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p40.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, where
<math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2.p40.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=d\exp(-\Omega(n\varepsilon/d))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=d\exp(-\Omega(n\varepsilon/d))</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, our goal is to analyze Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Problem 1.1 (Mean shift). ‣ Mean Shift Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>, where an <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of users may be adversarially contaminated, and the <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> distance between each user’s mean <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and the true mean <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Specifically, in <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Main Result ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, we restate the problem setting of Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Problem 1.1 (Mean shift). ‣ Mean Shift Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a> and present our upper-bound result. In <a href="#A3.SS2" title="C.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>, we formally define the polynomial system <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖠</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and describe our SoS-based algorithmic framework for achieving this upper bound; we also provide an informal proof sketch explaining why this design attains the optimal error rate. In <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>, we establish the satisfiability of the polynomial system, namely the existence of a feasible solution with high probability. Finally, in <a href="#A3.SS4" title="C.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>, we give a formal proof of correctness and derive the sample-complexity guarantee for our main result.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Main Result</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now, we restate the formal problem setup for learning from corrupted batches with bounded user means.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Problem 1.1 (Mean shift). ‣ Mean Shift Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Our main result of this section, which constitutes the upper-bound part of our main theorem (Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1 (Mean shift). ‣ 2 Main Results ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>), is as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Upper bound result of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1 (Mean shift). ‣ 2 Main Results ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in\left(0,0.1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in\left(0,0.1\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\left(0,0.1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\left(0,0.1\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=o(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=o(d)</annotation></semantics></math> samples from each of <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> users with at least <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="nN\geq\min\left\{\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon/n}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right),\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">nN\geq\min\left\{\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon/n}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right),\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> total samples,
there exists a polynomial-time algorithm (Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Algorithm ideas. ‣ 4.2 Leveraging Per-User Structure (Problem ). ‣ 4 Technical Overview ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) solving Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Problem 1.1 (Mean shift). ‣ Mean Shift Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a> that outputs <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and satisfies
<math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\mu-\widehat{\mu}\right\|_{2}=O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\mu-\widehat{\mu}\right\|_{2}=O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>,
with probability at least <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof of this theorem follows from the satisfiability (Lemma <a href="#A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ C.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>) and identifiability (Lemma <a href="#A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ C.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We give a detailed proof for the satisfiability (Lemma <a href="#A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ C.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>) and identifiability (Lemma <a href="#A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ C.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>) in <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a> and <a href="#A3.SS4" title="C.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>, respectively. The goal of this section is to state these lemmas, present a high level proof overview for them, and explain how we can design our algorithm (Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Algorithm ideas. ‣ 4.2 Leveraging Per-User Structure (Problem ). ‣ 4 Technical Overview ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) stated in the theorem.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Algorithmic design.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our polynomial time SoS algorithm (Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Algorithm ideas. ‣ 4.2 Leveraging Per-User Structure (Problem ). ‣ 4 Technical Overview ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) is based on the polynomial system <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖠</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is defined as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition C.2</span></span><span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Polynomial system <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖠</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{x_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{N}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{x_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{N}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of empirical means of each user, each of which is computed via averaging <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples. Let <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{z_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{N}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{z_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{N}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> set of pure empirical means of each user.
Let <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{Z_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{N}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{Z_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{N}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the variables representing the empirical means of (imaginary) uncorrupted <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{z_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{z_{i}\right\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be a matrix of “slack” variables.
For all <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, we let <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Given <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in\left(0,0.1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in\left(0,0.1\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\left(0,0.1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\left(0,0.1\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples from each of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> users, we define the polynomial system <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖠</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> with the following constraints:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx83" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex169"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex169.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varepsilon^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varepsilon^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex169.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\min\left\{\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\},\frac{1}{10}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min\left\{\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\},\frac{1}{10}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex170"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex170.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overline{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overline{Z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex170.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}Z_{i}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}Z_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex171"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex171.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{i}\left(Z_{i}-x_{i}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{i}\left(Z_{i}-x_{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex171.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex172"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex172.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{i}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{i}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex172.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=W_{i}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=W_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex173"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex173.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{N}W_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{N}W_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex173.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(1-\varepsilon^{\prime}\right)N," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(1-\varepsilon^{\prime}\right)N,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex174"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex174.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(Z_{i}-\overline{Z}\right)\left(Z_{i}-\overline{Z}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(Z_{i}-\overline{Z}\right)\left(Z_{i}-\overline{Z}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex174.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\left(\frac{1}{n}+\alpha\right)\mathbb{I}_{d}-BB^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\left(\frac{1}{n}+\alpha\right)\mathbb{I}_{d}-BB^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We first compute the empirical mean of each user as <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since each user provides only <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=o(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=o(d)</annotation></semantics></math> samples, we cannot rely on any single user’s data to estimate the true mean. Our goal is to find a subset with empirical covariance bounded by <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\frac{1}{n}+\alpha\right)\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\frac{1}{n}+\alpha\right)\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The intuition is that the empirical mean of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples from a distribution with covariance bounded by <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> has its covariance shrunk by a factor of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/n</annotation></semantics></math>, while the mean deviation <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\mu_{i}-\mu\right\|_{2}\leq\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\mu_{i}-\mu\right\|_{2}\leq\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> of each good user contributes at most an additional <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, if we can select the subset of users that collectively satisfies this bounded covariance condition, the empirical mean over this subset will closely approximate the true mean <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>. Finding such a subset exactly is computationally intractable; therefore, we design a SoS relaxation that enforces these covariance constraints over pseudo-expectations, yielding a polynomial-time algorithm that provably achieves the same statistical guarantee.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof overview.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proof proceeds in two main steps: <em id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">satisfiability</em> and <em id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">identifiability</em>.
We say a polynomial system (the set of SoS constraints) is satisfiable if it actually has a feasible solution. When the fraction of corrupted users and samples obeys the bounds <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, and the good users’ distributions satisfy the bounded-covariance.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In the first step, we show that the polynomial system is satisfiable with high probability. Intuitively, when all users are uncorrupted, setting <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> for the good users and letting <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> be the variable representing the empirical mean of user <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, it yields a valid solution that satisfies the bounded covariance condition</p>
<table id="A3.EGx84" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(Z_{i}-\mu\right)\left(Z_{i}-\mu\right)^{\top}\preceq 2\left(\frac{1}{n}+\alpha\right)\mathbb{I}_{d}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(Z_{i}-\mu\right)\left(Z_{i}-\mu\right)^{\top}\preceq 2\left(\frac{1}{n}+\alpha\right)\mathbb{I}_{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This holds because the empirical mean of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> i.i.d. samples has covariance bounded by <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the user-level deviation <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mu_{i}-\mu\|_{2}\leq\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mu_{i}-\mu\|_{2}\leq\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> adds at most <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> to the covariance. Therefore, the SoS constraints are feasible with high probability when instantiated on clean data.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.3</span></span><span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Satisfiability of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖠</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">With probability at least <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> clean empirical means <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{Z_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{Z_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy the bounded covariance condition (Eq. (<a href="#A3.E33" title="Equation 33 ‣ Proof overview. ‣ C.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>)) as long as</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx85" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex175"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex175.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle nN\geq\min\left\{\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon/n}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right),\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle nN\geq\min\left\{\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon/n}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right),\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The proof of Lemma <a href="#A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ C.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> is presented in <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>.
In the second step, we establish <em id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">identifiability</em>: if a pseudoexpectation <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\E}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies all the SoS constraints, then the mean estimate <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}=\widetilde{\E}[\overline{Z}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0.1389em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}=\widetilde{\E}[\overline{Z}]</annotation></semantics></math> must be close to the true mean <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>. The SoS proof guarantees that any feasible solution must have bounded covariance, and hence its pseudoexpectation cannot deviate significantly from <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.4</span></span><span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Identifiability of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖠</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\E}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the SoS constraints <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖠</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, then with probability at least <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a polynomial-time algorithm (Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Algorithm ideas. ‣ 4.2 Leveraging Per-User Structure (Problem ). ‣ 4 Technical Overview ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) solving Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Problem 1.1 (Mean shift). ‣ Mean Shift Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a> that outputs <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and satisfies
<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\mu-\widehat{\mu}\right\|_{2}=O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\mu-\widehat{\mu}\right\|_{2}=O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The proof of Lemma <a href="#A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ C.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> is presented in <a href="#A3.SS4" title="C.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>.
Combining the satisfiability and identifiability steps completes the proof of Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem C.1 (Upper bound result of Theorem ). ‣ C.1 Main Result ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, showing that our SoS-based algorithm finds a valid and accurate estimate of the true mean in polynomial time.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Satisfiability</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The goal of this section is to prove that the polynomial system defined in Definition <a href="#A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="Algorithmic design. ‣ C.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> is satisfiable with high probability. The key observation is that for each good user <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, since its mean <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> lies within <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> distance from the global mean <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A3.EGx86" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex176"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex176.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)^{\top}\right]\preceq\left(\frac{1}{n}+\alpha\right)\mathbb{I}_{d}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)^{\top}\right]\preceq\left(\frac{1}{n}+\alpha\right)\mathbb{I}_{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This is because of the following two reasons:</p>
<ol id="A3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the random variable representing the empirical mean of <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples from a distribution with covariance <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⪯</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}\left[z_{i}\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[\left(z_{i}-\mu_{i}\right)\left(z_{i}-\mu_{i}\right)^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}\left[z_{i}\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[\left(z_{i}-\mu_{i}\right)\left(z_{i}-\mu_{i}\right)^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>, and</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">since <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\mu-\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}^{2}\leq\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\mu-\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}^{2}\leq\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can get that <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\mu_{i}-\mu\right)\left(\mu_{i}-\mu\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\mu_{i}-\mu\right)\left(\mu_{i}-\mu\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is upper bounded by <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> as well.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To prove satisfiability, we need to show that the aggregated empirical covariance across users is bounded with high probability:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx87" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)^{\top}\preceq 2\left(\frac{1}{n}+\alpha\right)\mathbb{I}_{d}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)^{\top}\preceq 2\left(\frac{1}{n}+\alpha\right)\mathbb{I}_{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The main challenge is that the random vectors <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}-\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}-\mu</annotation></semantics></math> are unbounded, which prevents a direct application of standard concentration inequalities. To address this, we introduce a truncation step: each sample is clipped to a bounded region, producing truncated variables <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> that differ from <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> on at most an <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of users. We then apply the matrix Chernoff bound to the truncated variables to control their empirical covariance, and show that the truncation introduces only a small additional bias of order <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\varepsilon/n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\varepsilon/n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact C.5</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Matrix Chernoff Inequality, Theorem 3.12 from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\in\mathbb{Z}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\in\mathbb{Z}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be a sequence of independent random <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\times d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\times d</annotation></semantics></math> symmetric matrices with</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex177" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex177.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\preceq X_{k}\preceq R\cdot\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⪯</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\preceq X_{k}\preceq R\cdot\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">almost surely. Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\max}=\left\|\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{k}X_{k}\right]\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\max}=\left\|\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{k}X_{k}\right]\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, for any <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex178" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex178.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\left[\left\|\sum_{k}X_{k}\right\|_{2}&gt;(1+\Delta)\mu_{\max}\right]\leq d\left(\frac{e^{\Delta}}{(1+\Delta)^{1+\Delta}}\right)^{\mu_{\max}/R}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\left[\left\|\sum_{k}X_{k}\right\|_{2}&gt;(1+\Delta)\mu_{\max}\right]\leq d\left(\frac{e^{\Delta}}{(1+\Delta)^{1+\Delta}}\right)^{\mu_{\max}/R}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, we can view our samples as a <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-2\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-2\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> corrupted version of the truncated samples <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1}^{\prime},\ldots z_{n}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1}^{\prime},\ldots z_{n}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The mean would be shifted by an additional <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\varepsilon/n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\varepsilon/n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Also, the bounded covariance condition in Eq. (<a href="#A3.E34" title="Equation 34 ‣ C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>) holds with high probability, establishing the satisfiability of the SoS constraints.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_claim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.SS3.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim C.6</span></span><span id="A3.SS3.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all levels of corruption <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in\left(0,1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in\left(0,1\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, for all distributions <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}\left[X\right]=\Sigma\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>⪯</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}\left[X\right]=\Sigma\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E\left[X\right]=\mu_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E\left[X\right]=\mu_{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a distribution <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> defined as</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx88" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex179"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex179.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X^{\prime}:=\begin{cases}X&amp;\left\|X-\mu_{X}\right\|_{2}\leq 2\sqrt{\frac{d}{\varepsilon}}\\
\mu_{X}&amp;\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mi>X</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">otherwise.</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X^{\prime}:=\begin{cases}X&amp;\left\|X-\mu_{X}\right\|_{2}\leq 2\sqrt{\frac{d}{\varepsilon}}\\
\mu_{X}&amp;\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">such that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx89" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex180"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex180.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i}\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{i}\neq X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}}\geq\varepsilon\right]\leq\exp\left(-\frac{\varepsilon n}{4}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i}\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{i}\neq X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}}\geq\varepsilon\right]\leq\exp\left(-\frac{\varepsilon n}{4}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{X_{i}^{\prime}\right\}_{i=1}^{n}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> are the samples from <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">This directly follows from Claim <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a> by choosing <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">To proceed, we need to ensure that the truncation step—used to bound the covariance—does not alter the mean by too much. The following claim quantifies this effect, showing that the difference between the original and truncated means is small and scales as <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\left(\sqrt{\gamma\varepsilon}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\left(\sqrt{\gamma\varepsilon}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_claim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.SS3.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim C.7</span></span><span id="A3.SS3.4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{X^{\prime}}:=\E\left[X^{\prime}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{X^{\prime}}:=\E\left[X^{\prime}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{X}=\E\left[X\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{X}=\E\left[X\right]</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx90" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex181"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex181.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{X^{\prime}}-\mu_{X}\right\|_{2}\leq O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>X</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{X^{\prime}}-\mu_{X}\right\|_{2}\leq O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">This directly follows from Claim <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a> by choosing <math id="A3.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Having established in Claim <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a> that the means of the truncated and original variables are close, we now extend this result to show that the empirical covariance of the truncated variables remains well-behaved. The following claim applies the matrix Chernoff bound to demonstrate that the bounded covariance condition continues to hold with high probability.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_claim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.SS3.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim C.8</span></span><span id="A3.SS3.6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We define <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}:=\left\{X_{1}^{\prime},X_{2}^{\prime},\dots,X_{N}^{\prime}\right\}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}:=\left\{X_{1}^{\prime},X_{2}^{\prime},\dots,X_{N}^{\prime}\right\}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> to be a set of <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> independent truncated random variables, where <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}^{\prime}\sim\mathcal{D}_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}^{\prime}\sim\mathcal{D}_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are defined as in Claim <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>.
Let <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i}^{\prime}:=\E\left[X_{i}^{\prime}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i}^{\prime}:=\E\left[X_{i}^{\prime}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}\left[X_{i}^{\prime}\right]\preceq\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}\left[X_{i}^{\prime}\right]\preceq\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{n}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in\left(0,1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in\left(0,1\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assume that for all <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{i}^{\prime}\right\|_{2}&lt;2\sqrt{\frac{d}{n\varepsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{i}^{\prime}\right\|_{2}&lt;2\sqrt{\frac{d}{n\varepsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Claim <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a> with <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\frac{1}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\frac{1}{n}</annotation></semantics></math>). Then, for any failure probability <math id="A3.SS3.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in\left(0,0.1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in\left(0,0.1\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx91" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex182"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex182.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\left(X_{k}-\mu\right)\left(X_{k}-\mu\right)^{\top}\preceq 2\left(\frac{1}{n}+\alpha\right)\mathbb{I}_{d}\right]\geq 1-\delta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>⪯</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\left(X_{k}-\mu\right)\left(X_{k}-\mu\right)^{\top}\preceq 2\left(\frac{1}{n}+\alpha\right)\mathbb{I}_{d}\right]\geq 1-\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In addition,</span></p>
<ul id="A3.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">if </span><math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha n\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha n\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="A3.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\varepsilon N}{d}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\varepsilon N}{d}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">if </span><math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1&lt;\alpha n\leq\frac{d}{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1&lt;\alpha n\leq\frac{d}{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="A3.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\alpha n\varepsilon N}{d}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\alpha n\varepsilon N}{d}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">We define</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx92" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overline{X}_{k}:=\frac{1}{N}(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu)(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu)^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overline{X}_{k}:=\frac{1}{N}(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu)(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu)^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">By the definition of <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{k}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{k}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx93" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex183"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex183.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right\|_{2}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right\|_{2}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex183.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{k}^{\prime}+\mu_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{k}^{\prime}+\mu_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex184"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex184.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex184.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{k}^{\prime}\right\|_{2}+\left\|\mu_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{k}^{\prime}\right\|_{2}+\left\|\mu_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\frac{d}{n\varepsilon}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\frac{d}{n\varepsilon}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx94" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex185"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex185.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{k\in[N]}\left\|\overline{X}_{k}\right\|_{2}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{k\in[N]}\left\|\overline{X}_{k}\right\|_{2}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex185.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\max_{k\in[N]}\left\|\frac{1}{N}(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu)(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu)^{\top}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\max_{k\in[N]}\left\|\frac{1}{N}(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu)(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu)^{\top}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex186"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex186.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex186.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\max_{k\in[N]}\left\|(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu)(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu)^{\top}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\max_{k\in[N]}\left\|(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu)(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu)^{\top}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex187"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex187.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex187.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\max_{k\in[N]}\left\|X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\max_{k\in[N]}\left\|X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex188"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex188.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex188.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon nN}+\frac{\alpha}{N}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon nN}+\frac{\alpha}{N}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p11.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p11.4.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A3.E35" title="Equation 35 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>), the third step follows from Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem13" title="Fact A.13. ‣ A.3 Probabilistic and Algebraic Tools ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.13</span></a>, and the last step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A3.Ex183" title="In Proof. ‣ C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>).
This implies that <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=O\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon nN}+\frac{\alpha}{N}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=O\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon nN}+\frac{\alpha}{N}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> with</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx95" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex189"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex189.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{0}_{d\times d}\preceq\overline{X}_{k}\preceq R\cdot\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⪯</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{0}_{d\times d}\preceq\overline{X}_{k}\preceq R\cdot\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p11.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p11.5.1" class="ltx_text">Additionally, by Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem16" title="Fact A.16. ‣ A.3 Probabilistic and Algebraic Tools ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.16</span></a>, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx96" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex190"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex190.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}\left[X_{k}^{\prime}\right]\preceq\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{I}_{d}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}\left[X_{k}^{\prime}\right]\preceq\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{I}_{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p11.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p11.6.1" class="ltx_text">Also, since</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx97" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex191"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex191.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right\|_{2}^{2}&lt;\alpha," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right\|_{2}^{2}&lt;\alpha,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p11.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p11.7.1" class="ltx_text">we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx98" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex192"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex192.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\mu_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right)\left(\mu_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right)^{\top}\preceq\alpha\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\mu_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right)\left(\mu_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right)^{\top}\preceq\alpha\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p11.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p11.8.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx99" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex193"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex193.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\E\left[\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right)\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right)^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\E\left[\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right)\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right)^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex194"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex194.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex194.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\E\left[\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right)\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right)^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\E\left[\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right)\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right)^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex195"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex195.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex195.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\left(\E\left[\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{k}^{\prime}\right)\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{k}^{\prime}\right)^{\top}\right]+\E\left[\left(\mu_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right)\left(\mu_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right)^{\top}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\left(\E\left[\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{k}^{\prime}\right)\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu_{k}^{\prime}\right)^{\top}\right]+\E\left[\left(\mu_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right)\left(\mu_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right)^{\top}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex196"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex196.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex196.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\mathrm{Cov}\left[X_{k}^{\prime}\right]+\alpha\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\mathrm{Cov}\left[X_{k}^{\prime}\right]+\alpha\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex197"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex197.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\preceq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⪯</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\preceq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex197.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left(\frac{1}{n}+\alpha\right)\mathbb{I}_{d}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left(\frac{1}{n}+\alpha\right)\mathbb{I}_{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p11.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p11.9.1" class="ltx_text">This implies the largest eigenvalue of <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E\left[\sum_{k=1}^{n}\overline{X}_{k}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E\left[\sum_{k=1}^{n}\overline{X}_{k}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\max}\leq\frac{1}{n}+\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\max}\leq\frac{1}{n}+\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.
Choosing <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=1</annotation></semantics></math> and including these into the matrix Chernoff inequality (Fact <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem5" title="Fact C.5 (Matrix Chernoff Inequality, Theorem 3.12 from []). ‣ C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a>), we can get</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx100" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex198"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex198.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[\left\lVert\sum_{k}\overline{X}_{k}\right\rVert_{2}&gt;2\mu_{\max}\right]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[\left\lVert\sum_{k}\overline{X}_{k}\right\rVert_{2}&gt;2\mu_{\max}\right]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex198.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~\Pr\left[\left\|\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right)\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right)^{\top}\right\|_{2}&gt;2\mu_{\max}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\Pr\left[\left\|\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right)\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right)^{\top}\right\|_{2}&gt;2\mu_{\max}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex199"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex199.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex199.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~d\left(\frac{e}{4}\right)^{\mu_{\max}/R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>e</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~d\left(\frac{e}{4}\right)^{\mu_{\max}/R}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{N\left(1+\alpha n\right)}{\frac{d}{\varepsilon}+\alpha n}\right)\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{N\left(1+\alpha n\right)}{\frac{d}{\varepsilon}+\alpha n}\right)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p11.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p11.10.1" class="ltx_text">which follows from <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\max}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\max}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=O\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon nN}+\frac{\alpha}{N}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=O\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon nN}+\frac{\alpha}{N}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
In particular, in our setting, it is interesting to consider the situation when each user does not have sufficient sample to perform per-user mean estimation. Therefore, we consider <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=o(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=o(d)</annotation></semantics></math>, or <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha n\leq\frac{d}{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha n\leq\frac{d}{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, it suffices to consider two cases: <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha n\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha n\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1&lt;\alpha n\leq\frac{d}{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1&lt;\alpha n\leq\frac{d}{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 1 (<math id="A3.SS3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha n\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha n\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>).<span id="A3.SS3.p12.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose <math id="A3.SS3.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha n\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha n\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we can see that our failure probability in Eq. (<a href="#A3.Ex198" title="In Proof. ‣ C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>) is:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx101" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex200"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex200.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{N\left(1+\alpha n\right)}{\frac{d}{\varepsilon}+\alpha n}\right)\right)\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{N\left(1+\alpha n\right)}{\frac{d}{\varepsilon}+\alpha n}\right)\right)\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex200.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{N}{\frac{d}{\varepsilon}}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{N}{\frac{d}{\varepsilon}}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex201"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex201.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex201.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\varepsilon N}{d}\right)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\varepsilon N}{d}\right)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 2 (<math id="A3.SS3.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1&lt;\alpha n\leq\frac{d}{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1&lt;\alpha n\leq\frac{d}{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>).<span id="A3.SS3.p14.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose <math id="A3.SS3.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1&lt;\alpha n\leq\frac{d}{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1&lt;\alpha n\leq\frac{d}{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we can see that our failure probability<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
                  <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
                  
                  
                  
                  
                  
                  
                  
                At the point of applying this claim, We will set <math id="footnote2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="footnote2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> from Definition <a href="#A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="Algorithmic design. ‣ C.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>.</span></span></span> in Eq. (<a href="#A3.Ex198" title="In Proof. ‣ C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>) is:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx102" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex202"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex202.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{N\left(1+\alpha n\right)}{\frac{d}{\varepsilon}+\alpha n}\right)\right)\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{N\left(1+\alpha n\right)}{\frac{d}{\varepsilon}+\alpha n}\right)\right)\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex202.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\alpha nN}{\frac{d}{\varepsilon}}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\alpha nN}{\frac{d}{\varepsilon}}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex203"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex203.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex203.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\alpha\varepsilon nN}{d}\right)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\alpha\varepsilon nN}{d}\right)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, we can get that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx103" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex204"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex204.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\left(X_{k}-\mu\right)\left(X_{k}-\mu\right)^{\top}\preceq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\left(X_{k}-\mu\right)\left(X_{k}-\mu\right)^{\top}\preceq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex204.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right)\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right)\left(X_{k}^{\prime}-\mu\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex205"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex205.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\preceq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⪯</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\preceq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex205.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~2\mu_{\max}\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~2\mu_{\max}\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex206"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex206.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\preceq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⪯</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\preceq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex206.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~2\left(\frac{1}{n}+\alpha\right)\mathbb{I}_{d}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~2\left(\frac{1}{n}+\alpha\right)\mathbb{I}_{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">with probability <math id="A3.SS3.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS3.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&lt;d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\varepsilon N}{d}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&lt;d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\varepsilon N}{d}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A3.SS3.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&lt;d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\alpha\varepsilon nN}{d}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&lt;d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\alpha\varepsilon nN}{d}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, depending on which case applies.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_fact">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fact C.9</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},\dots,z_{N}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},\dots,z_{N}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> with empirical mean <math id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{z}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{z}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and fix any <math id="A3.Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx104" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex207"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex207.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(z_{i}-\overline{z}\right)\left(z_{i}-\overline{z}\right)^{\top}\preceq\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(z_{i}-\overline{z}\right)\left(z_{i}-\overline{z}\right)^{\top}\preceq\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.8" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">Our goal is to show that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx105" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex208"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex208.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(z_{i}-\overline{z}\right)\left(z_{i}-\overline{z}\right)^{\top}-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(z_{i}-\overline{z}\right)\left(z_{i}-\overline{z}\right)^{\top}-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p17.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p17.2.1" class="ltx_text">is positive semidefinite.
We have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx106" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex209"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex209.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(z_{i}-\overline{z})(z_{i}-\overline{z})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(z_{i}-\overline{z})(z_{i}-\overline{z})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex209.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(z_{i}-\mu)(z_{i}-\mu)^{\top}-(z_{i}-\mu)(\overline{z}-\mu)^{\top}-(\overline{z}-\mu)(z_{i}-\mu)^{\top}+(\overline{z}-\mu)(\overline{z}-\mu)^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(z_{i}-\mu)(z_{i}-\mu)^{\top}-(z_{i}-\mu)(\overline{z}-\mu)^{\top}-(\overline{z}-\mu)(z_{i}-\mu)^{\top}+(\overline{z}-\mu)(\overline{z}-\mu)^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p17.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p17.3.1" class="ltx_text">Averaging over <math id="A3.SS3.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\dots,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\dots,N</annotation></semantics></math> and using <math id="A3.SS3.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(z_{i}-\mu)=\overline{z}-\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(z_{i}-\mu)=\overline{z}-\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx107" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex210"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex210.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(z_{i}-\overline{z}\right)\left(z_{i}-\overline{z}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(z_{i}-\overline{z}\right)\left(z_{i}-\overline{z}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex211"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex211.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex211.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)^{\top}-(\overline{z}-\mu)(\overline{z}-\mu)^{\top}-(\overline{z}-\mu)(\overline{z}-\mu)^{\top}+(\overline{z}-\mu)(\overline{z}-\mu)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)^{\top}-(\overline{z}-\mu)(\overline{z}-\mu)^{\top}-(\overline{z}-\mu)(\overline{z}-\mu)^{\top}+(\overline{z}-\mu)(\overline{z}-\mu)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex212"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex212.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex212.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)^{\top}-(\overline{z}-\mu)(\overline{z}-\mu)^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)^{\top}-(\overline{z}-\mu)(\overline{z}-\mu)^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p17.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p17.4.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx108" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex213"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex213.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(z_{i}-\overline{z}\right)\left(z_{i}-\overline{z}\right)^{\top}-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)^{\top}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(z_{i}-\overline{z}\right)\left(z_{i}-\overline{z}\right)^{\top}-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)\left(z_{i}-\mu\right)^{\top}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex213.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~(\overline{z}-\mu)(\overline{z}-\mu)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~(\overline{z}-\mu)(\overline{z}-\mu)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex214"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex214.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\succeq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⪰</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\succeq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex214.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~{\bf 0}_{d\times d}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~{\bf 0}_{d\times d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p17.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p17.5.1" class="ltx_text">which implies</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex215" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex215.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(z_{i}-\overline{z})(z_{i}-\overline{z})^{\top}\preceq\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(z_{i}-\mu)(z_{i}-\mu)^{\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(z_{i}-\overline{z})(z_{i}-\overline{z})^{\top}\preceq\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(z_{i}-\mu)(z_{i}-\mu)^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p17.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p17.6.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p18.1" class="ltx_p">Now, we combine everything together to prove <a href="#A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ C.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.9" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ C.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Claim <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>, we have shown Eq. (<a href="#A3.E34" title="Equation 34 ‣ C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>) hold with high probability. Combining with Fact <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem9" title="Fact C.9. ‣ C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.9</span></a>, we can justify that our polynomial constraints from Definition <a href="#A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="Algorithmic design. ‣ C.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> holds with high probability.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of sample complexity.<span id="A3.SS3.p20.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
We apply Claims <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a> and <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a> with truncation parameter set equal to <math id="A3.SS3.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> from Definition <a href="#A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>, and the covariance and mean<span id="A3.SS3.p20.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>shift bounds are to be interpreted under that choice.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that from Claim <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>, we know if <math id="A3.SS3.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha n\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha n\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,
then we have
<math id="A3.SS3.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\varepsilon^{\prime}N}{d}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\varepsilon^{\prime}N}{d}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
                  <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
                  
                  
                  
                  
                  
                  
                  
                We want to highlight that in Claim <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>, we prove that this statement hold for all arbitrary <math id="footnote3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in\left(0,0.1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in\left(0,0.1\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since what we truly have in our polynomial constraints (Definition <a href="#A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="Algorithmic design. ‣ C.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>) is <math id="footnote3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, we insert this <math id="footnote3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in our failure probability.</span></span></span>, which implies that the number of collaborator <math id="A3.SS3.p21.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx109" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex216"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex216.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle N\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle N\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex216.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon^{\prime}}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon^{\prime}}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex217"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex217.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex217.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\min\left\{\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\},\frac{1}{10}\right\}}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\min\left\{\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\},\frac{1}{10}\right\}}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex218"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex218.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex218.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\}}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\}}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p21.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p21.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second step follows from the definition of <math id="A3.SS3.p21.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Definition <a href="#A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="Algorithmic design. ‣ C.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>) and the third step follows from <math id="A3.SS3.p21.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{10}</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant. If <math id="A3.SS3.p21.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\geq\alpha n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\geq\alpha n</annotation></semantics></math>, then we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx110" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex219"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex219.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle nN\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle nN\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex219.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon/n}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon/n}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p21.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p21.3.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A3.SS3.p21.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&lt;\alpha n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&lt;\alpha n</annotation></semantics></math>, then we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx111" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex220"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex220.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle nN\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle nN\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex220.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\Omega\left(\frac{dn}{\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\}}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\Omega\left(\frac{dn}{\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\}}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex221"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex221.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex221.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\Omega\left(\frac{dn}{n\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\Omega\left(\frac{dn}{n\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex222"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex222.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex222.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx112" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex223"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex223.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle nN\geq\min\left\{\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon/n}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right),\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle nN\geq\min\left\{\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon/n}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right),\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, if <math id="A3.SS3.p23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1&lt;\alpha n\leq\frac{d}{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1&lt;\alpha n\leq\frac{d}{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, then we have <math id="A3.SS3.p23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{\prime}=\min\left\{\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\},\frac{1}{10}\right\}=\min\left\{n\alpha,\frac{1}{10}\right\}=\frac{1}{10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{\prime}=\min\left\{\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\},\frac{1}{10}\right\}=\min\left\{n\alpha,\frac{1}{10}\right\}=\frac{1}{10}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Definition <a href="#A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="Algorithmic design. ‣ C.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>) and <math id="A3.SS3.p23.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\alpha n\varepsilon^{\prime}N}{d}\right)\right)=d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\alpha nN}{d}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\alpha n\varepsilon^{\prime}N}{d}\right)\right)=d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\alpha nN}{d}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies that the total number of samples <math id="A3.SS3.p23.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="nN" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">nN</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx113" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex224"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex224.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle nN\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle nN\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex224.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p23.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p23.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we have shown the satisfiability of our polynomial system <math id="A3.SS3.p23.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖠</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>Identifiability</h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">After showing the satisfiability our polynomial system <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖠</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> (Definition <a href="#A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="Algorithmic design. ‣ C.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>), we present how we can use the polynomial system <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖠</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> to get a SoS algorithm solving Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Problem 1.1 (Mean shift). ‣ Mean Shift Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>.
In this section, we establish the identifiability of the true mean under the polynomial system <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖠</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.
After proving in <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a> that the system is satisfiable with high probability, we now show that any feasible
pseudoexpectation satisfying the same constraints must correspond to an accurate estimate of the true mean <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The argument proceeds in two steps.
First, leveraging the bounded-covariance condition enforced by the SoS constraints,
we show that the pseudoexpectation output <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}=\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}[\overline{Z}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}=\widetilde{\mathbb{E}}[\overline{Z}]</annotation></semantics></math> cannot deviate significantly from the mean of the clean users. This follows from concentration bounds on the user-level empirical means, whose covariances shrink by a factor of <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/n</annotation></semantics></math>.
Second, we bound the deviation between each user’s mean and the population mean <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>
by combining this concentration property with the assumption that uncorrupted users satisfy
<math id="A3.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mu_{i}-\mu\|_{2}\leq\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mu_{i}-\mu\|_{2}\leq\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> and with Claim <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>, which shows that the truncation step may slightly shift the mean, i.e., <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}\leq O\left(\sqrt{\gamma\varepsilon}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\mu_{i^{\prime}}-\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}\leq O\left(\sqrt{\gamma\varepsilon}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, we set <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\frac{1}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\frac{1}{n}</annotation></semantics></math> since each <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the empirical mean of <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples from a distribution with covariance <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⪯</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, allowing us to bound <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}[z_{i}]\preceq\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}[z_{i}]\preceq\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Together, these steps yield the final guarantee:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx114" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex225"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex225.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\mu-\widehat{\mu}\right\|_{2}&lt;O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\mu-\widehat{\mu}\right\|_{2}&lt;O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">showing that the SoS-based estimator is both statistically consistent and computationally efficient.
In essence, identifiability ensures that the polynomial constraints not only admit a feasible solution
(satisfiability) but also that every feasible solution must be close to the ground-truth mean <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>,
thereby completing the proof of Theorem <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem C.1 (Upper bound result of Theorem ). ‣ C.1 Main Result ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ C.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#A2.SS1" title="B.1 Accurate Estimation of the Empirical Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, using the polynomial system <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖠</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{A}</annotation></semantics></math> as defined in the lemma statement, we can get a SoS algorithm that outputs <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\E}\left[\overline{Z}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\E}\left[\overline{Z}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> in polynomial time satisfying:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx115" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\overline{z}-\widetilde{\E}\left[\overline{Z}\right]\right\|_{2}&lt;O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon^{\prime}\left(\frac{1}{n}+\alpha\right)}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\overline{z}-\widetilde{\E}\left[\overline{Z}\right]\right\|_{2}&lt;O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon^{\prime}\left(\frac{1}{n}+\alpha\right)}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">By the triangle inequality, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx116" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex226"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex226.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\overline{z}-\mu\right\|_{2}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\overline{z}-\mu\right\|_{2}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex226.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\overline{z}-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mu_{i}+\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mu_{i}-\mu\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\overline{z}-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mu_{i}+\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mu_{i}-\mu\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\overline{z}-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}+\left\|\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mu_{i}-\mu\right\|_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\overline{z}-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}+\left\|\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mu_{i}-\mu\right\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Considering the first term of Eq. (<a href="#A3.Ex226" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>), <math id="A3.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\overline{z}-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\overline{z}-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we first note that since each <math id="A3.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is computed via <math id="A3.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples from user <math id="A3.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx117" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex227"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex227.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}\left[z_{i}\right]\preceq\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{I}_{d}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}\left[z_{i}\right]\preceq\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{I}_{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, since <math id="A3.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is truncated and <math id="A3.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}\left[z_{i}\right]\preceq\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}\left[z_{i}\right]\preceq\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, putting this inside Claim <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a>, we can get with probability <math id="A3.SS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx118" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}z_{i}-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}&lt;O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}z_{i}-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mu_{i}\right\|_{2}&lt;O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Considering the second term, by the assumption <math id="A3.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\mu_{i}-\mu\right\|_{2}&lt;\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\mu_{i}-\mu\right\|_{2}&lt;\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> and Claim <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a> with <math id="A3.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\frac{1}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\frac{1}{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx119" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mu_{i}-\mu\right\|_{2}\leq\sqrt{\alpha}+\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mu_{i}-\mu\right\|_{2}\leq\sqrt{\alpha}+\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining Eq. (<a href="#A3.Ex226" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>), Eq. (<a href="#A3.E40" title="Equation 40 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a>), and Eq. (<a href="#A3.E41" title="Equation 41 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx120" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\overline{z}-\mu\right\|_{2}&lt;O\left(\sqrt{\alpha}+\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\overline{z}-\mu\right\|_{2}&lt;O\left(\sqrt{\alpha}+\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining Eq. (<a href="#A3.E38" title="Equation 38 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A3.E42" title="Equation 42 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ C.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx121" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex228"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex228.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\mu-\widetilde{\E}\left[\overline{Z}\right]\right\|_{2}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\mu-\widetilde{\E}\left[\overline{Z}\right]\right\|_{2}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex228.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\mu-\overline{z}+\overline{z}-\widetilde{\E}\left[\overline{Z}\right]\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\mu-\overline{z}+\overline{z}-\widetilde{\E}\left[\overline{Z}\right]\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex229"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex229.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex229.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\mu-\overline{z}\right\|_{2}+\left\|\overline{z}-\widetilde{\E}\left[\overline{Z}\right]\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\mu-\overline{z}\right\|_{2}+\left\|\overline{z}-\widetilde{\E}\left[\overline{Z}\right]\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex230"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex230.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex230.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon^{\prime}\left(\frac{1}{n}+\alpha\right)}+\sqrt{\alpha}+\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon^{\prime}\left(\frac{1}{n}+\alpha\right)}+\sqrt{\alpha}+\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex231"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex231.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex231.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon^{\prime}}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon^{\prime}}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second step follows from the triangle inequality and the last step follows from <math id="A3.SS4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\leq\varepsilon^{\prime}=\min\left\{\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\},\frac{1}{10}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\leq\varepsilon^{\prime}=\min\left\{\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\},\frac{1}{10}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Definition <a href="#A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="Algorithmic design. ‣ C.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Definition <a href="#A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="Algorithmic design. ‣ C.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>, we have <math id="A3.SS4.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{\prime}=\min\left\{\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\},\frac{1}{10}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{\prime}=\min\left\{\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\},\frac{1}{10}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx122" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex232"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex232.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\mu-\widetilde{\E}\left[\overline{Z}\right]\right\|_{2}&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\mu-\widetilde{\E}\left[\overline{Z}\right]\right\|_{2}&lt;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex232.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\min\left\{\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\},\frac{1}{10}\right\}}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\min\left\{\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\},\frac{1}{10}\right\}}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex233"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex233.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex233.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\}}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\}}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second step follows from <math id="A3.SS4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min\left\{\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\},\frac{1}{10}\right\}\leq\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min\left\{\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\},\frac{1}{10}\right\}\leq\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 1.<span id="A3.SS4.p11.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> If <math id="A3.SS4.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\}=\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\}=\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, then we get</span></span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx123" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex234"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex234.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\mu-\widetilde{\E}\left[\overline{Z}\right]\right\|_{2}&lt;O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\mu-\widetilde{\E}\left[\overline{Z}\right]\right\|_{2}&lt;O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case 2.<span id="A3.SS4.p12.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> If <math id="A3.SS4.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\}=n\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\left\{\varepsilon,n\alpha\right\}=n\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, then we have</span></span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx124" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex235"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex235.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon^{\prime}}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon^{\prime}}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex235.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\frac{n\alpha}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\frac{n\alpha}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex236"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex236.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex236.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\alpha}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\alpha}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">which completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, our goal is to analyze Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Problem 1.2 (Adversarial). ‣ Adversarial Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>, where an <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of users may be adversarially strong contaminated and may
provide adversarially or arbitrarily chosen samples, and for all the <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of uncorrupted users, their <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of samples may be adversarially or arbitrarily contaminated. This hierarchical structure—with inter-user corruption parameter <math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and intra-user corruption
parameter <math id="A4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>—makes the setting substantially more challenging and necessitates a refined SoS
formulation that simultaneously enforces consistency across both user and sample levels.
Specifically, in <a href="#A4.SS1" title="D.1 Main Result ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>, we restate the problem setting of Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Problem 1.2 (Adversarial). ‣ Adversarial Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a> and present our upper-bound result. In <a href="#A4.SS2" title="D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>, we formally define the polynomial system <math id="A4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖡</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{B}</annotation></semantics></math> and describe our SoS-based algorithmic framework for achieving this upper bound; we also provide an informal proof sketch explaining why this design attains the optimal error rate. In <a href="#A4.SS3" title="D.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>, we establish the satisfiability of the polynomial system, namely the existence of a feasible solution with high probability. Finally, in <a href="#A4.SS4" title="D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a>, we give a formal proof of correctness and derive the sample-complexity guarantee for our main result.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Main Result</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now, we restate our formal problem setup and its corresponding main result.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Problem 1.2 (Adversarial). ‣ Adversarial Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">A straightforward approach to the problem is to ignore the two-level structure of corruption
and simply treat all the samples across all users as being jointly <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varepsilon+\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varepsilon+\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>-corrupted.
Under this view, one can directly apply a standard robust mean estimation algorithm designed
for an <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varepsilon+\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varepsilon+\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of arbitrary corruptions, yielding an estimator with
accuracy of <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\sqrt{\varepsilon+\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\sqrt{\varepsilon+\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math>.
However, this approach is suboptimal because it fails to exploit the fact that
most users are only <em id="A4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">partially</em> corrupted—each good user has at most an <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction
of bad samples, while only an <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of users are entirely unreliable.
By explicitly modeling this hierarchical corruption structure in our SoS formulation,
we are able to isolate the good users and leverage the concentration within their data,
thereby improving the estimation error bound beyond <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\sqrt{\varepsilon+\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\sqrt{\varepsilon+\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Our main result of this section, which constitutes the upper-bound part of our main theorem (Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2.2 (Adversarial). ‣ 2 Main Results ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>), is as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Upper bound result of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2.2 (Adversarial). ‣ 2 Main Results ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in\left(0,\frac{1}{18}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>18</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in\left(0,\frac{1}{18}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\left(0,\frac{1}{90}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>90</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\left(0,\frac{1}{90}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon+5\alpha&lt;\frac{1}{18}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>18</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon+5\alpha&lt;\frac{1}{18}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=o(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=o(d)</annotation></semantics></math> samples from each of <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\in\mathbb{Z}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\in\mathbb{Z}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> users satisfying <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="nN\geq\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">nN\geq\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a polynomial-time algorithm (Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Algorithm ideas. ‣ 4.3 Handling Small Corruption in Good Users (Problem ). ‣ 4 Technical Overview ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) solving Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Problem 1.2 (Adversarial). ‣ Adversarial Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a> that outputs <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and satisfies
<math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\widehat{\mu}-\mu\right\|_{2}=O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\widehat{\mu}-\mu\right\|_{2}=O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>
with probability at least <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof of this theorem follows from the satisfiability (Lemma <a href="#A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>) and identifiability (Lemma <a href="#A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We give a detailed proof for the satisfiability (Lemma <a href="#A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>) and identifiability (Lemma <a href="#A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>) in <a href="#A4.SS3" title="D.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a> and <a href="#A4.SS4" title="D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a>. The goal of this section is to state these lemmas, present a proof overview, and explain how we can design our algorithm (Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Algorithm ideas. ‣ 4.3 Handling Small Corruption in Good Users (Problem ). ‣ 4 Technical Overview ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) stated in the theorem.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Algorithmic design.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our polynomial time SoS algorithm (Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Algorithm ideas. ‣ 4.3 Handling Small Corruption in Good Users (Problem ). ‣ 4 Technical Overview ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) is based on the polynomial system <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖡</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{B}</annotation></semantics></math> (defined below in Definition <a href="#A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>). Since each user’s dataset may itself contain corrupted samples, our algorithm must jointly
handle both user-level and sample-level contamination. We therefore extend the SoS framework by introducing a two-layer polynomial system <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖡</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{B}</annotation></semantics></math> that captures this hierarchical corruption
structure. At the sample level, the system enforces that, within each user, at least a <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of samples are consistent and their empirical covariance remains bounded, thereby filtering out local outliers. At the user level, it enforces that at least a <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of users are globally consistent and that the empirical covariance of their aggregated (cleaned) means is spectrally bounded.
Together, these constraints enable the algorithm to recover the true mean <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> with improved precision,
leveraging the fact that the clean samples within each user further reduce variance by a factor of <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition D.2</span></span><span id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Polynomial system <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖡</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{B}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For each user <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math> and sample index <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, the observed data point <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> may be adversarially corrupted (with <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> user level strong contamination and <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> sample level strong contamination), and <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes its latent clean counterpart. The binary decision variable <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i,j}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i,j}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates whether the sample <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> is treated as clean, and the binary variable <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> specifies whether user <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is globally uncorrupted. The variables <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are treated as indeterminates in our SoS polynomial system. Let <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> represent the cleaned user-level mean used in the higher-level aggregation. Let <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{1},B_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{1},B_{2}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> be “slack” variables.
Given <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in\left(0,\frac{1}{18}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>18</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in\left(0,\frac{1}{18}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\left(0,\frac{1}{90}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>90</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\left(0,\frac{1}{90}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon+5\alpha&lt;\frac{1}{18}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>18</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon+5\alpha&lt;\frac{1}{18}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples from each of <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\in\mathbb{Z}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\in\mathbb{Z}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> users, we define the polynomial system <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖡</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{B}</annotation></semantics></math> with the following constraints:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx125" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_left" style="white-space:normal;" colspan="5"><span id="A4.EGx125.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Crude refinement:</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}Z_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}Z_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overline{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overline{Z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}Z_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}Z_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{i,j}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{i,j}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=W_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=W_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{j=1}^{n}W_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{j=1}^{n}W_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\alpha)nU_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\alpha)nU_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{i,j}(Z_{i,j}-x_{i,j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{i,j}(Z_{i,j}-x_{i,j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}(Z_{i,j}-\overline{Z})(Z_{i,j}-\overline{Z})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}(Z_{i,j}-\overline{Z})(Z_{i,j}-\overline{Z})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\mathbb{I}_{d}-B_{1}B_{1}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\mathbb{I}_{d}-B_{1}B_{1}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody><tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_left" style="white-space:normal;" colspan="5"><span id="A4.EGx125.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">User-level refinement:</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle U_{i}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U_{i}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=U_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=U_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overline{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overline{Y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E51.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}Y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}Y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E52.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha}{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha}{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E53.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\varepsilon)N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\varepsilon)N</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle U_{i}\left(Y_{i}-Z_{i}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle U_{i}\left(Y_{i}-Z_{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E54.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(Y_{i}-\overline{Y}\right)\left(Y_{i}-\overline{Y}\right)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(Y_{i}-\overline{Y}\right)\left(Y_{i}-\overline{Y}\right)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E55.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\frac{1}{n}+\tau\right)\mathbb{I}_{d}-B_{2}B_{2}^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\frac{1}{n}+\tau\right)\mathbb{I}_{d}-B_{2}B_{2}^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For each user <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the empirical mean of its clean samples as
<math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}Z_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}Z_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,
The global averages are defined as
<math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{Z}=\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}Z_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{Z}=\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}Z_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>
and
<math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{Y}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}Y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{Y}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}Y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>,
which correspond, respectively, to the mean of all clean samples and the mean of the user-level aggregated means.
The model captures two levels of corruption. The parameter <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\left(0,\frac{1}{90}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>90</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\left(0,\frac{1}{90}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the intra-user corruption rate, meaning that for any uncorrupted user, at least a <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of its samples are clean. The parameter <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in(0,\frac{1}{18})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>18</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in(0,\frac{1}{18})</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the inter-user corruption rate, meaning that at least a <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of users are globally uncorrupted.
These assumptions are enforced via polynomial constraints ensuring that
<math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=1}^{n}W_{i,j}\geq(1-\alpha)nU_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=1}^{n}W_{i,j}\geq(1-\alpha)nU_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>
for each user <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}\geq(1-\varepsilon)N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}\geq(1-\varepsilon)N</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Consistency constraints enforce that samples marked as clean must agree with the observations, namely
<math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i,j}(Z_{i,j}-x_{i,j})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i,j}(Z_{i,j}-x_{i,j})=0</annotation></semantics></math>,
and that for uncorrupted users the auxiliary variable coincides with the empirical mean, i.e.,
<math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}(Y_{i}-Z_{i})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}(Y_{i}-Z_{i})=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Boolean constraints
<math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i,j}^{2}=W_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i,j}^{2}=W_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>
and
<math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}^{2}=U_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}^{2}=U_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>
ensure that the corruption indicators are binary. Finally, bounded second-moment conditions are imposed at both the sample and user levels:
<math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}(Z_{i,j}-\overline{Z})(Z_{i,j}-\overline{Z})^{\top}=2\mathbb{I}_{d}-B_{1}B_{1}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}(Z_{i,j}-\overline{Z})(Z_{i,j}-\overline{Z})^{\top}=2\mathbb{I}_{d}-B_{1}B_{1}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and
<math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(Y_{i}-\overline{Y})(Y_{i}-\overline{Y})^{\top}=\left(\frac{1}{n}+\tau\right)\mathbb{I}_{d}-B_{2}B_{2}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(Y_{i}-\overline{Y})(Y_{i}-\overline{Y})^{\top}=\left(\frac{1}{n}+\tau\right)\mathbb{I}_{d}-B_{2}B_{2}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>,
where <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\frac{\alpha}{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\frac{\alpha}{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen to alleviate the tightness of this empirical covariance bound while ensuring that it does not negatively influence the error bound.
Together, these constraints define a polynomial system that models hierarchical corruption and enables a Sum-of-Squares relaxation for robust mean estimation in the collaborative setting.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof overview.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Formally, we compute a pseudoexpectation <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\E}[\overline{Y}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\E}[\overline{Y}]</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the constraints of the
polynomial system <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖡</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{B}</annotation></semantics></math> (Definition <a href="#A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>) and output it as the estimated mean. This hierarchical
design allows the SoS relaxation to exploit both inter-user and intra-user structure, yielding the
tighter and optimal error bound <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\widehat{\mu}-\mu\right\|_{2}=O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\widehat{\mu}-\mu\right\|_{2}=O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> (established in Theorem <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1 (Upper bound result of Theorem ). ‣ D.1 Main Result ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>).
The proof of Theorem <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1 (Upper bound result of Theorem ). ‣ D.1 Main Result ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> follows the same two-step structure as in <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>,
consisting of satisfiability and identifiability. In the satisfiability step, we show that the
polynomial system <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖡</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{B}</annotation></semantics></math> admits a feasible solution with high probability under the assumed two-level
corruption model. Intuitively, when users are uncorrupted, setting <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i,j}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i,j}=1</annotation></semantics></math> for all clean samples and <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> for all good users yields a valid assignment that satisfies the bounded covariance conditions in <span id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 1</span> and <span id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 2</span> of Lemma <a href="#A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.3</span></span><span id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Satisfiability of <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖡</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{B}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let the notation be defined as in Definition <a href="#A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>. Let <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in\left(0,0.1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in\left(0,0.1\right)</annotation></semantics></math> be the failure probability. Then, with at least <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="nN\geq\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">nN\geq\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math> total number of samples, we can show that the following equation hold with probability at least <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Part 1.</span><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
</span><math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{nN}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left(Z_{i,j}-\overline{Z}\right)\left(Z_{i,j}-\overline{Z}\right)^{\top}\preceq 2\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{nN}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left(Z_{i,j}-\overline{Z}\right)\left(Z_{i,j}-\overline{Z}\right)^{\top}\preceq 2\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Part 2.</span><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
</span><math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(Y_{i}-\overline{Y}\right)\left(Y_{i}-\overline{Y}\right)^{\top}\preceq\left(\frac{1}{n}+\tau\right)\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(Y_{i}-\overline{Y}\right)\left(Y_{i}-\overline{Y}\right)^{\top}\preceq\left(\frac{1}{n}+\tau\right)\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Apply Lemma <a href="#A4.SS3" title="D.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a> with failure probability <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta/2</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain <span id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 1</span> with probability at least <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta/2</annotation></semantics></math>.
Apply Lemma <a href="#A4.SS3" title="D.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a> with failure probability <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta/2</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain <span id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 2</span> with probability at least <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta/2</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the union bound, both parts hold simultaneously with probability at least <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.4</span></span><span id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Identifiability of <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖡</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{B}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\E}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the SoS constraints <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖡</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, then with probability at least <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}=\widetilde{\E}[\overline{Y}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0.1389em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}=\widetilde{\E}[\overline{Y}]</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies
<math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\widehat{\mu}-\mu\right\|_{2}&lt;O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\widehat{\mu}-\mu\right\|_{2}&lt;O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The proof of this lemma is deferred to <a href="#A4.SS4" title="D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a>.
Combining the satisfiability and identifiability steps completes the proof of
Theorem <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem D.1 (Upper bound result of Theorem ). ‣ D.1 Main Result ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>, establishing that our SoS-based estimator achieves an accurate mean
recovery under multi-level corruption.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Satisfiability</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we show that our polynomial system <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖡</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{B}</annotation></semantics></math> is satisfiable (Lemma <a href="#A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>), namely it holds with high probability. We prove this under Lemma <a href="#A4.SS3" title="D.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#A4.SS3" title="D.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To show the satisfiability of our polynomial system <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖡</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, we need to prove that Eq. (<a href="#A4.E49" title="Equation 49 ‣ Definition D.2 (Polynomial system 𝖡). ‣ Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A4.E55" title="Equation 55 ‣ Definition D.2 (Polynomial system 𝖡). ‣ Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">55</span></a>) can be satisfied with high probability given the corrupted samples.
To prove them, we can adapt the same high-probability
covariance concentration arguments as those used in Claims <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>, <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>, and <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>.
Regarding Eq. (<a href="#A4.E49" title="Equation 49 ‣ Definition D.2 (Polynomial system 𝖡). ‣ Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a>), it claims that the empirical covariance of the aggregated clean samples is spectrally bounded by <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> with high probability.
To prove this, we use the truncation and concentration method introduced in Claims <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>.
As truncations only apply to the random variables, we define <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> as a random variable representing the raw data point <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.SS3.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.5</span></span><span id="A4.SS3.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let the notation be defined as in Definition <a href="#A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>. Let <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in\left(0,0.1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in\left(0,0.1\right)</annotation></semantics></math> be the failure probability. Then, with at least <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="nN\geq\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">nN\geq\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math> total number of samples, the <span id="A4.SS3.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 1</span> of Lemma <a href="#A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> holds with probability at least <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We define <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu:=\E\left[v_{i,j}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu:=\E\left[v_{i,j}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> truncated random variables</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx126" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X^{\prime}_{i,j}:=\begin{cases}v_{i,j},&amp;\text{if }\left\|v_{i,j}-\mu\right\|_{2}\leq 2\sqrt{\frac{d}{\alpha}},\\
\mu,&amp;\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise.</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X^{\prime}_{i,j}:=\begin{cases}v_{i,j},&amp;\text{if }\left\|v_{i,j}-\mu\right\|_{2}\leq 2\sqrt{\frac{d}{\alpha}},\\
\mu,&amp;\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">The probability that <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}_{i,j}\neq v_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}_{i,j}\neq v_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> exceeds <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> is exponentially small by
a Chernoff bound (by choosing <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=1</annotation></semantics></math> and inserting our <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> into the place of <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> in Claim <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>). In addition, by Claim <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>, we can get that the shift in mean is tightly bounded:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx127" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{X^{\prime}}-\mu\right\|_{2}\leq O\left(\sqrt{\alpha}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{X^{\prime}}-\mu\right\|_{2}\leq O\left(\sqrt{\alpha}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{X^{\prime}}=\E\left[X^{\prime}_{i,j}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{X^{\prime}}=\E\left[X^{\prime}_{i,j}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since each truncated variable satisfies <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}\left[X^{\prime}_{i,j}\right]\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}\left[X^{\prime}_{i,j}\right]\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, the population covariance of the truncated variables is bounded by <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We intend to apply the matrix Chernoff inequality (see Fact <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem5" title="Fact C.5 (Matrix Chernoff Inequality, Theorem 3.12 from []). ‣ C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a>). Thus, we define</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx128" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overline{X}_{i,j}^{\prime}:=\frac{1}{nN}(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}})(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}})^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overline{X}_{i,j}^{\prime}:=\frac{1}{nN}(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}})(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}})^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">By the definition of <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. (<a href="#A4.E56" title="Equation 56 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a>)), we know that for all <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx129" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex237"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex237.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|X_{i,j}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|X_{i,j}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex237.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|X_{i,j}^{\prime}-\mu\right\|_{2}+\left\|\mu-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|X_{i,j}^{\prime}-\mu\right\|_{2}+\left\|\mu-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex238"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex238.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex238.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\frac{d}{\alpha}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\frac{d}{\alpha}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E59.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\frac{d}{\alpha}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\frac{d}{\alpha}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from the triangle inequality, the second step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A4.E56" title="Equation 56 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A4.E57" title="Equation 57 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">57</span></a>), and the last step follows from <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Additionally, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx130" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex239"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex239.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{i\in[N],j\in[n]}\left\|\overline{X}_{i,j}^{\prime}\right\|_{2}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{i\in[N],j\in[n]}\left\|\overline{X}_{i,j}^{\prime}\right\|_{2}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex239.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\max_{i\in[N],j\in[n]}\left\|\frac{1}{nN}\left(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\left(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\max_{i\in[N],j\in[n]}\left\|\frac{1}{nN}\left(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\left(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex240"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex240.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex240.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{nN}\max_{i\in[N],j\in[n]}\left\|\left(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\left(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{nN}\max_{i\in[N],j\in[n]}\left\|\left(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\left(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex241"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex241.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex241.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{nN}\max_{i\in[N],j\in[n]}\left\|X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{nN}\max_{i\in[N],j\in[n]}\left\|X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E60.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{d}{nN\alpha}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{d}{nN\alpha}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A4.E58" title="Equation 58 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a>), the third step follows from Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem13" title="Fact A.13. ‣ A.3 Probabilistic and Algebraic Tools ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.13</span></a>, and the last step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A4.Ex237" title="In Proof. ‣ D.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">59</span></a>).
This implies that <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=O\left(\frac{d}{nN\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=O\left(\frac{d}{nN\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> with</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx131" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex242"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex242.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{0}_{d\times d}\preceq\overline{X}_{i,j}^{\prime}\preceq R\cdot\mathbb{I}_{d}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⪯</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{0}_{d\times d}\preceq\overline{X}_{i,j}^{\prime}\preceq R\cdot\mathbb{I}_{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p4.7.1" class="ltx_text">Furthermore, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx132" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex243"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex243.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\E\left[\frac{1}{nN}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\left(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>nN</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\E\left[\frac{1}{nN}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\left(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex243.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{nN}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\E\left[\left(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\left(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{nN}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\E\left[\left(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\left(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex244"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex244.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex244.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{nN}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\mathrm{Cov}\left[X^{\prime}_{i,j}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{nN}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\mathrm{Cov}\left[X^{\prime}_{i,j}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex245"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex245.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\preceq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⪯</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\preceq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex245.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\mathbb{I}_{d}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\mathbb{I}_{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p4.8.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from the linearity of expectation, the second step follows from the definition of covariance, and the last step follows from <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}\left[X^{\prime}_{i,j}\right]\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}\left[X^{\prime}_{i,j}\right]\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This implies the largest eigenvalue of <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E\left[\sum_{k=1}^{n}\overline{X}_{i,j}^{\prime}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E\left[\sum_{k=1}^{n}\overline{X}_{i,j}^{\prime}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\max}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\max}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Choosing <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=1</annotation></semantics></math> and including these into the matrix Chernoff inequality (Fact <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem5" title="Fact C.5 (Matrix Chernoff Inequality, Theorem 3.12 from []). ‣ C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a>), we can get</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx133" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex246"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex246.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[\left\|\frac{1}{nN}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\left(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{2}&gt;2\right]\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[\left\|\frac{1}{nN}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\left(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{2}&gt;2\right]\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex246.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~d\left(\frac{e}{4}\right)^{\mu_{\max}/R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>e</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~d\left(\frac{e}{4}\right)^{\mu_{\max}/R}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex247"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex247.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex247.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{Nn\alpha}{d}\right)\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{Nn\alpha}{d}\right)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p4.9.1" class="ltx_text">where the second step follows from plugging in <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\max}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\max}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=O\left(\frac{d}{nN\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=O\left(\frac{d}{nN\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
This implies that with probability at least <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{Nn\alpha}{d}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{Nn\alpha}{d}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx134" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex248"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex248.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{nN}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\left(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\preceq 2\mathbb{I}_{d}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{nN}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)\left(X^{\prime}_{i,j}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\preceq 2\mathbb{I}_{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p4.10.1" class="ltx_text">which supports that <span id="A4.SS3.p4.10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 1</span> of Lemma <a href="#A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> holds with probability at least <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{Nn\alpha}{d}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{Nn\alpha}{d}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
To ensure that our failure probability <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{Nn\alpha}{d}\right)\right)\leq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{Nn\alpha}{d}\right)\right)\leq\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, for all arbitrary <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in\left(0,0.1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in\left(0,0.1\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, we need our total sample <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="nN" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">nN</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx135" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex249"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex249.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle nN\geq\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle nN\geq\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p4.11.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, since <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> (the clean samples) differs from <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> (corrupted samples that we receive) on at most an <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon+\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon+\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of indices (due to the two levels of strong contamination by Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Problem 1.2 (Adversarial). ‣ Adversarial Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>), and <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> differs from <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> on at most an <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of indices (due to Claim <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>), our truncated random variable <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> can be viewed as <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon+2\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon+2\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> strong contamination from corrupted samples that we receive <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Now, considering Eq. (<a href="#A4.E55" title="Equation 55 ‣ Definition D.2 (Polynomial system 𝖡). ‣ Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">55</span></a>), we use <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> to represent the cleaned user-level mean.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.SS3.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.6</span></span><span id="A4.SS3.4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let the notation be defined as in Definition <a href="#A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>. Let <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in\left(0,0.1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in\left(0,0.1\right)</annotation></semantics></math> be the failure probability. Then, with at least <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="nN\geq\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">nN\geq\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math> total number of samples, the <span id="A4.SS3.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 2</span> of Lemma <a href="#A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> holds with probability at least <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">This proof shares the same structure as Lemma <a href="#A4.SS3" title="D.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>. We further make use of the random variable <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i,j}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i,j}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> from Lemma <a href="#A4.SS3" title="D.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a> (see Eq. (<a href="#A4.E56" title="Equation 56 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a>)). We define the random variable <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}^{\prime}:=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}X_{i,j}^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}^{\prime}:=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}X_{i,j}^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, for all <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|X^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}\leq 2\sqrt{\frac{d}{n\varepsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|X^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}\leq 2\sqrt{\frac{d}{n\varepsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then we define our <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{i,j}^{\prime}:=X^{\prime}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{i,j}^{\prime}:=X^{\prime}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>; otherwise, we define <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{i,j}^{\prime}=\mu_{X^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{i,j}^{\prime}=\mu_{X^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This can make <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{i}^{\prime}:=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}Y_{i,j}^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{i}^{\prime}:=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}Y_{i,j}^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx136" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y_{i}^{\prime}:=\begin{cases}X_{i}^{\prime},&amp;\text{if }\left\|X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}\leq 2\sqrt{\frac{d}{n\varepsilon}},\\
\mu_{X^{\prime}},&amp;\text{otherwise,}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise,</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y_{i}^{\prime}:=\begin{cases}X_{i}^{\prime},&amp;\text{if }\left\|X_{i}^{\prime}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}\leq 2\sqrt{\frac{d}{n\varepsilon}},\\
\mu_{X^{\prime}},&amp;\text{otherwise,}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{X^{\prime}}=\E\left[X_{i}^{\prime}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{X^{\prime}}=\E\left[X_{i}^{\prime}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{Y^{\prime}}=\E\left[Y_{i}^{\prime}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{Y^{\prime}}=\E\left[Y_{i}^{\prime}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>.
The probability that <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}_{i}\neq Y_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}_{i}\neq Y_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> exceeds <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is exponentially small by
a Chernoff bound (by choosing <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=1/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=1/n</annotation></semantics></math> in Claim <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>). In addition, by Claim <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>, we can get that the shift in mean is tightly bounded:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx137" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{X^{\prime}}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}\leq O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon/n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{X^{\prime}}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}\leq O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon/n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since each truncated variable satisfies <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}\left[Y_{i}^{\prime}\right]\preceq\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}\left[Y_{i}^{\prime}\right]\preceq\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, the population covariance of the truncated variables is bounded by <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We intend to apply the matrix Chernoff inequality (see Fact <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem5" title="Fact C.5 (Matrix Chernoff Inequality, Theorem 3.12 from []). ‣ C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a>). Thus, we define</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx138" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overline{Y}_{i}^{\prime}:=\frac{1}{N}\left(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right)\left(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overline{Y}_{i}^{\prime}:=\frac{1}{N}\left(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right)\left(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">By the definition of <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{\prime}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{\prime}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. (<a href="#A4.E61" title="Equation 61 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">61</span></a>)), we know that for all <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx139" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex250"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex250.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex250.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}+\left\|\mu_{X^{\prime}}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{X^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}+\left\|\mu_{X^{\prime}}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex251"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex251.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex251.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\frac{d}{n\varepsilon}}+\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\frac{d}{n\varepsilon}}+\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E64.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\frac{d}{n\varepsilon}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\sqrt{\frac{d}{n\varepsilon}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from the triangle inequality, the second step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A4.E61" title="Equation 61 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">61</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A4.E62" title="Equation 62 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">62</span></a>), and the last step follows from <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Additionally, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx140" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex252"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex252.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{i\in[N],j\in[n]}\left\|\overline{Y}_{i}^{\prime}\right\|_{2}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{i\in[N],j\in[n]}\left\|\overline{Y}_{i}^{\prime}\right\|_{2}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex252.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\max_{i\in[N],j\in[n]}\left\|\frac{1}{N}\left(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right)\left(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\max_{i\in[N],j\in[n]}\left\|\frac{1}{N}\left(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right)\left(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex253"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex253.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex253.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\max_{i\in[N],j\in[n]}\left\|\left(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right)\left(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\max_{i\in[N],j\in[n]}\left\|\left(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right)\left(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex254"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex254.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex254.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\max_{i\in[N],j\in[n]}\left\|Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\max_{i\in[N],j\in[n]}\left\|Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E65.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{d}{Nn\varepsilon}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{d}{Nn\varepsilon}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p7.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p7.6.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A4.E63" title="Equation 63 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">63</span></a>), the third step follows from Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem13" title="Fact A.13. ‣ A.3 Probabilistic and Algebraic Tools ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.13</span></a>, and the last step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A4.Ex250" title="In Proof. ‣ D.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">64</span></a>).
This implies that <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=O\left(\frac{d}{Nn\varepsilon}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=O\left(\frac{d}{Nn\varepsilon}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> with</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx141" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex255"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex255.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{0}_{d\times d}\preceq\overline{Y}_{i}^{\prime}\preceq R\cdot\mathbb{I}_{d}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⪯</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{0}_{d\times d}\preceq\overline{Y}_{i}^{\prime}\preceq R\cdot\mathbb{I}_{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p7.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p7.7.1" class="ltx_text">Furthermore, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx142" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex256"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex256.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\E\left[\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right)\left(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\E\left[\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right)\left(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex256.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\E\left[\left(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right)\left(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\E\left[\left(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right)\left(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}}\right)^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex257"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex257.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex257.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathrm{Cov}\left[Y^{\prime}_{i}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathrm{Cov}\left[Y^{\prime}_{i}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex258"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex258.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\preceq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⪯</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\preceq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex258.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{I}_{d}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{I}_{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p7.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p7.8.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from the linearity of expectation, the second step follows from the definition of covariance, and the last step follows from our polynomial constraint (see Definition <a href="#A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>).
This implies the largest eigenvalue of <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\E\left[\sum_{k=1}^{n}\overline{Y}_{i}^{\prime}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\E\left[\sum_{k=1}^{n}\overline{Y}_{i}^{\prime}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\max}\leq 1/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\max}\leq 1/n</annotation></semantics></math>.
Choosing <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=n\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=n\tau</annotation></semantics></math> and including these into the matrix Chernoff inequality (Fact <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem5" title="Fact C.5 (Matrix Chernoff Inequality, Theorem 3.12 from []). ‣ C.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix C Learning From Corrupted Batches With Bounded User Means ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a>), we can get</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx143" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex259"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex259.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[\left\|\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}})(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}})^{\top}\right\|_{2}&gt;\left(1+n\tau\right)\frac{1}{n}\right]\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[\left\|\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}})(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}})^{\top}\right\|_{2}&gt;\left(1+n\tau\right)\frac{1}{n}\right]\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex259.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~d\left(\frac{e^{n\tau}}{\left(1+n\tau\right)^{1+n\tau}}\right)^{\mu_{\max}/R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~d\left(\frac{e^{n\tau}}{\left(1+n\tau\right)^{1+n\tau}}\right)^{\mu_{\max}/R}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex260"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex260.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex260.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{d}{\left(1+n\tau\right)^{\mu_{\max}/R}}\left(\frac{e}{1+n\tau}\right)^{n\tau\mu_{\max}/R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{d}{\left(1+n\tau\right)^{\mu_{\max}/R}}\left(\frac{e}{1+n\tau}\right)^{n\tau\mu_{\max}/R}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex261"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex261.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex261.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~d\left(\frac{e}{1+n\tau}\right)^{n\tau\mu_{\max}/R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~d\left(\frac{e}{1+n\tau}\right)^{n\tau\mu_{\max}/R}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex262"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex262.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex262.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\varepsilon n\tau N}{d}\right)\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\varepsilon n\tau N}{d}\right)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p7.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p7.9.1" class="ltx_text">where the third step follows from <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+n\tau&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+n\tau&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and the last step follows from plugging in <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\max}\leq 1/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\max}\leq 1/n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\left(\frac{d}{n\varepsilon}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\left(\frac{d}{n\varepsilon}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
This implies that with probability at least <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\varepsilon n\tau N}{d}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\varepsilon n\tau N}{d}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx144" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex263"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex263.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}})(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}})^{\top}\preceq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}})(Y^{\prime}_{i}-\mu_{Y^{\prime}})^{\top}\preceq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex263.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left(1+n\tau\right)\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left(1+n\tau\right)\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex264"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex264.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex264.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left(\frac{1}{n}+\tau\right)\mathbb{I}_{d}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left(\frac{1}{n}+\tau\right)\mathbb{I}_{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p7.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p7.10.1" class="ltx_text">which supports that <span id="A4.SS3.p7.10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 2</span> of Lemma <a href="#A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> holds with probability at least <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\varepsilon n\tau N}{d}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\varepsilon n\tau N}{d}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
To ensure that our failure probability <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\varepsilon n\tau N}{d}\right)\right)\leq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\exp\left(-\Omega\left(\frac{\varepsilon n\tau N}{d}\right)\right)\leq\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, for all arbitrary <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in\left(0,0.1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in\left(0,0.1\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, we need our total sample <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="nN" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">nN</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx145" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex265"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex265.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle nN\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle nN\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex265.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon\tau}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\varepsilon\tau}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex266"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex266.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex266.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p7.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p7.11.1" class="ltx_text">where the second step follows from <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\frac{\alpha}{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\frac{\alpha}{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Definition <a href="#A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>).
Finally, we have shown in Lemma <a href="#A4.SS3" title="D.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a> that our initial truncated random variable <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> can be viewed as <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon+2\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon+2\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> strong contamination from corrupted samples that we receive <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the definition of <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{i}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{i}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{i,j}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{i,j}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. (<a href="#A4.E61" title="Equation 61 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">61</span></a>)), we note that <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{i,j}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{i,j}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> can be viewed as <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> strong contamination from <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we can view <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{i,j}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{i,j}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\varepsilon+2\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\varepsilon+2\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> strong contamination from corrupted samples that we receive <math id="A4.SS3.p7.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Identifiability</h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The goal of this section is to establish the identifiability of the true mean <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>
under the two-level corruption model captured by the polynomial system <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖡</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{B}</annotation></semantics></math>.
After showing in <a href="#A4.SS3" title="D.3 Satisfiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a> that the system is satisfiable with high probability,
we now argue that any feasible pseudoexpectation consistent with the SoS constraints
must correspond to an accurate estimate of <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">At a high level, our proof proceeds in two stages: First each good user may contain at most an <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of corrupted samples. The SoS constraints ensure that the empirical mean of the remaining <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\alpha)n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\alpha)n</annotation></semantics></math> samples has covariance bounded by <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, the user-level cleaned means <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{Y_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{Y_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> concentrate tightly around
their expectations.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Second, an <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of users may be entirely corrupted,
but the remaining users have bounded deviations.
Using the bounded-covariance conditions enforced by the SoS system,
we show that the pseudoexpectation output <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\E}[\overline{Y}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\E}[\overline{Y}]</annotation></semantics></math>
(and thus the estimator <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>) cannot deviate far from the mean
of the clean users.
The total deviation accumulates additively from the two levels of corruption:
<math id="A4.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> from user-level corruption
and <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> from the corruption of samples within each uncorrupted user.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Together, these steps show that any feasible pseudoexpectation satisfying
the SoS constraints must yield a mean estimate <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</p>
<table id="A4.EGx146" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex267"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex267.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\widehat{\mu}-\mu\right\|_{2}&lt;O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\widehat{\mu}-\mu\right\|_{2}&lt;O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">thereby establishing identifiability of <math id="A4.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> under the hierarchical corruption model.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">For all <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math> and for all <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[n]</annotation></semantics></math>, we define</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx147" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\mu}_{i}:=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}v_{i,j}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\mu}_{i}:=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}v_{i,j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the clear counterpart of the corrupted sample <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Definition <a href="#A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>), and</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx148" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\mu}:=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\widetilde{\mu}_{i}=\frac{1}{nN}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}v_{i,j}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\mu}:=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\widetilde{\mu}_{i}=\frac{1}{nN}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}v_{i,j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">We introduce a new indicator variable</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx149" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E68.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{i}:=\mathds{1}_{\left\{\text{User $i$ has}\geq\left(1-\alpha\right)\text{ fraction }v_{i,j}=x_{i,j}\right\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mtext>User </mtext><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mtext> has</mtext></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>)</mo><mtext> fraction </mtext><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{I}_{i}:=\mathds{1}_{\left\{\text{User $i$ has}\geq\left(1-\alpha\right)\text{ fraction }v_{i,j}=x_{i,j}\right\}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">which indicates whether user <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> has at least <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of uncorrupted samples.
By the definition of the <math id="A4.SS4.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx150" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex268"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex268.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{4}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\left\{\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}=\langle\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\rangle^{2}\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:9.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="9.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">4</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="9.0pt"><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em">{</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{4}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\left\{\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}=\langle\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\rangle^{2}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, by combining Eq. (<a href="#A4.E51" title="Equation 51 ‣ Definition D.2 (Polynomial system 𝖡). ‣ Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">51</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A4.E67" title="Equation 67 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">67</span></a>), we can get</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx151" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex269"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex269.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{4}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\left\{\langle\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\rangle^{2}=\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(1-U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i})\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\rangle+\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i}\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\rangle\right)^{2}\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:9.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="9.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">4</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="9.0pt"><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{4}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\left\{\langle\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\rangle^{2}=\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(1-U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i})\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\rangle+\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i}\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\rangle\right)^{2}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Applying the SoS inequality <math id="A4.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a+b)^{2}\leq 2a^{2}+2b^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a+b)^{2}\leq 2a^{2}+2b^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, which follows from</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx152" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex270"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex270.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2a^{2}+2b^{2}-(a+b)^{2}=(a-b)^{2}\geq 0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2a^{2}+2b^{2}-(a+b)^{2}=(a-b)^{2}\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx153" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E69.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{4}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\left\{\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\leq 2\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(1-U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i})\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\rangle\right)^{2}+2\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i}\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\rangle\right)^{2}\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:9.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="9.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">4</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="9.0pt"><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em">{</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{4}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\left\{\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\leq 2\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(1-U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i})\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\rangle\right)^{2}+2\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i}\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\rangle\right)^{2}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Considering the first term of Eq. (<a href="#A4.E69" title="Equation 69 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">69</span></a>), we use the SoS Cauchy-Schwarz inequality (Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Fact A.1 (SoS Cauchy-Schwarz, Claim 2.6 in []). ‣ A.1 Sum-of-squares ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>) to obtain</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx154" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E70.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{6}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(1-U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i})\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\rangle\right)^{2}\leq\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(1-U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i})^{2}\right)\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\rangle^{2}\right)\Bigg\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:9.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="9.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">6</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="9.0pt"><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{6}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(1-U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i})\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\rangle\right)^{2}\leq\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(1-U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i})^{2}\right)\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\rangle^{2}\right)\Bigg\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Regarding <math id="A4.SS4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(1-U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(1-U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx155" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex271"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex271.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{2}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(1-U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i})^{2}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:9.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="9.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="9.0pt"><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{2}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(1-U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i})^{2}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex271.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}1+U_{i}^{2}\mathcal{I}_{i}^{2}-2U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}1+U_{i}^{2}\mathcal{I}_{i}^{2}-2U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex272"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex272.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex272.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}1-U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}1-U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex273"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex273.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex273.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}1-U_{i}+U_{i}\left(1-\mathcal{I}_{i}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}1-U_{i}+U_{i}\left(1-\mathcal{I}_{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex274"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex274.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex274.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~1-\left(1-\varepsilon\right)+\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}\left(1-\mathcal{I}_{i}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~1-\left(1-\varepsilon\right)+\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}\left(1-\mathcal{I}_{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex275"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex275.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex275.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\varepsilon+\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(1-\mathcal{I}_{i}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\varepsilon+\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(1-\mathcal{I}_{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E71.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~2\varepsilon\Bigg\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~2\varepsilon\Bigg\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second step follows from <math id="A4.SS4.p9.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{7.98607pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-7.98607pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[7.98607pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{2}$}}}\hskip-7.98607pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[7.98607pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{}$}}}$}}}\left\{U_{i}^{2}=U_{i}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:8.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:8.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="8.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:8.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="8.0pt"></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em">{</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{7.98607pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-7.98607pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[7.98607pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{2}$}}}\hskip-7.98607pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[7.98607pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{}$}}}$}}}\left\{U_{i}^{2}=U_{i}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Eq. (<a href="#A4.E50" title="Equation 50 ‣ Definition D.2 (Polynomial system 𝖡). ‣ Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a>)) and the fact that <math id="A4.SS4.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is an indicator variable (see Eq. (<a href="#A4.E68" title="Equation 68 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">68</span></a>)), the third step follows from the definition of <math id="A4.SS4.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Eq. (<a href="#A4.E68" title="Equation 68 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">68</span></a>)), the fourth step follows from <math id="A4.SS4.p9.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{7.98607pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-7.98607pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[7.98607pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{1}$}}}\hskip-7.98607pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[7.98607pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{}$}}}$}}}\left\{\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}\geq(1-\varepsilon)N\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:8.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:8.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="8.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:8.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="8.0pt"></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em">{</mo><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{7.98607pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-7.98607pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[7.98607pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{1}$}}}\hskip-7.98607pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[7.98607pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{}$}}}$}}}\left\{\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}\geq(1-\varepsilon)N\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the fifth and the last step follows from the fact that <math id="A4.SS4.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> fraction of the users are corrupted.
Furthermore, defining <math id="A4.SS4.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b:=\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b:=\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx156" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex276"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex276.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{4}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},b\rangle^{2}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:9.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="9.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">4</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="9.0pt"><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{4}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},b\rangle^{2}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex276.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i}+b-b,b\rangle^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i}+b-b,b\rangle^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex277"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex277.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex277.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(\langle\widetilde{\mu}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},b\rangle-\langle\overline{Y}-Y_{i},b\rangle+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(\langle\widetilde{\mu}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},b\rangle-\langle\overline{Y}-Y_{i},b\rangle+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex278"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex278.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex278.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{3}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\langle\widetilde{\mu}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},b\rangle^{2}+\langle\overline{Y}-Y_{i},b\rangle^{2}+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{3}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\langle\widetilde{\mu}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},b\rangle^{2}+\langle\overline{Y}-Y_{i},b\rangle^{2}+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E72.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~3\left(b^{\top}\Sigma_{\widetilde{\mu}}b+b^{\top}\mathrm{Cov}\left[Y_{i}\right]b+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)\Bigg\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~3\left(b^{\top}\Sigma_{\widetilde{\mu}}b+b^{\top}\mathrm{Cov}\left[Y_{i}\right]b+\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)\Bigg\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the second step follows from the linearity of inner product, the third step follows from Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem5" title="Fact A.5. ‣ A.1 Sum-of-squares ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>, and the last step follows from the definition of the (empirical) covariance. In addition, due to Eq. (<a href="#A4.E66" title="Equation 66 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">66</span></a>) (<math id="A4.SS4.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mu}_{i}:=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}v_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mu}_{i}:=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}v_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>) and for each <math id="A4.SS4.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS4.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}\left[v_{i,j}\right]\preceq 2\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}\left[v_{i,j}\right]\preceq 2\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that the empirical covariance <math id="A4.SS4.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\widetilde{\mu}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\widetilde{\mu}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx157" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E73.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{2}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{b^{\top}\Sigma_{\widetilde{\mu}}b\leq\frac{2}{n}\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}\Bigg\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:9.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="9.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="9.0pt"><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mi>b</mi><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{2}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{b^{\top}\Sigma_{\widetilde{\mu}}b\leq\frac{2}{n}\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}\Bigg\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">hold with high probability.
Similarly, by Eq. (<a href="#A4.E55" title="Equation 55 ‣ Definition D.2 (Polynomial system 𝖡). ‣ Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">55</span></a>) and Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Fact A.2 (SoS operator norm, Claim 2.7 in []). ‣ A.1 Sum-of-squares ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx158" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E74.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{2}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{b^{\top}\mathrm{Cov}\left[Y_{i}\right]b\leq\left(\frac{1}{n}+\tau\right)\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}\Bigg\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:9.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="9.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="9.0pt"><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{2}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{b^{\top}\mathrm{Cov}\left[Y_{i}\right]b\leq\left(\frac{1}{n}+\tau\right)\left\|b\right\|_{2}^{2}\Bigg\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(74)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining Eq. (<a href="#A4.Ex276" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">72</span></a>), Eq. (<a href="#A4.E73" title="Equation 73 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">73</span></a>), and Eq. (<a href="#A4.E74" title="Equation 74 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">74</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx159" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E75.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{4}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},b\rangle^{2}\leq 3\left(4\left(\frac{1}{n}+\tau\right)\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)\Bigg\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:9.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="9.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">4</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="9.0pt"><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{4}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},b\rangle^{2}\leq 3\left(4\left(\frac{1}{n}+\tau\right)\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)\Bigg\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(75)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">We further combine Eq. (<a href="#A4.E70" title="Equation 70 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">70</span></a>), Eq. (<a href="#A4.Ex271" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">71</span></a>), and Eq. (<a href="#A4.E75" title="Equation 75 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">75</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx160" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E76.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{6}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{2\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(1-U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i})\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\rangle\right)^{2}\leq 12\varepsilon\left(4\left(\frac{1}{n}+\tau\right)\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)\Bigg\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:9.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="9.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">6</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="9.0pt"><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{6}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{2\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(1-U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i})\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\rangle\right)^{2}\leq 12\varepsilon\left(4\left(\frac{1}{n}+\tau\right)\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)\Bigg\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(76)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">which completes the bound for the first term of Eq. (<a href="#A4.E69" title="Equation 69 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">69</span></a>).
Now, we consider the second term of Eq. (<a href="#A4.E69" title="Equation 69 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">69</span></a>). We have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx161" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E77.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{4}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i}\left\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\rangle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:9.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="9.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">4</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="9.0pt"><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{4}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i}\left\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\rangle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E77.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i}\left(\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\rangle\right)\Bigg\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i}\left(\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\rangle\right)\Bigg\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(77)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A4.E66" title="Equation 66 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">66</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A4.E44" title="Equation 44 ‣ Definition D.2 (Polynomial system 𝖡). ‣ Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>).
Now, with any arbitrary <math id="A4.SS4.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider <math id="A4.SS4.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\langle Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\langle Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. We give the following claim:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.2.1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_claim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.SS4.2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim D.7</span></span><span id="A4.SS4.2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.SS4.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We define <math id="A4.SS4.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A:=\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A:=\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx162" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex279"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex279.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{2}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\left\langle Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j},A\right\rangle=\left(1-W_{i,j}\mathds{1}_{\left\{v_{i,j}=x_{i,j}\right\}}\right)\cdot\left\langle Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j},A\right\rangle\Bigg\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:9.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="9.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="9.0pt"><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{2}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\left\langle Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j},A\right\rangle=\left(1-W_{i,j}\mathds{1}_{\left\{v_{i,j}=x_{i,j}\right\}}\right)\cdot\left\langle Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j},A\right\rangle\Bigg\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS4.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">It suffices to show</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx163" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E78.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{2}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{0=-W_{i,j}\mathds{1}_{\left\{v_{i,j}=x_{i,j}\right\}}\cdot\left\langle Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j},A\right\rangle\Bigg\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:9.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="9.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="9.0pt"><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{2}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{0=-W_{i,j}\mathds{1}_{\left\{v_{i,j}=x_{i,j}\right\}}\cdot\left\langle Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j},A\right\rangle\Bigg\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(78)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A4.SS4.p13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathds{1}_{\left\{v_{i,j}=x_{i,j}\right\}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathds{1}_{\left\{v_{i,j}=x_{i,j}\right\}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then Eq. (<a href="#A4.E78" title="Equation 78 ‣ Proof. ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">78</span></a>) holds. If <math id="A4.SS4.p13.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathds{1}_{\left\{v_{i,j}=x_{i,j}\right\}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟙</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathds{1}_{\left\{v_{i,j}=x_{i,j}\right\}}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, then we have <math id="A4.SS4.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i,j}=x_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i,j}=x_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>. By our polynomial constraint (Eq. (<a href="#A4.E48" title="Equation 48 ‣ Definition D.2 (Polynomial system 𝖡). ‣ Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>)),
we have <math id="A4.SS4.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i,j}(Z_{i,j}-x_{i,j})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i,j}(Z_{i,j}-x_{i,j})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we have <math id="A4.SS4.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i,j}(Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i,j}(Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Taking inner product
with <math id="A4.SS4.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> gives us <math id="A4.SS4.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i,j}\langle Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j},A\rangle=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i,j}\langle Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j},A\rangle=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, combining Eq. (<a href="#A4.E77" title="Equation 77 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">77</span></a>) and Claim <a href="#A4.SS4" title="D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx164" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex280"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
