<p id="A4.SS4.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second step follows from the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality (see Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Fact A.1 (SoS Cauchy-Schwarz, Claim 2.6 in []). ‣ A.1 Sum-of-squares ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>), the third step follows from <math id="A4.SS4.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}=U_{i}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}=U_{i}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Eq. (<a href="#A4.E50" title="Equation 50 ‣ Definition D.2 (Polynomial system 𝖡). ‣ Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a>)), the definition of the indicator function <math id="A4.SS4.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the last step follows from</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx165" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex284"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex284.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left(1-W_{i,j}\mathds{1}_{\left\{v_{i,j}=x_{i,j}\right\}}\right)^{2}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(1-W_{i,j}\mathds{1}_{\left\{v_{i,j}=x_{i,j}\right\}}\right)^{2}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex284.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~1+W_{i,j}^{2}\mathds{1}_{\left\{v_{i,j}=x_{i,j}\right\}}^{2}-2W_{i,j}\mathds{1}_{\left\{v_{i,j}=x_{i,j}\right\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>𝟙</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mn>𝟙</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~1+W_{i,j}^{2}\mathds{1}_{\left\{v_{i,j}=x_{i,j}\right\}}^{2}-2W_{i,j}\mathds{1}_{\left\{v_{i,j}=x_{i,j}\right\}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
