<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E80.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~2\alpha\Bigg\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~2\alpha\Bigg\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(80)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the third step follows from <math id="A4.SS4.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i},\mathcal{I}_{i},W_{i,j}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i},\mathcal{I}_{i},W_{i,j}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the fourth step follows from our polynomial constraint <math id="A4.SS4.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}=(1-\varepsilon)N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}=(1-\varepsilon)N</annotation></semantics></math> (see Eq. (<a href="#A4.E53" title="Equation 53 ‣ Definition D.2 (Polynomial system 𝖡). ‣ Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">53</span></a>)) and the definition of <math id="A4.SS4.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Eq. (<a href="#A4.E68" title="Equation 68 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">68</span></a>)), the fifth step follows from our polynomial constraints <math id="A4.SS4.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}^{2}=U_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}^{2}=U_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Eq. (<a href="#A4.E50" title="Equation 50 ‣ Definition D.2 (Polynomial system 𝖡). ‣ Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a>)) and <math id="A4.SS4.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=1}^{n}W_{i,j}=(1-\alpha)nU_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=1}^{n}W_{i,j}=(1-\alpha)nU_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Eq. (<a href="#A4.E47" title="Equation 47 ‣ Definition D.2 (Polynomial system 𝖡). ‣ Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>)), the sixth step follows from our polynomial constraint <math id="A4.SS4.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}=(1-\varepsilon)N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}=(1-\varepsilon)N</annotation></semantics></math> (see Eq. (<a href="#A4.E53" title="Equation 53 ‣ Definition D.2 (Polynomial system 𝖡). ‣ Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">53</span></a>)), and the seventh step follows from our Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Problem 1.2 (Adversarial). ‣ Adversarial Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a> that at most an <math id="A4.SS4.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of good user’s samples are corrupted and at most <math id="A4.SS4.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> fraction of users are bad.
Considering the second part <math id="A4.SS4.p15.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\rangle^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\rangle^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> of Eq. (<a href="#A4.Ex280" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">79</span></a>), we define <math id="A4.SS4.p15.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c:=\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c:=\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> and have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx167" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex296"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex296.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{4}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:9.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="9.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">4</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="9.0pt"><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mpadded></mpadded><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{4}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex296.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j},c\right\rangle^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j},c\right\rangle^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex297"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex297.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex297.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j}-c+c,c\right\rangle^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j}-c+c,c\right\rangle^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex298"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex298.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex298.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left(\left\langle Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j}-c,c\right\rangle+\left\langle c,c\right\rangle\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left(\left\langle Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j}-c,c\right\rangle+\left\langle c,c\right\rangle\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex299"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex299.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex299.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left(\left\langle Z_{i,j}-\overline{Y},c\right\rangle-\left\langle v_{i,j}-\widetilde{\mu},c\right\rangle+\left\|c\right\|_{2}^{2}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left(\left\langle Z_{i,j}-\overline{Y},c\right\rangle-\left\langle v_{i,j}-\widetilde{\mu},c\right\rangle+\left\|c\right\|_{2}^{2}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E81.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{3}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle Z_{i,j}-\overline{Y},c\right\rangle^{2}+\frac{3}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle v_{i,j}-\widetilde{\mu},c\right\rangle^{2}+3\left\|c\right\|_{2}^{4}\Bigg\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{3}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle Z_{i,j}-\overline{Y},c\right\rangle^{2}+\frac{3}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle v_{i,j}-\widetilde{\mu},c\right\rangle^{2}+3\left\|c\right\|_{2}^{4}\Bigg\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(81)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p15.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p15.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the second and the third step follow from the linearity of inner product and the last step follows from Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem5" title="Fact A.5. ‣ A.1 Sum-of-squares ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a>.
In particular, considering the first term of Eq. (<a href="#A4.Ex296" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">81</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx168" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex300"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex300.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{6}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:9.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="9.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">6</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="9.0pt"><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mpadded></mpadded><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{6}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex300.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{3}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle Z_{i,j}-\overline{Y},c\right\rangle^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{3}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle Z_{i,j}-\overline{Y},c\right\rangle^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex301"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex301.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex301.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{6}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle Z_{i,j}-\overline{Z},c\right\rangle^{2}+\frac{6}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle\overline{Z}-\overline{Y},c\right\rangle^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{6}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle Z_{i,j}-\overline{Z},c\right\rangle^{2}+\frac{6}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle\overline{Z}-\overline{Y},c\right\rangle^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex302"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex302.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex302.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~6c^{\top}\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left(Z_{i,j}-\overline{Z}\right)\left(Z_{i,j}-\overline{Z}\right)^{\top}c+\frac{6}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle\overline{Z}-\overline{Y},c\right\rangle^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~6c^{\top}\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left(Z_{i,j}-\overline{Z}\right)\left(Z_{i,j}-\overline{Z}\right)^{\top}c+\frac{6}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle\overline{Z}-\overline{Y},c\right\rangle^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex303"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex303.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex303.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~12\left\|c\right\|_{2}^{2}+\frac{6}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle\overline{Z}-\overline{Y},c\right\rangle^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~12\left\|c\right\|_{2}^{2}+\frac{6}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle\overline{Z}-\overline{Y},c\right\rangle^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex304"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex304.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex304.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|c\right\|_{2}^{2}\left(12+\frac{6}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\|\overline{Z}-\overline{Y}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|c\right\|_{2}^{2}\left(12+\frac{6}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\|\overline{Z}-\overline{Y}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E82.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~12\left\|c\right\|_{2}^{2}\left(1+\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|c\right\|_{2}^{2}\right)\Bigg\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>12</mn><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~12\left\|c\right\|_{2}^{2}\left(1+\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|c\right\|_{2}^{2}\right)\Bigg\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(82)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p15.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p15.4.1" class="ltx_text">where the second step follows from the definition of the inner product, the third step follows from our polynomial constraint (see Eq. (<a href="#A4.E49" title="Equation 49 ‣ Definition D.2 (Polynomial system 𝖡). ‣ Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a>)) and Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Fact A.2 (SoS operator norm, Claim 2.7 in []). ‣ A.1 Sum-of-squares ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, the fourth step follows from the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality (see Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Fact A.1 (SoS Cauchy-Schwarz, Claim 2.6 in []). ‣ A.1 Sum-of-squares ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>), and the last step follows from the triangle inequality.
Considering the second term of Eq. (<a href="#A4.Ex296" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">81</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx169" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex305"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex305.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{2}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\frac{3}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle v_{i,j}-\widetilde{\mu},c\right\rangle^{2}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:9.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="9.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">2</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="9.0pt"><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{2}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\frac{3}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle v_{i,j}-\widetilde{\mu},c\right\rangle^{2}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex305.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~3c^{\top}\Sigma_{v}c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~3c^{\top}\Sigma_{v}c</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E83.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~6\left\|c\right\|_{2}^{2}\Bigg\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~6\left\|c\right\|_{2}^{2}\Bigg\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(83)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p15.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p15.5.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from the definition of <math id="A4.SS4.p15.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Eq. (<a href="#A4.E67" title="Equation 67 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">67</span></a>)).
Combining Eq. (<a href="#A4.Ex296" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">81</span></a>), Eq. (<a href="#A4.Ex300" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">82</span></a>), and Eq. (<a href="#A4.Ex305" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">83</span></a>), we can bound the second part of Eq. (<a href="#A4.Ex280" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">79</span></a>) as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx170" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E84.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{6}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j},c\right\rangle^{2}\leq 12\left\|c\right\|_{2}^{2}\left(1.5+\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+1.25\left\|c\right\|_{2}^{2}\right)\Bigg\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:9.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="9.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">6</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="9.0pt"><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>12</mn><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1.5</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>1.25</mn><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{6}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\frac{1}{Nn}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\left\langle Z_{i,j}-v_{i,j},c\right\rangle^{2}\leq 12\left\|c\right\|_{2}^{2}\left(1.5+\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+1.25\left\|c\right\|_{2}^{2}\right)\Bigg\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(84)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, combining Eq. (<a href="#A4.Ex287" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">80</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A4.E84" title="Equation 84 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">84</span></a>), we can bound the Eq. (<a href="#A4.Ex280" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">79</span></a>) as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx171" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E85.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{6}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:9.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="9.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">6</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="9.0pt"><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mpadded></mpadded><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{6}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E85.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~2\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i}\left\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\rangle\right)^{2}\leq 12\alpha\left\|c\right\|_{2}^{2}\left(6+4\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+5\left\|c\right\|_{2}^{2}\right)\Bigg\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>α</mi><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~2\left(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}U_{i}\mathcal{I}_{i}\left\langle Y_{i}-\widetilde{\mu}_{i},\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\rangle\right)^{2}\leq 12\alpha\left\|c\right\|_{2}^{2}\left(6+4\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+5\left\|c\right\|_{2}^{2}\right)\Bigg\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(85)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">Combining the bounds of both terms (Eq. (<a href="#A4.E76" title="Equation 76 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">76</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A4.E85" title="Equation 85 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">85</span></a>)) of Eq. (<a href="#A4.E69" title="Equation 69 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">69</span></a>) together, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx172" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex306"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex306.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{6}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:9.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="9.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">6</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="9.0pt"><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{6}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Y}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex306.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~12\varepsilon\left(4\left(\frac{1}{n}+\tau\right)\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~12\varepsilon\left(4\left(\frac{1}{n}+\tau\right)\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E86.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle~12\alpha\left(6\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+4\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+5\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)\Bigg\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>12</mn><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>6</mn><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~12\alpha\left(6\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+4\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+5\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)\Bigg\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(86)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#A2.SS1" title="B.1 Accurate Estimation of the Empirical Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, by choosing <math id="A4.SS4.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi=\xi=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi=\xi=1</annotation></semantics></math> and taking <math id="A4.SS4.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon+\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon+\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> as the given level of corruption, we also have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx173" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E87.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{6}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Z}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\leq\frac{20(\varepsilon+\alpha)}{3}\left(4\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)\Bigg\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖡</mi><mpadded voffset="3.4pt"><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:0.5pt;height:12.9pt;position:relative; bottom:-6.5pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mtext class="ltx_markedasmath"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_markedasmath" style="width:9.0pt;height:0.5pt;position:relative; bottom:-0.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></mtext><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="-6.5pt" width="9.0pt"><mn mathsize="0.700em">6</mn></mpadded><mpadded style="width:9.0pt;" voffset="2.0pt" width="9.0pt"><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.700em">Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mpadded></mpadded><mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{B}\mathrel{\hbox{\raisebox{3.44444pt}{$\rule[-6.45831pt]{0.47787pt}{12.91663pt}\rule[-0.23894pt]{8.99995pt}{0.47787pt}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{-6.47223pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{6}$}}}\hskip-8.99995pt\raisebox{1.96112pt}{\makebox[8.99995pt]{\hbox{$\scriptstyle{\overline{Z}}$}}}$}}}\Bigg\{\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\leq\frac{20(\varepsilon+\alpha)}{3}\left(4\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)\Bigg\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(87)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we consider the bound on the pseudoexpectation of Eq. (<a href="#A4.Ex306" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">86</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx174" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex307"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex307.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex308"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex308.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex308.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[12\varepsilon\left(4\left(\frac{1}{n}+\tau\right)\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)+12\alpha\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\left(6+4\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+5\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[12\varepsilon\left(4\left(\frac{1}{n}+\tau\right)\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)+12\alpha\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\left(6+4\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+5\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex309"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex309.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex309.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~12\varepsilon\left(4\left(\frac{1}{n}+\tau\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]+\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~12\varepsilon\left(4\left(\frac{1}{n}+\tau\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]+\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E88.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~12\alpha\left(6\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]+4\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]+5\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~12\alpha\left(6\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]+4\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]+5\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(88)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p18.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p18.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second step follows from the linearity of pseudoexpectation (see Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem6" title="Fact A.6 (Linearity of Pseudoexpectation). ‣ A.2 Pseudo-expectation properties ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a>).
In particular, by Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem7" title="Fact A.7 (Cauchy Schwarz for Pseudoexpectation, Fact 3.10 in []). ‣ A.2 Pseudo-expectation properties ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx175" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]\leq\sqrt{\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]}\sqrt{\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]\leq\sqrt{\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]}\sqrt{\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(89)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">Considering <math id="A4.SS4.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>, by Eq. (<a href="#A4.E87" title="Equation 87 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">87</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx176" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex310"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex310.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex310.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\frac{20\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)}{3}\left(4\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\frac{20\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)}{3}\left(4\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex311"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex311.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex311.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{20(\varepsilon+\alpha)}{3}\left(4\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]+\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{20(\varepsilon+\alpha)}{3}\left(4\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]+\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p19.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p19.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the first step follows from Eq. (<a href="#A4.E87" title="Equation 87 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">87</span></a>) and the second step follows from the linearity of pseudoexpectation (see Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem6" title="Fact A.6 (Linearity of Pseudoexpectation). ‣ A.2 Pseudo-expectation properties ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a>).
This implies that, with <math id="A4.SS4.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon+\alpha&lt;\frac{1}{10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon+\alpha&lt;\frac{1}{10}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx177" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex312"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex312.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(1-\frac{20(\varepsilon+\alpha)}{3}\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(1-\frac{20(\varepsilon+\alpha)}{3}\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex312.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 4\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 4\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex313"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex313.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex313.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{4}{1-\frac{20(\varepsilon+\alpha)}{3}}\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{4}{1-\frac{20(\varepsilon+\alpha)}{3}}\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx178" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E90"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]=O\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]=O\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(90)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">By <span id="A4.SS4.p21.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 1</span> of Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem8" title="Fact A.8. ‣ A.2 Pseudo-expectation properties ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a>, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx179" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex314"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex314.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]^{2}\leq\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0.1389em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]^{2}\leq\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p21.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p21.2.1" class="ltx_text">so that combining with Eq. (<a href="#A4.E90" title="Equation 90 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">90</span></a>) gives us</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx180" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]\leq O\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]\leq O\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(91)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p21.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p21.3.1" class="ltx_text">Furthermore, combining Eq. (<a href="#A4.E91" title="Equation 91 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">91</span></a>) with Eq. (<a href="#A4.E90" title="Equation 90 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">90</span></a>) again implies</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx181" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E92"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]}\leq\sqrt{O\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)\cdot O\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)}=O\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Z}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]}\leq\sqrt{O\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)\cdot O\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)}=O\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(92)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, combining Eq. (<a href="#A4.Ex307" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">88</span></a>), Eq. (<a href="#A4.E92" title="Equation 92 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">92</span></a>), and Eq. (<a href="#A4.E89" title="Equation 89 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">89</span></a>) together, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx182" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex315"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex315.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex316"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex316.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex316.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~12\varepsilon\left(4\left(\frac{1}{n}+\tau\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]+\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~12\varepsilon\left(4\left(\frac{1}{n}+\tau\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]+\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex317"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex317.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex317.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~12\alpha\left(6\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]+O\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)\sqrt{\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]}+5\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~12\alpha\left(6\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]+O\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)\sqrt{\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]}+5\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex318"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex318.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex318.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left(\frac{48\varepsilon}{n}+48\varepsilon\tau+72\alpha\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]+\left(12\varepsilon+60\alpha\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]+O\left(\alpha\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)\right)\sqrt{\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>48</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>48</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>72</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left(\frac{48\varepsilon}{n}+48\varepsilon\tau+72\alpha\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]+\left(12\varepsilon+60\alpha\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]+O\left(\alpha\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)\right)\sqrt{\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex319"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex319.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex319.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left(\frac{48\varepsilon}{n}+120\alpha\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]+\left(12\varepsilon+60\alpha\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]+O\left(\alpha\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)\right)\sqrt{\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>48</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>120</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left(\frac{48\varepsilon}{n}+120\alpha\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]+\left(12\varepsilon+60\alpha\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]+O\left(\alpha\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)\right)\sqrt{\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p22.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p22.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the last step follows from the definition of <math id="A4.SS4.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\frac{\alpha}{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\frac{\alpha}{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> (Definition <a href="#A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="Algorithmic design. ‣ D.2 Algorithmic Design and Proof Overview ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>),
so with <math id="A4.SS4.p22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&lt;\frac{1}{18}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>18</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&lt;\frac{1}{18}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS4.p22.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&lt;\frac{1}{90}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>90</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&lt;\frac{1}{90}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS4.p22.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon+5\alpha&lt;\frac{1}{18}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>18</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon+5\alpha&lt;\frac{1}{18}</annotation></semantics></math>, we subtract <math id="A4.SS4.p22.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(12\varepsilon+60\alpha\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(12\varepsilon+60\alpha\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> from both sides of the inequality and make each side divided by <math id="A4.SS4.p22.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\left(12\varepsilon+60\alpha\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\left(12\varepsilon+60\alpha\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, so we can get</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx183" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex320"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex320.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex320.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{n}+\alpha\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]+O\left(\alpha\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)\right)\sqrt{\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{n}+\alpha\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]+O\left(\alpha\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)\right)\sqrt{\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A4.SS4.p23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b:=O\left(\alpha\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b:=O\left(\alpha\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS4.p23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c:=O\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{n}+\alpha\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c:=O\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{n}+\alpha\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS4.p23.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x:=\sqrt{\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x:=\sqrt{\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]}</annotation></semantics></math>. To make <math id="A4.SS4.p23.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{2}-bx-c\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{2}-bx-c\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we need</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx184" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex321"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex321.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{b-\sqrt{b^{2}+4c}}{2}\leq x\leq\frac{b+\sqrt{b^{2}+4c}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{b-\sqrt{b^{2}+4c}}{2}\leq x\leq\frac{b+\sqrt{b^{2}+4c}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p23.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p23.2.1" class="ltx_text">so that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx185" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex322"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex322.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x^{2}\leq\max\left\{\left(\frac{b-\sqrt{b^{2}+4c}}{2}\right)^{2},\left(\frac{b+\sqrt{b^{2}+4c}}{2}\right)^{2}\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x^{2}\leq\max\left\{\left(\frac{b-\sqrt{b^{2}+4c}}{2}\right)^{2},\left(\frac{b+\sqrt{b^{2}+4c}}{2}\right)^{2}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p23.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p23.3.1" class="ltx_text">By the definition of <math id="A4.SS4.p23.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b,c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b,c</annotation></semantics></math>, we know that <math id="A4.SS4.p23.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b,\sqrt{b^{2}+4c}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b,\sqrt{b^{2}+4c}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, so</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx186" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex323"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex323.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max\left\{\left(\frac{b-\sqrt{b^{2}+4c}}{2}\right)^{2},\left(\frac{b+\sqrt{b^{2}+4c}}{2}\right)^{2}\right\}=\left(\frac{b+\sqrt{b^{2}+4c}}{2}\right)^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max\left\{\left(\frac{b-\sqrt{b^{2}+4c}}{2}\right)^{2},\left(\frac{b+\sqrt{b^{2}+4c}}{2}\right)^{2}\right\}=\left(\frac{b+\sqrt{b^{2}+4c}}{2}\right)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p23.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p23.4.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx187" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex324"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex324.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex324.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left(\frac{O\left(\alpha\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)\right)+\sqrt{O\left(\alpha\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)\right)^{2}+O\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{n}+\alpha\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]}}{2}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left(\frac{O\left(\alpha\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)\right)+\sqrt{O\left(\alpha\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)\right)^{2}+O\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{n}+\alpha\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]}}{2}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex325"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex325.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex325.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\alpha^{2}\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)^{2}\right)+O\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{n}+\alpha\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\alpha^{2}\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)^{2}\right)+O\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{n}+\alpha\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p23.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p23.5.1" class="ltx_text">Since, by <span id="A4.SS4.p23.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 1</span> of Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem8" title="Fact A.8. ‣ A.2 Pseudo-expectation properties ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx188" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex326"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex326.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]\geq\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0.1389em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{4}\right]\geq\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p23.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p23.6.1" class="ltx_text">we can get</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx189" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex327"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex327.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]^{2}-O\left(\alpha^{2}\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)^{2}\right)-O\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{n}+\alpha\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]\leq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]^{2}-O\left(\alpha^{2}\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)^{2}\right)-O\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{n}+\alpha\right)\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]\leq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p23.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p23.7.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, we can get</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx190" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex328"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex328.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex328.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\frac{O\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{n}+\alpha\right)+\sqrt{O\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{n}+\alpha\right)^{2}+O\left(\alpha^{2}\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)^{2}\right)}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\frac{O\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{n}+\alpha\right)+\sqrt{O\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{n}+\alpha\right)^{2}+O\left(\alpha^{2}\left(\varepsilon+\alpha\right)^{2}\right)}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex329"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex329.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex329.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{n}+\alpha+\varepsilon\alpha+\alpha^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{n}+\alpha+\varepsilon\alpha+\alpha^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex330"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex330.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex330.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{n}+\alpha\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{n}+\alpha\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p24" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text">In addition, by <span id="A4.SS4.p24.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part 3</span> of Fact <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem8" title="Fact A.8. ‣ A.2 Pseudo-expectation properties ‣ Appendix A Additional Preliminaries ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx191" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex331"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex331.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\widetilde{\E}\left[\overline{Y}\right]-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\widetilde{\E}\left[\overline{Y}\right]-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex331.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\widetilde{\E}\left[\left\|\overline{Y}-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E93"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E93.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{n}+\alpha\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{n}+\alpha\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(93)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p25" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p25.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p25.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that our empirical mean <math id="A4.SS4.p25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> is computed via <math id="A4.SS4.p25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Nn" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Nn</annotation></semantics></math> clean samples, so putting this inside Claim <a href="#A2.SS2.SSS2.Px2" title="Proof overview. ‣ B.2.2 The Existence of a Stable Set ‣ B.2 From the Empirical Mean to the True Mean ‣ Appendix B Robust Mean Estimation Via SoS ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2.2</span></a>, we can get with probability <math id="A4.SS4.p25.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx192" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E94"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\widetilde{\mu}-\mu\right\|_{2}^{2}\leq O\left(\alpha\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\widetilde{\mu}-\mu\right\|_{2}^{2}\leq O\left(\alpha\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(94)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p25.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p25.2.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="A4.SS4.p25.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Nn\geq\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Nn\geq\Omega\left(\frac{d}{\alpha}\log\left(d/\delta\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p26" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p26.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p26.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we can bound the output of the SoS algorithm with the true mean <math id="A4.SS4.p26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx193" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex332"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex332.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\widetilde{\E}\left[\overline{Y}\right]-\mu\right\|_{2}^{2}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\widetilde{\E}\left[\overline{Y}\right]-\mu\right\|_{2}^{2}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex332.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\left\|\widetilde{\E}\left[\overline{Y}\right]-\widetilde{\mu}+\widetilde{\mu}-\mu\right\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\left\|\widetilde{\E}\left[\overline{Y}\right]-\widetilde{\mu}+\widetilde{\mu}-\mu\right\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex333"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex333.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex333.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~2\left\|\widetilde{\E}\left[\overline{Y}\right]-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+2\left\|\widetilde{\mu}-\mu\right\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo lspace="0em">𝔼</mo><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~2\left\|\widetilde{\E}\left[\overline{Y}\right]-\widetilde{\mu}\right\|_{2}^{2}+2\left\|\widetilde{\mu}-\mu\right\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex334"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex334.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex334.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{n}+\alpha\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~O\left(\frac{\varepsilon}{n}+\alpha\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p26.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p26.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second step follows from the triangle inequality and the third step follows from combining Eq. (<a href="#A4.Ex331" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">93</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A4.E94" title="Equation 94 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.4 Identifiability ‣ Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">94</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Adaptive Collaborative Mean Estimation Under Unknown Corruption</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> users, each contributing <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=o(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=o(d)</annotation></semantics></math> samples in <math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
An <math id="A5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of users may be arbitrary (user-level adversaries).
For the remaining users (the “good” ones), consider two canonical variants:</p>
<ul id="A5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part A.</span> Each good user <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> has i.i.d. data with mean <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and covariance <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{i}\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⪯</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{i}\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and satisfies <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mu_{i}-\mu\|_{2}^{2}\leq\alpha^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mu_{i}-\mu\|_{2}^{2}\leq\alpha^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> for a common target mean <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part B.</span> Each good user contributes <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples of which at most an <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction are adversarial (strong contamination), and the clean samples have covariance <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⪯</mo><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\preceq\mathbb{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In both parts, the true parameters <math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{*},\alpha^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{*},\alpha^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> are unknown to the algorithm.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem E.1</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose we have two unknown parameters <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
With additional <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Nn=o\left(d\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Nn=o\left(d\right)</annotation></semantics></math> clean samples,</span></p>
<ul id="A5.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A5.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">in equivalent model of Problem </span><a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Problem 1.1 (Mean shift). ‣ Mean Shift Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a><span id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, where </span><math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{*}\in\left(0,0.1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{*}\in\left(0,0.1\right)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the fraction of corrupted user and </span><math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{*}\in\left(0,0.1\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{*}\in\left(0,0.1\right)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the quality of good batches, there exists a polynomial-time algorithm that returns </span><math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfying, with probability at least </span><math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,
</span><math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\widehat{\mu}-\mu\|_{2}\leq O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon^{*}}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha^{*}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\widehat{\mu}-\mu\|_{2}\leq O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon^{*}}{n}}+\sqrt{\alpha^{*}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">in equivalent model of Problem </span><a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Problem 1.2 (Adversarial). ‣ Adversarial Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a><span id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, where </span><math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{*}\in\left(0,\frac{1}{18}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>18</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{*}\in\left(0,\frac{1}{18}\right)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the fraction of corrupted user and </span><math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{*}\in\left(0,\frac{1}{90}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>90</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{*}\in\left(0,\frac{1}{90}\right)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the fraction of corrupted samples within each uncorrupted user, there exists a polynomial-time algorithm that returns </span><math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfying, with probability at least </span><math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,
</span><math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\widehat{\mu}-\mu\|_{2}\leq O\left(\sqrt{\alpha^{*}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\widehat{\mu}-\mu\|_{2}\leq O\left(\sqrt{\alpha^{*}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.
Similarly, if </span><math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{*}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{*}=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then our </span><math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfies </span><math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\widehat{\mu}-\mu\|_{2}\leq O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon^{*}}{n}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mfrac><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\widehat{\mu}-\mu\|_{2}\leq O\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon^{*}}{n}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Both rates are minimax-optimal up to constant factors.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Even a small number of clean samples from a user can be leveraged to <em id="A5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">verify</em> the accuracy of the estimated mean. This verification step enables the user to <em id="A5.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">adaptively adjust</em> to the effective level of corruption relevant to their own distribution—allowing for personalized robustness that naturally reflects user-specific data quality.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Although <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite> also removed the need to know the corruption level by combining estimates obtained at multiple guessed parameters, it inherently yields only a constant-factor approximation and incurs repeated estimator runs. Tolerant testing instead offers an absolute certification of accuracy using a small number of clean samples, allowing the algorithm to adaptively stop at the optimal rate for the true corruption level and achieve minimax-optimal error without post-hoc aggregation. It can further returns the unknown <math id="A5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Moreover, the algorithm succeeds via a logarithmic search over candidate
<math id="A5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> (and, if needed, <math id="A5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>), where each guess is certified by a tolerant mean tester;
the number of guesses is
<math id="A5.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\left(\log\frac{\varepsilon_{0}}{\max\left\{\varepsilon^{*},\sqrt{\frac{d}{Nn}}\right\}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\left(\log\frac{\varepsilon_{0}}{\max\left\{\varepsilon^{*},\sqrt{\frac{d}{Nn}}\right\}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> in the base routine.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For <span id="A5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part A</span>, we run the user-mean SoS program from Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1 (Mean shift). ‣ 2 Main Results ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> on a geometric sequence of guesses
<math id="A5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0},\varepsilon_{0}/2,\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0},\varepsilon_{0}/2,\ldots</annotation></semantics></math>; for each successful SoS solution, validate the candidate mean using the tolerant tester
from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> (which estimates <math id="A5.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mu\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mu\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> from two halves and distinguishes scales with
<math id="A5.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="nN=\widetilde{O}\left(\sqrt{d}/\tau^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">nN=\widetilde{O}\left(\sqrt{d}/\tau^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> at tolerance <math id="A5.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>). The SoS soundness in Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1 (Mean shift). ‣ 2 Main Results ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> yields the error</p>
<table id="A5.EGx194" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex335"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex335.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widetilde{O}\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon/n}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widetilde{O}\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon/n}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p6.2" class="ltx_p">whenever the guessed <math id="A5.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varepsilon,\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varepsilon,\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> dominate
<math id="A5.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varepsilon^{*},\alpha^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varepsilon^{*},\alpha^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>; the tester guarantees we stop near the smallest valid guess, thus achieving the same
rate with <math id="A5.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varepsilon,\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varepsilon,\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> replaced by <math id="A5.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varepsilon^{*},\alpha^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varepsilon^{*},\alpha^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> and high probability by the strengthened
high-probability stability (see Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1 (Mean shift). ‣ 2 Main Results ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> and its bound, and the user-mean SoS triangle-inequality
conclusion).</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p7.1" class="ltx_p">For <span id="A5.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Part B</span>, we use the two-level SoS system (sample- and user-level constraints) and apply the same unknown-<math id="A5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>
search plus validation. The identifiability analysis of <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Learning From Corrupted Batches With Fractional User Data Corruption ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a> gives</p>
<table id="A5.EGx195" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex336"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex336.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon/n}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle O\left(\sqrt{\varepsilon/n}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p7.2" class="ltx_p">the search-and-test wrapper again adapts to the
unknown <math id="A5.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varepsilon^{*},\alpha^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varepsilon^{*},\alpha^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> with high probability.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p8.1" class="ltx_p">With the initial guess <math id="A5.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}\in\left(0,\frac{1}{18}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>18</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}\in\left(0,\frac{1}{18}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{t+1}=\frac{1}{2}\varepsilon_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{t+1}=\frac{1}{2}\varepsilon_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the iteration bound</p>
<table id="A5.EGx196" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex337"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex337.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle O\left(\log\frac{\varepsilon_{0}}{\max\left\{\varepsilon^{*},\sqrt{\frac{d}{Nn}}\right\}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle O\left(\log\frac{\varepsilon_{0}}{\max\left\{\varepsilon^{*},\sqrt{\frac{d}{Nn}}\right\}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Also, with the initial guess <math id="A5.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{0}\in\left(0,\frac{1}{90}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>90</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{0}\in\left(0,\frac{1}{90}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t+1}=\frac{1}{2}\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t+1}=\frac{1}{2}\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the iteration bound</p>
<table id="A5.EGx197" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex338"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex338.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle O\left(\log\frac{\alpha_{0}}{\max\left\{\alpha^{*},\sqrt{\frac{d}{Nn}}\right\}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle O\left(\log\frac{\alpha_{0}}{\max\left\{\alpha^{*},\sqrt{\frac{d}{Nn}}\right\}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Hardness</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present the proof of the lower bound of our main results (<a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1 (Mean shift). ‣ 2 Main Results ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorems</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> and <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2.2 (Adversarial). ‣ 2 Main Results ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>). Specifically, in <a href="#A6.SS1" title="F.1 Hardness of Problem ‣ Appendix F Hardness ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.1</span></a>, we present the lower bound of <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1 (Mean shift). ‣ 2 Main Results ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>. In <a href="#A6.SS2" title="F.2 Hardness of Problem ‣ Appendix F Hardness ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.2</span></a>, we present the lower bound of <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2.2 (Adversarial). ‣ 2 Main Results ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>. In <a href="#A6.SS3" title="F.3 Permutation Invariant ‣ Appendix F Hardness ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3</span></a>, we introduce permutation invariant.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Hardness of Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Problem 1.1 (Mean shift). ‣ Mean Shift Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A6.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem F.1</span></span><span id="A6.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the model in Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem1" title="Problem 1.1 (Mean shift). ‣ Mean Shift Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>.
Then there exists a choice of uncorrupted user distributions <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{D}_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{D}_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and an <math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-user adversary such that for any estimator
<math id="A6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx198" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex339"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex339.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[\|\widehat{\mu}-\mu\|_{2}\geq\Omega\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\frac{d}{nN}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)\right]\geq\frac{1}{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[\|\widehat{\mu}-\mu\|_{2}\geq\Omega\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\frac{d}{nN}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)\right]\geq\frac{1}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">It follows from Lemma <a href="#A6.SS2.SSS1" title="F.2.1 The Case When 𝛼=0 ‣ F.2 Hardness of Problem ‣ Appendix F Hardness ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.2.1</span></a>. The <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(\sqrt{\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(\sqrt{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math> lower bound is straightforward: suppose the true mean is <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, for all users, the adversary could simply change the mean to some <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> that is <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> apart, and no algorithms could tell whether the true mean is <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Hardness of Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Problem 1.2 (Adversarial). ‣ Adversarial Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A6.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem F.2</span></span><span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in\left(0,\frac{1}{18}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>18</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in\left(0,\frac{1}{18}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\left(0,\frac{1}{90}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>90</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\left(0,\frac{1}{90}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon+5\alpha&lt;\frac{1}{18}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>18</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon+5\alpha&lt;\frac{1}{18}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=o(d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=o(d)</annotation></semantics></math> samples from each of <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> users, there exists an instance of Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Problem 1.2 (Adversarial). ‣ Adversarial Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a>—consisting of a choice of uncorrupted data distributions with mean <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and a choice of adversarial corruptions—such that for any estimator <math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\widehat{\mu}-\mu\right\|_{2}=\Omega\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\frac{d}{nN}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\widehat{\mu}-\mu\right\|_{2}=\Omega\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}+\sqrt{\frac{d}{nN}}+\sqrt{\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">It follows from combining Lemma <a href="#A6.SS2.SSS1" title="F.2.1 The Case When 𝛼=0 ‣ F.2 Hardness of Problem ‣ Appendix F Hardness ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.2.1</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#A6.SS2.SSS2" title="F.2.2 The Case When 𝜀=0 ‣ F.2 Hardness of Problem ‣ Appendix F Hardness ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.2.2</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">F.2.1 </span>The Case When <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSS1.2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma F.3</span></span><span id="A6.SS2.SSS1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the setting of Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Problem 1.2 (Adversarial). ‣ Adversarial Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a> with <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in(0,\frac{1}{18})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>18</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in(0,\frac{1}{18})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there exist two hypotheses <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0},H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0},H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> over
<math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Var}(H_{0}),\text{Var}(H_{1})\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Var}(H_{0}),\text{Var}(H_{1})\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\mu_{H_{0}}-\mu_{H_{1}}\right|=\Omega\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\mu_{H_{0}}-\mu_{H_{1}}\right|=\Omega\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>,
such that under the <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-user corruption model the induced distributions of the
<em id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">observed</em> samples are identical.
Consequently, for all estimator <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx199" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex340"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex340.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[\|\widetilde{\mu}-\mu\|_{2}\geq\Omega\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}\right)\right]\geq\frac{1}{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[\|\widetilde{\mu}-\mu\|_{2}\geq\Omega\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}\right)\right]\geq\frac{1}{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for at least one of the two hypotheses.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We consider the case <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0</annotation></semantics></math>, so there is no within-user corruption.
Fix <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}:=\varepsilon/n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}:=\varepsilon/n</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider a one-dimensional random variable
<math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> with</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx200" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex341"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex341.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[X=0\right]=1-\varepsilon_{0}\quad\text{and}\quad\Pr\left[X=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\varepsilon_{0}}}\right]=\varepsilon_{0}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mtext>and</mtext><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[X=0\right]=1-\varepsilon_{0}\quad\text{and}\quad\Pr\left[X=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\varepsilon_{0}}}\right]=\varepsilon_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">We use <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> as a hypothesis or distribution that satisfy this. We use <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> as a hypothesis or distribution that satisfy <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Under <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx201" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex342"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex342.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu_{H_{0}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu_{H_{0}}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex342.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\mathbb{E}\left[X\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\mathbb{E}\left[X\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex343"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex343.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex343.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\varepsilon_{0}\cdot\frac{1}{\sqrt{\varepsilon_{0}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\varepsilon_{0}\cdot\frac{1}{\sqrt{\varepsilon_{0}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex344"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex344.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex344.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sqrt{\varepsilon_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sqrt{\varepsilon_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex345"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex345.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex345.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Additionally, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx202" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex346"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex346.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[X^{2}]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[X^{2}]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex346.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\varepsilon_{0}\cdot\frac{1}{\varepsilon_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\varepsilon_{0}\cdot\frac{1}{\varepsilon_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex347"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex347.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex347.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx203" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex348"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex348.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}\left[X\right]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}\left[X\right]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex348.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\mathbb{E}[X^{2}]-\mu_{H_{0}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\mathbb{E}[X^{2}]-\mu_{H_{0}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex349"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex349.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex349.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~1-\varepsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~1-\varepsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex350"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex350.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex350.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Under <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}\left[Y\right]=0\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}\left[Y\right]=0\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus both <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy the bounded-variance assumption.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">In our model with user-level corruption <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, the adversary may arbitrarily
modify all the samples coming from an <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of the users.
Under <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, each user draws <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> i.i.d. copies of <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. In expectation there
are <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}n=\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}n=\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> non-zero samples per user, and these are exactly the
points that distinguish <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where all samples are identically
zero. By corrupting entire users whose batches contain any non-zero sample and replacing them by <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>,
the adversary can transform the <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> instance into one that is
<em id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p7.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">identically distributed</em> to the <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> instance (all observed samples are
zero in either case). Therefore, no algorithm can distinguish <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>
with probability better than <math id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">However, since</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx204" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex351"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex351.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{H_{0}}-\mu_{H_{1}}\right\|_{2}=\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\mu_{H_{0}}-\mu_{H_{1}}\right\|_{2}=\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">we have that every estimator suffers worst-case error</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx205" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex352"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex352.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\widetilde{\mu}-\mu\right\|_{2}\geq\Omega\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\widetilde{\mu}-\mu\right\|_{2}\geq\Omega\left(\sqrt{\frac{\varepsilon}{n}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">F.2.2 </span>The Case When <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=0</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSS2.2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS2.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma F.4</span></span><span id="A6.SS2.SSS2.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the setting of Problem <a href="#S1.Thmtheorem2" title="Problem 1.2 (Adversarial). ‣ Adversarial Model. ‣ 1.1 Problem Setup ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ High-Dimensional Robust Mean Estimation with Untrusted Batches" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.2</span></a> with <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=0</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\left(0,\frac{1}{90}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>90</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\left(0,\frac{1}{90}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then there exist two hypotheses <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{2},H_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{2},H_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Var}(H_{2}),\text{Var}(H_{3})\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Var}(H_{2}),\text{Var}(H_{3})\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|\mu_{H_{2}}-\mu_{H_{3}}\right|=\Omega\left(\sqrt{\alpha}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|\mu_{H_{2}}-\mu_{H_{3}}\right|=\Omega\left(\sqrt{\alpha}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>,
such that the induced distributions of the observed samples are identical under the <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction within user corruption. Consequently, for any estimator <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx206" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex353"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex353.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[\|\widetilde{\mu}-\mu\|_{2}\geq\Omega\left(\sqrt{\alpha}\right)\right]\geq\frac{1}{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[\|\widetilde{\mu}-\mu\|_{2}\geq\Omega\left(\sqrt{\alpha}\right)\right]\geq\frac{1}{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for at least one of the two hypotheses.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, we consider the case where <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">There are no fully corrupted users,
but each (good) user may have an <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction of corrupted samples.
Again we work in one dimension and define</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx207" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex354"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex354.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr[X=0]=1-\alpha\qquad\text{and}\qquad\Pr\left[X=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha}}\right]=\alpha." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mtext>and</mtext><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr[X=0]=1-\alpha\qquad\text{and}\qquad\Pr\left[X=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha}}\right]=\alpha.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, we use <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> as a hypothesis or distribution that satisfy this. We use <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> as a hypothesis or distribution
that satisfy <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can bound their variance as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx208" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex355"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex355.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu_{H_{2}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu_{H_{2}}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex355.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\mathbb{E}[X]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\mathbb{E}[X]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex356"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex356.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex356.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\alpha\cdot\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\alpha\cdot\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex357"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex357.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex357.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\sqrt{\alpha}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\sqrt{\alpha}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Also, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx209" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex358"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex358.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[X^{2}]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[X^{2}]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex358.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~\alpha\cdot\frac{1}{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~\alpha\cdot\frac{1}{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex359"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex359.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex359.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle~1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle~1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">so</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx210" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex360"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex360.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}\left[X\right]=1-\alpha\leq 1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}\left[X\right]=1-\alpha\leq 1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Under <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> we again have <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}\left[Y\right]=0\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}\left[Y\right]=0\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> also satisfies the variance bound.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let a (good) user draw <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> i.i.d. samples <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},\ldots,X_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},\ldots,X_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> from the
distribution in <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx211" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex361"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex361.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle T:=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{j}\neq 0\right\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>:=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mn>𝟙</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T:=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\mathds{1}_{\left\{X_{j}\neq 0\right\}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">be the number of non-zero samples. Therefore, we can see that <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\sim\mathrm{Bin}(n,\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Bin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\sim\mathrm{Bin}(n,\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies
<math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[T]=\alpha n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[T]=\alpha n</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the Chernoff bound, we can get that for all <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx212" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex362"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex362.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[T\geq(1+\delta)\alpha n\right]\leq\exp\left(-\frac{\delta^{2}}{2+\delta}\alpha n\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>α</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[T\geq(1+\delta)\alpha n\right]\leq\exp\left(-\frac{\delta^{2}}{2+\delta}\alpha n\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Choosing <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=2</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx213" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex363"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex363.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Pr\left[T\geq 3\alpha n\right]\leq\exp\left(-\alpha n\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>α</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Pr\left[T\geq 3\alpha n\right]\leq\exp\left(-\alpha n\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we can get that with high probability, every good user has at most <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\alpha n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\alpha n)</annotation></semantics></math> non-zero samples.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider an adversary that is allowed to corrupt an <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-fraction
of each user’s samples. Under <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, each user draws <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> samples from the
distribution above; the non-zero samples are exactly those that distinguish
<math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, where all samples are zero. On the typical event that a user
has at most <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\alpha n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\alpha n</annotation></semantics></math> non-zero samples, the adversary can change all of these
to <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, staying within the <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha n</annotation></semantics></math> corruption budget up to constants.
Consequently, after corruption the distribution of the observed samples under
<math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is identical to that under <math id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> (all zeros), and no algorithm can
distinguish the two hypotheses.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx214" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex364"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex364.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\widetilde{\mu}-\mu\right\|_{2}\geq\Omega\left(\sqrt{\alpha}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\widetilde{\mu}-\mu\right\|_{2}\geq\Omega\left(\sqrt{\alpha}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.SSS2.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3 </span>Permutation Invariant</h3>

<div id="A6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Under our two-level corruption model, an adversary first selects a subset of
<math id="A6.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon N</annotation></semantics></math> users to corrupt and, for each uncorrupted user, a subset of
<math id="A6.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha n</annotation></semantics></math> samples to corrupt. A priori, the adversary may choose these
subsets in an arbitrary way, leading to a
complicated pattern of corrupted entries in the <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math>-th entry <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">However, if the estimator is permutation invariant, then only the counts of corrupted users and corrupted samples matter, not their specific indices.
Consequently, we may equivalently consider a symmetrized case in which
the adversary first fixes an arbitrary corruption pattern and we then apply a
uniform random permutation <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> to the users and independent uniform random
permutations <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\sigma_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\sigma_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> to the samples within each user. From the point of
view of a permutation-invariant estimator, this symmetrized case is
identical to the original one.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In particular, after this random symmetrization, the distribution of each entry
<math id="A6.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> is the same across all <math id="A6.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A6.Ex365" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex365.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i,j}\sim\begin{cases}P_{0},&amp;\text{with probability }1-\rho,\\[5.69054pt]
Q,&amp;\text{with probability }\rho,\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>with probability </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>with probability </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i,j}\sim\begin{cases}P_{0},&amp;\text{with probability }1-\rho,\\[5.69054pt]
Q,&amp;\text{with probability }\rho,\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">for some contamination rate <math id="A6.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> that depends only on <math id="A6.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\varepsilon,\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\varepsilon,\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>
and on whether we are in the user-level or sample-level corruption regime.
Under the hypothesis <math id="A6.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> there is no corruption, so
<math id="A6.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i,j}\sim P_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i,j}\sim P_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A6.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math>; under the alternative <math id="A6.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, each
<math id="A6.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> follows the above <math id="A6.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\rho)P_{0}+\rho Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\rho)P_{0}+\rho Q</annotation></semantics></math> mixture. Thus, the
complicated adversarial pattern of corruptions in the original matrix model is,
after symmetrization, equivalent to an i.i.d. product model over entries.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
